:00:10-07:00","id":1479742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479737#post1479737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From Dusk till Dawn always comes to mind, and Near Dark is pretty quintessentially Gangrel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much,also American Vampire by Scott Snyder","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T14:10:11-07:00","id":1479743,"title":"","content":"Got to love a treatment that regards City Gangrel as authentic and valid members of the clan. Looking forward to digging into this further later tonight.<br /> <br /> Thank you for the bundle and the Mekhet updates, as well. This has been a big labor of love, and you deserve to know that it's seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T14:45:23-07:00","id":1479746,"title":"","content":"It is finally here! I have only skimmed it so far, but this is probably my favorite. But then again, the Gangrel are my favorite, so that probably would have been the case anyway. Also, the art for the bloodlines is absolutely killer! I especially love the Oberloch and Wicker illustrations.<br /> <br /> Plus, I can cross illustrating Count Fucking Dracula off my bucket list now. That was the absolutely the coolest part of working on this book for me. Love that guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T15:35:04-07:00","id":1479754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479739#post1479739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my God.<br /> You put the Pillar Men in here.<br /> You magnificent bastard.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can believe it, the parallel was a lot closer in the author's first draft. I loved the reference, but I had to file off a loooot of the edges, lol.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T17:53:15-07:00","id":1479766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479739#post1479739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my God.<br /> You put the Pillar Men in here.<br /> You magnificent bastard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where, where?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T18:20:42-07:00","id":1479767,"title":"","content":"I'm still reading though this, but as I expected based on the rest in the series it's a great book so far. The one thing that has stuck out to me so far as confusing, though, is that the Yarilo dropped Resilience in favor of Celerity. It seems like a strange choice all things considered. Regardless, it might be my favorite bloodline in the book. It's so hard to choose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T19:22:01-07:00","id":1479771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479767#post1479767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still reading though this, but as I expected based on the rest in the series it's a great book so far. The one thing that has stuck out to me so far as confusing, though, is that the Yarilo dropped Resilience in favor of Celerity. It seems like a strange choice all things considered. Regardless, it might be my favorite bloodline in the book. It's so hard to choose.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, funny enough, the Yarilo did in fact go through a few Discipline combo iterations. We always felt they had to keep Animalism, Dominate, and Protean, for obvious reasons, but the last one we went back and forth on. Originally, they had Obfuscate, but it didn't really fit with their themes, ultimately. Plants aren't really stealthy (or, most plants aren't). I also felt they should have a physical power. Resilience felt less appropriate mostly due to their weakness: they shouldn't be good at absorbing fire damage if that's an aspect of their bane. Vigor was a possibility, but it still didn't really put me in mind of plant life. Ultimately, we went with Celerity because it implies a kind of delicacy in the bloodline: they're fast, but they're fragile, yet they know their forest so well that they can practically teleport around their domains, picking off their prey from the vines.<br /> <br /> And of course, you're more than free to adjust as you see fit for your chronicle! That's just how we came down on things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T20:17:00-07:00","id":1479775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479766#post1479766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Where, where?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Narya, a race of ancient vampire-like god-kings with powerful biokinetic and inanimate transmutation abilities who nearly came to rule the world, but were cursed with sterility - they reproduce like mortals, but any child of theirs is apparently a normal human, though a plot hook is a descendant of one starts to metamorphosize into a full one.<br /> <br /> They even have torpor in statue armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T07:01:40-07:00","id":1479804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book#post1479721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of <b>Strange Shades</b>, we\u2019ve added a bunch of content to that supplement. It no longer relies on <b>Geist </b>for the Shadow Cult system, and we\u2019ve added a whole new Horror! The other clan books have also had some tweaks and new art added.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like I must be missing something here. When I redownloaded it on STV it still says to use the Geist system unless otherwise stated and I don't see a new Horror. Am I supposed to download the one marked (Old) instead for some reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T10:13:22-07:00","id":1479817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479804#post1479804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I must be missing something here. When I redownloaded it on STV it still says to use the Geist system unless otherwise stated and I don't see a new Horror. Am I supposed to download the one marked (Old) instead for some reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re not missing anything, something\u2019s just gone wrong! I\u2019m not sure what, however, because the preview file is showing the correct version. I <i>suspect</i> it\u2019s a file name issue, so I\u2019ll reupload it when I\u2019m at my computer in a little bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T10:44:35-07:00","id":1479821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479804#post1479804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I must be missing something here. When I redownloaded it on STV it still says to use the Geist system unless otherwise stated and I don't see a new Horror. Am I supposed to download the one marked (Old) instead for some reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, it's fixed! I think what happened was, I used the same file name for the new upload as for the old version, and that confused the system. Now it's labeled v2.0, and that's the one with all the updates.<br /> <br /> On a different note, here's our first excerpt: the <b>Oberlochs</b>! An old favourite from <b>Bloodlines: The Whichever One of Those Books They're From I'm Not Looking It Up Right Now.</b><br /> <br /> I don't have much to say about this bloodline, other than I've always really liked the Oberlochs (I apparently have a thing for aging vampires). That said, I've never liked aging vampires where the bane/weakness is that you become infirm. That always struck me as both unfun and not really something that's going to come up in most chronicles. It seemed to me that the crux of the Oberlochs is that they're utterly alienated from the rest of the All Night Society. It also seemed like joining the bloodline was kind of a hard sell, so now part of their weakness is that the Embrace confers it like a disease (there are, of course, social reasons one might want to be an Oberloch, but sometimes you want the system to reflect that). Still, apart from some mechanical quality of life updates, these aren't too different from the original version, though I feel like the backstory is a little more open to interpretation and, thus, more story opportunities:<br /> <br /> <b>Oberlochs: The ones who want you gone</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Get out or get dead. All the same to me.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The city is a straightjacket. To live in a modern metropolis, Kindred leash themselves with human mores in the hope that they might keep the prey ignorant to the monsters lurking in the dark. Maybe that means better eating, but anyone who sacrifices liberty for gratification is a fool, a dog who\u2019ll sniff any master\u2019s throne for a big enough bone. The Oberlochs know better. Living off the grid has taught them many harsh lessons, but the one that took root was the simplest: Freedom trumps safety. <i>Safety </i>is an illusion for bloated ticks who think hiding in concrete slabs is living.<br /> <br /> The Kin are the most isolated bloodline in the All Night Society. Called Rats among the Kindred (at least Kindred who\u2019ve survived an encounter), they make their havens in the hamlets and homesteads that still riddle Appalachia, whether mountain hideaways or just towns that never got around to incorporating. They nest in places the long arc of progress didn\u2019t give a shit about, bringing kine to heel with the Blood and the boot. They\u2019re moonshiners with secret recipes for bathtub gin and biker crank. They\u2019re sallow-eyed villagers who turn hitchhikers into statistics. They\u2019re mutant cannibals on the edge of town who worship made-up death gods just for the thrill of it. No two broods are alike, but they all follow the same code: outsiders stay out. This is the highest law of the grandparents, a gerontocracy composed of the bloodline\u2019s mustiest elders, and they\u2019ll enforce it with an authoritarian zeal the Invictus would blush at.<br /> <br /> That grandparent terminology isn\u2019t just metaphor, either. Rather than the eternal summer of other Kindred, the Oberlochs suffer a ceaseless winter, aging into husks as they surpass mortal lifespans. This even carries over into other forms, though some find petty pleasures in taking on the shape of skeletal wolves and bats to scare off trespassers. All who bear Oberloch Vitae share this burden, and so the bloodline seeks out ever fresher flesh to fasten to its decrepit corpse.<br /> <br /> The reasons for this curse are disputed. Back in the 1800s, the mortal Oberloch family fed on death long before they became vampires. Their mining concern was the most profitable in Pennsylvania, and its coffers were slick with its workers\u2019 blood. Among their many victims were the mortal relatives of a Gangrel wanderer called Bartholomew Ahern, who returned to his native soil only to find most of his kin dead or maimed in the mines. Without much of a grip on Humanity in the first place, the loss fueled a lust for vengeance that overtook his reason, and he bound every worker to his Vitae in order to unleash them on the family\u2019s manor house. Fire consumed most of Millionaire\u2019s Row that night, and the Oberloch estate was the blazing epicenter.<br /> <br /> Only one family member survived: Alice, the mother. Ahern was impressed as she climbed from the wreckage, gifting her with the Embrace for her desperation, and this is the lie Alice still tells her grandchilder to this very night.<br /> <br /> Whatever the true catalyst for her Damnation, Alice fled into the wild. Ashamed of what she\u2019d become, and terrified of being caught by her family\u2019s former victims, she wandered Appalachia for many years, scraping by on the blood of beasts and unfortunate travelers. When her hair began to gray and her skin to wrinkle, she didn\u2019t realize anything was wrong, taking it as a given that the punishment for her family\u2019s sins was to be eternal suffering. However, as the years grew longer, she became lonely, missing the pleasures of her daylight life. In Harmony, Pennsylvania, a backwater even among backwaters, Alice took back what was taken from her. Her coal baron husband taught her everything she needed to know about ruling over peasants, and years of life on the lam had ground out whatever compassion she had left.<br /> <br /> Tonight, Old Alice still casts a shadow over her bloodline, <i>prima inter pares </i>of the grandparents. Under her watchful, desiccated eyes, the Oberlochs expand far and wide across the Midwest, testing prospects for physical strength, low cunning, and an inclination to go along to get along.<br /> <br /> The Oberlochs believe in freedom, sure, but they\u2019re not anarchists. Liberty has to have structure, and the bloodline\u2019s leaders know the kind of bedlam that would befall their domains if they let their childer run wild. They <i>are </i>Savages, after all. Which isn\u2019t to say there\u2019s no room for upward mobility, but you also have to take what you can get. If someone else wants it, you\u2019d better be ready to stake them for the sun, Kin or otherwise. If not, it was never yours to begin with.<br /> <br /> Some Kindred worry the Kin are siring an army, hidden from the Masquerade\u2019s scrutiny in their rural strongholds. Rumors make the rounds that the Rats are abandoning their nests, making their way into domains they would\u2019ve once avoided. Rural America only continues to shrink, and forced from their domains, the time may be coming for the Oberlochs to fight back.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Kin (among themselves), Rats (derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Putrefying Curse):</b> The Oberlochs age. Due to this eternal half-life, Kin have difficulty connecting to true immortals, taking [REDACTED]. In addition, when Kin Embrace, their childer join their bloodline automatically.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, <i>Dominate</i>, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 04-30-2022, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T18:09:21-07:00","id":1479849,"title":"","content":"Their hypocrisy bleeds outward as youthless immortality. Nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T19:22:54-07:00","id":1479854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479849#post1479849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their hypocrisy bleeds outward as youthless immortality. Nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great way of putting it. The Oberlochs have long been a bloodline I'll throw in chronicles just as a background element, and it's a lot of fun to do a little <i>Texas Chain Saw Massacre\u2013</i>style horror in the Chronicles of Darkness.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T04:43:40-07:00","id":1479888,"title":"","content":"The Colossi are definitely my favorite thing in this book, and I am also very excited to see the Society of the Accord back!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T11:35:14-07:00","id":1479905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479888#post1479888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Colossi are definitely my favorite thing in this book, and I am also very excited to see the Society of the Accord back!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really happy with how the Accord turned out, and I love the way the author updated their powers into a new form rather than just doing off-brand Coils again.<br /> <br /> Anyway, a happy Sunday to you all! Time for another excerpt, this time for another First Edition bloodline: The <b>Childer of the Morrigan</b>, from <b>Circle of the Crone</b>.<br /> <br /> This bloodline was on my list fairly early on. They're much beloved in the fandom, and, like the Oberlochs, they're another one that didn't need a lot of overhauling (unlike, say, the Dead Wolves and Mystikoi, who needed a bit more work). The big change here is a simplification of the bloodline's bane and an upgrade to its relationship to Cruac.<br /> <br /> The original bane, like many 1E weaknesses, was long and complicated, and it relied on the late and not lamented Derangement system. So, we took the basic concept and condensed it: Now, if they back down from a challenge/conflict, they suffer a penalty to frenzy, and the more challenges they back down from in a night, the worse it gets.<br /> <br /> In terms of Cruac, in 1E, they got a free rite at Blood Potency 3 (more or less). Not very exciting, and the original book treats this stystem as optional. We figured, let's go with something fancier. Now, the Morrigans are chaos witches: any Cruac spell they know of three dots or lower, they can choose to cast as an instant action, but if they fail, they cause a side effect, inflicting them and anyone else around them with temporary banes.<br /> <br /> We also tweaked the backstory a bit, partially because the Circle of the Crone's own backstory is a bit different in 2E. And, as usual, we wanted to make things a little more multiple-choice in terms of where they really come from and what they really are.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, I'll be back with another 1E bloodlne: The Dead Wolves.<br /> <br /> Here are the Morrigans!<br /> <br /> <b>Childer of the Morrigan: The ones who never stop fighting you</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;My goddess doesn't want your apologies \u2014 just your blood.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Something vicious this way comes. Its left-hand holds a bleeding ax, blade chipped and well-loved; its right holds your best friend\u2019s head. You run, and its laugh pursues you, the sound of carrion crows celebrating a fresh meal.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone is a young covenant, not even two centuries past its gory birth. Founded from a place of oppression and persecution, the Mother\u2019s Army\u2019s formation was \u2014 by necessity \u2014 a violent one, and the Childer of the Morrigan were at the vanguard of that violence. They still are. Acting as unforgiving guardians for their fellow Acolytes, the Stormcrows defend their covens and cults against those who would see them broken. In domains where they\u2019re active, they hunt known enemies of the Crone and slay them for sport, their remains put on garish display so the rest of the All Night Society gets the message: To attack the Dark Mother is to invoke the wrath of the Morrigans, and like the goddess they\u2019re named for, their fury is endless.<br /> <br /> The unifying philosophy of the Mother\u2019s Army (if the notoriously fractious covenant can be said to have one), is evolution and creation through tribulation \u2014 suffer, endure, and grow stronger. Many Acolytes view conflict as a chance for growth, but while some are content to wait for it to come to them, others like to strike the sparks of their own trials by fire. Stormcrows exemplify the latter philosophy, preferring to make their own trouble.<br /> <br /> While the stereotypical image of a Morrigan is that of a hard-bitten warrior spattered with gore, the bloodline understands modern nights have spawned a wide variety of conflicts that require diverse \u2014 and not always immediately violent \u2014 solutions. Broken teeth and shattered glass are all well and good, but you can\u2019t always punch your problems away. It\u2019s for this reason that hacktivists, lobbyists, academic firebrands, and more can find a home with the Stormcrows, united by their desire for direct action.<br /> Others in the Circle argue over dogma; the Morrigans see a threat and snuff it out. While their Gangrel heritage does predispose them to rather reckless solutions, a Stormcrow is just as likely to destroy an enemy with a strategically leaked email as with a sledgehammer to the skull.<br /> <br /> While this decisiveness and ferocity earns the Morrigan healthy measures of respect and fear, these traits cause as many problems as they solve. Diplomacy goes out the window once a Stormcrow hurls a Molotov cocktail through it, and their \u201cshoot first, ask questions while shooting\u201d attitude doesn\u2019t win them many friends outside the Circle, or even within it. Childer of the Morrigan may be the Acolytes\u2019 most effective enforcers, but their actions are often the flashpoint that escalates a minor conflict into holy war. Not that the Stormcrows mind, of course \u2014 they\u2019re closest to their goddess with viscera in their hair and screams in their ears.<br /> <br /> This reckless attitude extends to the Morrigans\u2019 use of Cr\u00faac. Something in the Stormcrows\u2019 blood allows them to enact rituals in a tiny fraction of the time they should need, reducing what would normally be an hour of frantic dancing and chanting to a single muttered prayer and a spray of Vitae. The Childer of the Morrigan claim this ability proves they\u2019re favored by the Crone as her chosen warriors, but other Acolytes say it\u2019s another reason to give the bloodline a wide berth. When these rushed rituals work, they\u2019re just as effective as if they had been done traditionally, but when they don\u2019t, the results are hazardous to not only the Morrigan enacting them, but to anyone unlucky enough to be nearby.<br /> <br /> Despite their harsh methods (or maybe because of them), the Childer of the Morrigan enjoy a high status in their covenant due to their willingness to fling themselves into danger on behalf of the Dark Mother. Problems arise in how they\u2019re perceived by outsiders. Rightly or wrongly, many Kindred view Stormcrows as zealots first and very little second, which can make forming ties outside of the Mother\u2019s Army difficult. Their dedication to being the most brutal monsters in a covenant that glorifies monstrousness makes it hard to relate to mortals as well, and many Morrigans find their Humanity frays badly before long.<br /> <br /> Some Childer counter this by immersing themselves in some facet of the living world: The steely-eyed night-shift volunteer at the women\u2019s shelter who drains the blood of abusers; the ruthless campaign staffer who employs backroom intimidation and boardroom sorcery to advance her cause; the gray-hat hacker, teeth gleaming in the light of her monitor, tower anointed with the arterial spray of the last troll she hunted down. All are Childer of the Morrigan, roosting in places where they can channel their need to fight for a cause.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Stormcrows, Crows, Morrigans<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Warmonger\u2019s Curse):</b> Childer of the Morrigan crave battle. Doesn\u2019t matter if it\u2019s a back-alley brawl with broken bottles or a boardroom negotiation with expensive pens. What matters is the fight, and Stormcrows have difficulty walking away from one. Whenever a Morrigan backs down from a challenge, deescalates a problem, or otherwise resolves an important issue through means other than direct conflict, she suffers a cumulative \u20131 on frenzy resistance for the rest of the night. A Stormcrow\u2019s Beast demands bloody victory and will howl with greater and greater intensity until it gets what it desires.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: Banshee Cr\u00faac</b><br /> <br /> Besides their zealous love of battle, the Childer of the Morrigan have an instinctual affinity for Cr\u00faac, able to call up power in moments where most Witches need hours. Much like the Stormcrows themselves, this power is difficult to control, and it\u2019s prone to lashing out at anyone around it. It was dubbed \u201cBanshee\u201d Cr\u00faac by other Acolytes because of the misfortune it causes to those nearby, and because if you\u2019re close enough to hear a Stormcrow invoke it, it\u2019s already too late.<br /> <br /> Banshee Cr\u00faac uses the following system:<ul><li>A Childer of the Morrigan can spend a Willpower when attempting to cast any rite with a dot rating of three or less. If she does, the action becomes instant rather than extended, and she only needs to achieve a number of successes equal to the ritual\u2019s dot rating to cast it. Contested rituals are resisted as normal. The Potency of these rites is always considered to be one, and no more.</li> <li>If a Morrigan fails to cast a ritual using this method, it counts as a dramatic failure. In addition to the normal consequences of dramatically failing Cr\u00faac, the caster and those around her will suffer a magical backlash from the fumbled power. For each dot of the failed ritual, [REDACTED].</li> <li>Targets of rituals cast this way must be within line of sight, even if the ritual normally does not require this proximity.</li> <li>Exceptional successes on rituals cast this way always result in the Ecstatic Condition.</li> </ul><br /> In addition, all Childer of the Morrigan with a dot of Cr\u00faac receive an additional animal form upon learning Beast\u2019s Skin, that of a crow or a raven. This form does not count toward the number of shapes a Stormcrow can have at the ready and is always available to her. The exact type of corvid varies depending on what species an individual Morrigan considers to be typical to her part of the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T21:52:18-07:00","id":1479931,"title":"","content":"I got this book and am still reading through it with unmatched excitement. I skipped ahead to read the Narya when I realised that they were basically the Pillar Men and caught a glimpse of the 'preview'.<br /> &quot;Glory reigns above, death rules below.&quot;<br /> <br /> I've been wondering what you would do after this series of Clan focused books, Yossarian, and now I'm even more hyped. How much are you willing to talk about this next plan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T22:52:36-07:00","id":1479933,"title":"","content":"Banshee Cruac is a thing to envy.<br /> <br /> Really, the whole sourcebook has the Nossies and the Gangrel fighting for second favorite now.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, fucking love the entire section Protean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-02-2022, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T11:43:19-07:00","id":1479964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479931#post1479931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got this book and am still reading through it with unmatched excitement. I skipped ahead to read the Narya when I realised that they were basically the Pillar Men and caught a glimpse of the 'preview'.<br /> &quot;Glory reigns above, death rules below.&quot;<br /> <br /> I've been wondering what you would do after this series of Clan focused books, Yossarian, and now I'm even more hyped. How much are you willing to talk about this next plan?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I can say that the next thing you'll probably see from us in regards to <b>Requiem </b>is (finally) the long-promised <b>Bloodlines: The Ageless</b>, which is basically in redlines ATM. That's an update of all the bloodlines from <b>Ancient Bloodlines </b>that we haven't covered yet.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;Glory reigns...&quot;, I'm keeping a tight lid on that for now, because I'm still working out some details, but that's going to be a <i>big one</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479933#post1479933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banshee Cruac is a thing to envy.<br /> <br /> Really, the whole sourcebook has the Nossies and the Gangrel fighting for second favorite now.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, fucking love the entire section Protean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Banshee Cruac is one of my favourite things in the book. The author had the idea of letting them do fast-casting with consequences, and had the idea of those consequences being sort of like Wild Magic from D&amp;D. I think it came together really well.<br /> <br /> And yeah, that Protean section was very important to me to get in. It's a really different Discipline from the other 9, and it felt worthwhile to have an in depth discussion of how it changes the way you play the game. Especially considering how different it is from the 1E version.<br /> <br /> Anyway, today, let's look at the <b>Dead Wolves</b>!<br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, this bloodline is the only ones that's not from a <b>Vampire</b>-branded book. Though <b>Shadows of Mexico </b>kind of <i>is </i>a <b>Vampire </b>book with the serial numbers filed off...except it <i>has </i>a <b>Vampire </b>serial number so, uh...<br /> <br /> I digress. It's another bloodline that gets a lot of love in the fandom. Gangrel-as-werewolves is a very natural theme, and I think part of the reason the Dead Wolves are so well-liked is that they have an interesting cultural context, both the Latine context and the Uratha one.<br /> <br /> Apart from a few tweaks to the backstory, the big change was Sublunario. The old version is so unlike other Disciplines that I'm not sure why it wasn't a Merit to begin with. It actually has some fun powers, it just has a <i>really </i>weird format. So, we figured the natural thing to do was indeed to make it a Merit, adding in some. Auspex also felt like the natural choice of a fourth Discipline: the Gangrel Disciplines are pretty werewolfy already, and Auspex provides the spooky touch the Dead Wolves have going.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I <i>believe </i>we came up with &quot;Namus-Ur&quot;. It means...Dead Wolf (as opposed to Death Wolf).<br /> <br /> So, here are the Lobos de Sangre, back to howl at the moon once more. Tomorrow, let's finish off the 1E bloodlines with the Mystikoi.<br /> <br /> <b>Dead Wolves: The ones who hunt you by moonlight</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cThese? All the better to eat you with, my dear.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> A predator prowls the night, but it\u2019s not alone. Swift-running shadows lope beside it, and ghostly howls echo around it. It has allies of flesh and spirit, and they\u2019re on the hunt. You\u2019d best hope you\u2019re not the quarry.<br /> <br /> Vampires are not the only hunters stalking human prey. For as long as Kindred have feasted on blood, werewolves have ripped flesh from bone in the name of their sacred hunts. However, despite sharing the night for millennia, the two monsters have little in common besides their predatory nature. Kindred are selfish, immortal parasites, obsessed with building their own temporal power at the cost of everyone around them. Conversely, Uratha have a sacred duty to guard the divide between flesh and spirit, and anything that interferes in that is an obstacle to be torn asunder. Usually, they ignore each other, but when Kindred and werewolves do cross paths, things have a tendency to end poorly, as misunderstanding and ignorance lead to savage violence that can spark decades-long conflicts. It\u2019s this status quo that makes the existence of the Dead Wolves unique \u2014 and very strange.<br /> <br /> Originating primarily in Mexico, the Lobos de Sangre exist as a tenuous link between werewolf and vampire cultures. While they\u2019re certainly Kindred, the Dead Wolves have a spiritual awareness other vampires lack, paired with an instinctual understanding of werewolf society that lets them interact with the Uratha and (usually) walk away whole. In fact, in regions where they\u2019re active, it\u2019s not that unusual for <i>Namus-Ur </i>\u2014 as the werewolves call them \u2014 to be made part of a pack. Uratha packs are often called upon to hunt humans in order to serve the balance between the worlds, and nothing is better adapted for that purpose than a vampire. In return for their expertise, Lobos who join packs get to experience true camaraderie and trust, which are rarer than diamonds in the All Night Society. These \u201cadopted\u201d Dead Wolves can also serve as diplomats and ambassadors, helping to settle conflict between Licks and wolves before violence breaks out.<br /> <br /> However, some Lobos de Sangre take their Requiems in a completely different direction, using their insight into the ways of the Uratha to become deadly hunters of their so-called \u201cliving cousins.\u201d These mercenaries sell their services to princes and covenant heads, acting as consultants and exterminators for a high price. Wielding silver weaponry and an understanding of the Uratha mindset, such Dead Wolves are adept at isolating pack members and picking them off one by one. Their ability to interact with the Shadow gives them another advantage, as Uratha often have many enemies among the spirit world who are eager to assist in their elimination.<br /> <br /> What truly sets the Dead Wolves apart from their Kindred isn\u2019t their relationship to werewolves, but rather that awareness of the Shadow. For the normally spiritually blind vampires, this opens up a whole new dimension of opportunity and danger, and it\u2019s one of the reasons this scattered and independent bloodline has survived \u2014 and even thrived \u2014 for as long as it has. Of course, becoming aware of spirits also means the spirits are aware of them, and not all of them are keen on making deals with dead things.<br /> <br /> The Dead Wolves hold a singular place in Mexico\u2019s supernatural ecology. Embraced as vampires but with a connection to a wondrous and horrifying world that other Kindred are barely aware of, the Lobos de Sangre rarely feel completely at home in the All Night Society. As <i>Namus-Ur</i>, they\u2019re capable of running with the Uratha, but they\u2019re never thought of as equals to their moon-born comrades, and they\u2019re perpetually on the bottom of any pack they manage to join.<br /> <br /> However, this eternal\u2013outsider status means that neither Kindred nor Uratha know what the Dead Wolves are truly capable of. Vampires who persecute them turn up torpid with missing limbs, and werewolves who decide the bloodline is prey are found riddled with silver buckshot. Ultimately, <i>Namus-Ur </i>walk their own path, and both sides of their bloody, brutal family have learned to leave them to it.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Lobos de Sangre, Lobos, <i>Namus-Ur (</i>among werewolves)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Moonstruck Curse): </b>Dead Wolves don\u2019t (necessarily) worship Mother Luna like their Forsaken cousins, but beholding the moon in all its glory does stir the Beast. When Lobos view the full moon for the first time in a night [REDACTED]. Furthermore, silver, blessed metal of the Moon, has a maddening effect on Dead Wolves. The first time in any scene a <i>Namus-Ur </i>takes damage from a weapon coated with silver, she must resist fear frenzy with a \u20133 modifier.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, <i>Auspex</i>, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>Sublunario (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Prerequisite: </b>Dead Wolf<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>A combination of mystical insight and instinctive skills, Sublunario grants several distinct benefits to any Namus-Ur who listens to the howling in her blood.<br /> <br /> <b>Wolf\u2019s Blood (\u2022):</b> Dead Wolves have a subconscious understanding of how to behave around werewolves and their kin. Your character gains a +1 to Animal Ken, Empathy, and Socialize rolls that involve Uratha, Wolf-Blooded, or wolves. She also counts as Wolf-Blooded for all intents and purposes (see <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b>, p. 296).<br /> <br /> <b>Forgotten Rapport (\u2022\u2022):</b> Dead Wolves who attain this level receive a sliver of the connection their Uratha cousins enjoy to spirits. Your character gains a free Occult Specialty in Spirits and can communicate in the First Tongue.<br /> <br /> <b>Taste of Home (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Blood calls to blood, living or dead. Your character knows instantly if blood she smells or tastes belongs to Uratha or Wolf-Blooded. Furthermore, she adds her Sublunario dots to Taste of Blood rolls to gain details from the blood of werewolves and their kin.<br /> <br /> <b>Moon\u2019s Blessing (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Namus-Ur might not be Luna\u2019s children, but perhaps they\u2019re close enough that she takes pity on them. When your character gains this Merit, choose New Moon, Crescent Moon, Half Moon, Gibbous Moon, or Full Moon: She gains the 9-again benefit on the two Insight Skills associated with this chosen moon phase (see below). During nights where her chosen moon is in the sky, she exceptionally succeeds on her Insight Skills with three successes instead of five.<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 05-02-2022, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T18:31:35-07:00","id":1479995,"title":"","content":"I have to say, this book is really excellent. I like the fact that there's support to use Protean as Vicissitude, but at the same time, you've avoided making any one bloodline into the &quot;Tzimisce update.&quot; You and the whole team should be proud of what you'd made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27139-chevaliermalfet","name":"ChevalierMalFet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T18:54:09-07:00","id":1479998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChevalierMalFet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479995#post1479995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, this book is really excellent. I like the fact that there's support to use Protean as Vicissitude, but at the same time, you've avoided making any one bloodline into the &quot;Tzimisce update.&quot; You and the whole team should be proud of what you'd made.</div> </div> </div> </div>This book is such a stealth &quot;Requiem Vicissitude&quot; update it's not even funny.<br /> <br /> And thank you!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-03T13:07:45-07:00","id":1480053,"title":"","content":"Let's talk Mystikoi.<br /> <br /> The Illuminated have changed a lot from their 1E version. Previously, they used their bloodline Discipline to channel the Beast in order to become closer to the Divine Unity. While this is a cool concept on paper, we had a lot of difficulty with the mechanics of their power, which is a good example of a design philosophy I've tried to move away from with these updates: the bloodline Discipline makes the bloodline bane pointless. This was a pretty clear example. Their 1E weakness was that they couldn't spend Willpower to add dice to frenzy or to spend Willpower to resist any power that would cause them to fall to frenzy. Not a bad bane, in the abstract, but then the first dot of Spiritus Sancti lets you spend a Vitae to ride the wave, which the bloodline specifically <i>can </i>spend Willpower on.<br /> <br /> And while the idea of allowing the Beast closer to the surface to assume godliness was a neat idea, Spiritus Sancti mostly felt redundant with the Coil of the Wyrm, apart from the spiritual aspects, which we didn't feel were very well integrated.<br /> <br /> So, the author did some reworking. While still scholars and monks, the Mystikoi are also now a hunting lodge for ephemeral beings. By devouring these creatures, they believe they can attain apotheosis. Spiritus Sancti is now a way to make yourself (and eventually, the world around you) more accommodating to your divine becoming. The Beast/frenzy aspects are gone, but you could easily make a Dragon Mystikoi with Wyrm powers and regain all those elements.<br /> <br /> We also felt this bloodline was a fun contrast to the Dead Wolves: The Mystikoi are far more potent when it comes to spirits, but unlike the Dead Wolves, they have no <i>idea </i>what they're doing, at least in werewolf terms.<br /> <br /> With all that said, here are the Mystikoi! Tomorrow, I'll be back with one of the new bloodlines.<br /> <br /> <b>Mystikoi: The ones who surpass you</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Blood? A distraction. Our true thirst is for God.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Despite being immortal parasites who feed on the living, Kindred are rather earthly, ignorant of the many different layers of reality that surround them. Closed off to the harmonies of spiritual choirs, they are blind to the thorns lurking just off the path. Vampires are drawn to spinning schemes that might take centuries to mature but will only ever affect a few square miles of steel and glass. This is for the best. When Kindred <i>do </i>catch a glimpse of the wider world, they naturally want to know more: to reach out and touch it, to explore this new layer of their existence \u2014 and to exploit it.<br /> <br /> One part hunting lodge, one part Christian cult, the Mystikoi believe they\u2019ve found the secret to (eventual) divinity. To become closer to the sacred Unity, the origin of all things, one must take pieces of it into oneself. The more Divine energy one consumes, the closer one comes to being part of the Unity. They accomplish this by eating spirits. The Illuminated (so-called because they alone see the light of the Divine) have the ability not only to perceive beings in Twilight, but to interact with them in all manner of ways, from simple conversation to tearing open their strange forms and feasting on the Essence within. Rather than projecting their minds outward with prayer or meditation, however, the Mystikoi rip bloody holes in reality, using the power of Spiritus Sancti to assault beings they shouldn\u2019t even be aware of.<br /> <br /> The Mystikoi\u2019s focus on spirits \u2014 creatures the vast majority of Kindred don\u2019t even realize exist \u2014 has caused the Lancea et Sanctum to label them dangerous Heretics, and the covenant would have hunted the bloodline to extinction if it weren\u2019t for the intervention of the Ordo Dracul. The Dragons have protected and shepherded the Illuminated for centuries, using them as hunting hounds and guard dogs for Wyrm\u2019s Nests. The entities the bloodline covets are drawn to Nests and often interfere with the work of Defiant who seek to study them. The Mystikoi are some of the only Kindred who can deal with angry spirits directly, and the Order is willing to indulge them with their strange beliefs if it means heightened security for their most important assets. There\u2019s also the <i>slight </i>chance the Illuminated are on to something, and if that\u2019s the case, the Dragons want to be on hand to record <i>exactly </i>what a steady diet of Essence does to a vampire.<br /> <br /> Hunting is as central to the Mystikoi as their divine philosophy, and a great deal of any Illuminated\u2019s time is dedicated to tracking and studying potential prey. Largely ignorant of the Shadow and its laws, Mystikoi can only hunt those spirits who manage to exist in the between-state of Twilight. Thus, they can\u2019t afford to be picky: Heretics will attack anything they can sink their fangs into in their quest for divinity, and their blurry understanding of what spirits are means that ghosts and other, stranger entities often end up on the menu.<br /> <br /> Fortunately for the rest of the All Night Society, the Mystikoi are an obscure bloodline with few members. What they lack in numbers, however, they make up for in zeal. Unlike most Kindred, the Mystikoi aren\u2019t spiritually blind, or helplessly bound by the dogma of either Longinus or the Crone. They\u2019ve seen the truth behind the veil, and it\u2019s made them hungry for more.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Illuminated, Mystikos (singular), Heretics<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Consubstantiation Curse): </b>Pursuing the divine isn\u2019t just dogma to the Mystikoi: It\u2019s bound to their blood. Each night, Mystikoi can only consume Vitae [REDACTED]. Their ability to feed from Kindred is not affected, but only as long as Blood Potency remains below six dots. The Essence-rich blood of werewolves is also exempt, but feeding on Uratha tends to bring about its own dangers.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience, <i>Spiritus Sancti</i><br /> <br /> <b>Spiritus Sancti</b><br /> <br /> Literally translating to \u201cHoly Spirit,\u201d Spiritus Sancti is what allows Mystikoi to perceive, feed from, and manipulate their sacred prey.<br /> <br /> While much ritual and esoterica surround this Discipline, at its core, Spiritus Sancti is about teaching the Beast to hunt a new kind of food. As a consequence of this, an Illuminated in the grips of hunger frenzy will perceive spirits as a source of nourishment and is fully capable of using all levels of Spiritus Sancti to bring down his prey.<br /> <br /> <b>Cast Off the Scales \u2022</b><br /> <br /> The most basic level of Spiritus Sancti allows the Illuminated to track the Divine beings at play behind the scenes and feast upon their Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>None<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>None<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> <br /> The vampire can perceive beings in Twilight for the rest of the scene, even if these creatures have a supernatural power of concealment. Nothing can escape his divine sight so long as they remain in his presence. Furthermore, his Kindred Senses attune with his new prey, and he can detect the presence of nearby ephemera exactly as if he were attempting to detect the blood of living creatures.<br /> <br /> The vampire can use Disciplines on ephemeral beings as he would humans and animals if they can perceive him, but effects that require victims to smell his Vitae do not work unless he uses Step Upon the Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-03T17:11:17-07:00","id":1480061,"title":"","content":"Ooh. Wonder if they can diablerize spirits for Influence/Numen, claim Loci to project their Predatory Aura anywhere the Locus' Resonance reaches, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-03T18:52:46-07:00","id":1480071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480061#post1480061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh. Wonder if they can diablerize spirits for Influence/Numen, claim Loci to project their Predatory Aura anywhere the Locus' Resonance reaches, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With something like the apocryphal Coil of the Locust, they might very much try. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T14:10:14-07:00","id":1480129,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's get into some of the new blood.<br /> <br /> The <b>Verlice </b>are a bloodline of wanderers, Gangrel who develop a sympathetic-magic-like connection to vehicles and serve the All Night Society as messengers and couriers (when they deign to take such roles). Their &quot;Rides&quot; are vehicles imbued with...sentience, let's say, and these vehicles can help their masters get out of scrapes on their own initiative.<br /> <br /> This bloodline didn't change much from first draft to development, apart from some mechanical tweaks here and there. I especially like how they take the sort of subtheme of &quot;freedom&quot; that runs through the book and makes it far more of an imperative. The Needles are forced to wander by their very blood, and though some make their Requiems in cities, most take to the open road. Another thing I like about this bloodline is that it ties into the idea of coyotes, vampires who can help Kindred move between cities despite the dangers of the sun (hence their other nickname).<br /> <br /> Vehicles come up a couple of times in this book (cf., the Brides of Dracula), which was inadvertent, but it's something that really fits the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> So, here are the Verlice. Tomorrow, let's look at the Wickers, one of the stranger bloodlines in the book...and perhaps the most dangerous.<br /> <br /> <b>Verlice: The ones you can't catch</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You think those walls will protect you?&quot;<br /> <br /> The headlights blind you as your squint at them in your mirror. No one else should be on the road this late \u2014 not way out here \u2014 so it\u2019s just your luck you found the only midnight tailgater. You don\u2019t see any flashing colors, so it\u2019s not the cops.<br /> <br /> Just as suddenly as they appear, they\u2019re gone. What happened back there? Did they crash? You pull over and step out onto the old cracked pavement and look back, calling out. The only answer is the headlights, right behind your car again, and a dark blur rushing toward you. </i><br /> <br /> The world is littered with small towns, villages, and hamlets, lost in a concrete bramble tying all the little points of light together. These places are usually invisible to Kindred; they can\u2019t support even a single vampire long-term, and even if they could, they provide little support to build a Requiem.<br /> <br /> The Verlice see the bigger picture. A small town might not sustain a Lick forever, but it provides enough sustenance for a few nights \u2014 even a week. The Needles draw maps and plot routes, hopping from one quiet oasis to the next in search of a meal or a job, sometimes going years without encountering their Kindred. Plenty of places don\u2019t even appear on GPS, but a well-traveled Needle knows them all, collecting those tiny drops of blood overlooked by the rest of the All Night Society. The world is a much larger place than most vampires think, and a Verlice can traverse that void like a wolf.<br /> <br /> When Needles do choose to stay in town, they explore, digging into all the little cracks and worming their way through the secret pathways that lace the city together, but they\u2019re always alert for trouble, ready to set out on the road at a moment\u2019s notice. Either the trouble they cause or the call of their own blood eventually compels them to seek new journeys. They make a habit of begging forgiveness rather than asking permission, especially when it comes to the territory of others. A little poaching is easy to get away with if no one knows your face, let alone your name.<br /> <br /> Travel is a way of life for this bloodline, and members will offer their services as couriers and transports to other vampires for favors owed (if they ever return), or just for the materials they require to keep them moving. They take particular interest in local Gangrel, ever watchful for others they can free from the confines of a city\u2019s gilded cage. Needles look at cities and don\u2019t see the neighborhoods or buildings the way most other Kindred do. No, they see a circulatory system at work, moving lifeblood around to touch every person, place, and dead thing.<br /> <br /> To a Verlice on the road, their Ride is their home, hideout, and fortress. The stereotypical Needle owns a muscle car, an old warhorse that was hardy even before the vampire got hold of it, but many use trucks, vans, boats, or even small planes. Few use motorcycles, though, mainly because of the lack of shelter and storage space. Their whole existence comes with them wherever they go, and it\u2019s a rare Needle who gets by with so little that it fits in a saddlebag long-term. The bond a Verlice shares with her Ride runs deep, and most hold superstitious beliefs about treating them well. They\u2019re often overheard speaking to them as if they were pets, and rumors abound that these vehicles are intelligent to a limited extent, watching out for their owners and working to keep them safe. Stories of a Ride\u2019s engines growling around particular people, smelling faintly of old, rusted blood, or of silently turning to face someone when they weren\u2019t looking are just that \u2014 stories. Right?<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Needles, Coyotes, Trespassers (disrespectful)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Stagnant Curse): </b>The boredom of staying still is blood deep for the Needles, and it drives the Verlice to inhuman things in an attempt to feel connected. All Trespassers suffer from a withering of their Touchstones when they remain in the same place. Each night after the first that a Verlice sleeps in the same (Blood Potency) kilometer radius, her effective Humanity lowers by a dot for the purposes of attached Touchstones. Only resting in a new area for a full day can alleviate this bane, and she cannot rest in the same area for a full week.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b><i>Auspex</i>, Obfuscate, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: The Ride</b><br /> <br /> A Verlice can anoint a vehicle with a point of Vitae and spend a Willpower to designate it as her Ride, bonding with it the way a human might bond with a pet. The Ride responds to this relationship. Small coincidences make it seem like the car wants to help its Needle: The doors are never locked for its owner, its horn goes off or flash its lights if danger is nearby, it subtly nudges the steering wheel during a tense chase to avoid an obstacle, etc. If the Ride\u2019s aid could benefit one of the Needle\u2019s actions, once per chapter, the Storyteller can roll the vampire\u2019s Drive + Blood Potency in secret, applying successes as a bonus to a relevant action. In addition, reduce a Ride\u2019s Handling Modifier by half, rounding down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T18:43:53-07:00","id":1480138,"title":"","content":"I've given a quick description of the bloodlines in the book to a couple friends and the Verlice is always the one they immediately pick up on. It is, admittedly, one of the more out there bloodlines despite being relatively simple to understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T19:30:03-07:00","id":1480139,"title":"","content":"The Verlice don\u2019t have Animalism? That\u2019s unexpected; I somewhat expected them to have Devotions that treat vehicles as animals. (Or maybe I saw such in someone else\u2019s homebrew some time ago) I do wonder how Auspex and Obfuscate fit, though I can sorta see the outlines I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T19:41:48-07:00","id":1480142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480138#post1480138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've given a quick description of the bloodlines in the book to a couple friends and the Verlice is always the one they immediately pick up on. It is, admittedly, one of the more out there bloodlines despite being relatively simple to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a simple concept with a lot of depth, I'd say. &quot;Cars + Gangrel&quot; has obvious tropes that come to mind, but you can do a <i>lot </i>with those tropes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480139#post1480139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Verlice don\u2019t have Animalism? That\u2019s unexpected; I somewhat expected them to have Devotions that treat vehicles as animals. (Or maybe I saw such in someone else\u2019s homebrew some time ago) I do wonder how Auspex and Obfuscate fit, though I can sorta see the outlines I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of it is that, despite their wandering ways, they're very urban. They hunt in towns and cities and on highways, not so much the dark woods. Auspex lets them see further down the road, and Obfuscate allows them to keep a low profile when the heat inevitably comes down (there's a fun Merit involving Obfuscating your Ride, for instance). Despite being Gangrel, they're a bit sneaky, in their way, and those Disciplines fit well with that theme. We also felt that, while using Animalism on vehicles could be a fun avenue to explore, ultimately, it pigeonholed the concept a bit too much (we'd also done some stuff with Animalism as a form of power over machines with the Connected in <b>Strange Shades</b>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T20:42:15-07:00","id":1480145,"title":"","content":"wouldnt the eternal predator merit have worked better for the gangrel then the ventrue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T21:12:48-07:00","id":1480146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480142#post1480142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of it is that, despite their wandering ways, they're very urban. They hunt in towns and cities and on highways, not so much the dark woods. Auspex lets them see further down the road, and Obfuscate allows them to keep a low profile when the heat inevitably comes down (there's a fun Merit involving Obfuscating your Ride, for instance). Despite being Gangrel, they're a bit sneaky, in their way, and those Disciplines fit well with that theme. We also felt that, while using Animalism on vehicles could be a fun avenue to explore, ultimately, it pigeonholed the concept a bit too much (we'd also done some stuff with Animalism as a form of power over machines with the Connected in <b>Strange Shades</b>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, I see I see. And there was the Connected. Cool. (I\u2019ve been discovered as a not-yet-buyer! Time to break out memory-wiping Dominate\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-04T21:50:42-07:00","id":1480148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480146#post1480146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahh, I see I see. And there was the Connected. Cool. (I\u2019ve been discovered as a not-yet-buyer! Time to break out memory-wiping Dominate\u2026)</div> </div> </div> </div>@_@ BUY MY BOOK @_@<br /> <br /> (But actually, no worries. Do check it out when you get the chance!)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T18:00:15-07:00","id":1480226,"title":"","content":"Happy... post-Wednesday!<br /> <br /> So, the <b>Wickers </b>are one of six new bloodlines out of the ten in the book (eleven, technically, if you count the Bruja's cameo). As an aside, part of the reason we did so many bloodlines instead of our typical seven or eight is because the Gangrel didn't get a lot of love in <b>Spilled Blood</b>, and only four collectively show up in <b>Bloodlines: The Resurrected </b>and <b>Devoted</b>. So, we wanted to make up for a lack of Savage blood. You might've also noticed that this is the only one of our clan books where we didn't do full write-ups of the bloodlines from the original clan book, those being the Mabry and the Hounds of Acteon. To be honest, neither of those bloodlines set our world on fire conceptually, and neither of them had mechanics that were in desperate need of updating. Which isn't to say we won't do them at some point in the future, but the quick conversions in <b>Bloodlines: The Devoted </b>ought to do for now. And while I'm sure we could've had fun with them, we felt it was more important to add some new bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to the Wickers. The Wickers are sort of what happens when you ride <i>just </i>up to the boundary between Kindred and Strix and then vomit on it. The Flock are sort of antigens to the dooms brought on by the Owls, but this has cost them a great deal. They're sort of anti-prophets, if that makes any sense, using their collective, flock-like collective unconscious to stay one step ahead of the Striges. They don't have the easiest Requiems, but when you need them, they're the only thing that will do.<br /> <br /> Development-wise, the concept was pretty consistent throughout the process, though we played around a lot with their systems, and it took a while to find a good mechanic for their Murmur power. Their Council of Talons cult was also more prominent in the beginning, but I ultimately felt it was better to leave them more to the imagination. One thing that stands out about this bloodline is their Discipline spread. Normally, there's kind of an unwritten rule that bloodlines shouldn't get more than two clan-unique Disciplines, but the combo of Auspex, Nightmare, and Protean was too fun to pass up, and we felt their bane balanced the, for lack of a better term, power-gaminess. Plus, when you've got ten bloodlines, you start to want to break some rules so things don't feel monotonous.<br /> <br /> Speaking of their bane, this bloodline might have my favourite curse in the book, though it's certainly one you have to be careful with. Still, I like the idea of the Strix's self-proclaimed worst enemies also being vectors for them...<br /> <br /> Anyway, meet the Wickers, but don't get too close. Tomorrow, I think I'll do the Baetyl or the Yarilo, though if anyone has a preference, comment below.<br /> <br /> <b>Wickers: The ones who grip your fate</b><br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;Hear that \u2014 the silence? The birds have stopped singing. Run.&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cGo ask the Hawk.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnything but that\u2026\u201d Scout shudders, blood and soot still smeared across his haggard face. His packmates back away, leaving him groveling on his knees. Everyone else knows what\u2019s good for them and gets out.<br /> <br /> Lucifer takes a long, warm drink from his pint, mulling over the disaster facing his family. Fledgling or not, Scout fucked up. He curls his lip and repeats himself, voice like lead, \u201cGo ask the Hawk.\u201d<br /> <br /> Scout\u2019s really squirming now, every twitch an apology. But it\u2019s too late for sorries. \u201cMaggie went to the Hawk and came back babbling about monsters. Seared her own eyes out!\u201d Lucifer snorts, slamming the glass down on the table, frothy red liquid spraying across the tarnished wood. \u201cYou should\u2019ve thought of that before you fucked over your pack. Might\u2019ve started a war tonight. I don\u2019t see a way out of it. Neither do you, clearly.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease, anything else!\u201d<br /> <br /> The old vampire licks a fang and shakes his head, mentally washing his hands clean of his dumb-as-shit childe.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe only one who can help you now\u2019s the Wicker\u2026 and that\u2019s punishment enough.\u201d </i><br /> <br /> When you\u2019re backed into a corner and can\u2019t see a way out. When you\u2019ve made a mistake you wish you could take back\u2026 go ask the Hawks.<br /> <br /> The Wickers glean secrets never whispered, each pair of glowing eyes foreseeing a different permutation of a disastrous future. They seek meaning in the Requiem, but their path to succor is twisted and full of terror \u2014 for them and their prey. The desperate seek them out, looking for counsel, support, or just impossible solutions. And they <i>do </i>know things, but other Gangrel say they\u2019re too far gone. Perhaps they\u2019re so secretive because they\u2019re trying to create distance. Owl and Hawk, ancient enemies, tug on the same threads of fate, but there\u2019s only room for one monster in the skies, and the Flock will break into a thousand pieces before they\u2019ll allow themselves to be caught. Where the Striges bring vile omens, the Wickers dare to prevent those dooms.<br /> <br /> If a Gangrel\u2019s goal is to be at the top of the food chain, a Wicker\u2019s is to be the carrion bird, cleaning up after the fray. They remain on the fringes of society, holding court among the derelicts and destitute. If you only see one, take care; they can be in many places at once. You might not even notice them among the pigeons clogging the city streets, the murmurs of starlings inking the twilit sky. When they coalesce, they cut the kind of figure most folk would cross the street to avoid: ragged, soiled, <i>not quite right</i>. In their efforts to outpace the Strix and defend the All Night Society from its fringes, they\u2019ve slipped to the other side of the mirror. If they catch your eye, you might see horrible things, or feel like you\u2019re falling into the void, or be forced to fight against a sudden, debilitating fear. Consider this a handshake. It\u2019s a courtesy; they don\u2019t have to let you see them at all.<br /> <br /> When hunting, they take to many wings, shifting into murders and rookeries and parliaments and scattering themselves across the weald and suburb alike, joining with the nightmares they create. You don\u2019t want to be on the end of their talons unless you\u2019d like to lose a few pints. It\u2019s easier to feast from a thousand cuts than it is to drain a single corpse. Drink too much from one and their memories can transfer, swilling around with all the other voices in the Flock. That kind of invitation isn\u2019t given lightly.<br /> <br /> So, find the crumbled stairway, the forsaken ruins, the thousand glowing eyes. Make your request. When they\u2019re ready, the Hawks will find you.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Hawks, the Flock<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Curse of the Parliament): </b>Long have the Wickers and Strix warred, and the Owls watch for any signs of their enemy. If a Hawk [REDACTED]. On a failure, a Strix will find her before the end of the story. Each time this roll is a success, the Storyteller applies a cumulative \u20131 the next time it triggers. Once it goes off, this bane is dormant for the rest of the story, and any accrued penalties reset at the beginning of the next. As a rule of thumb, the Owl\u2019s Shadow Potency should be equal to the vampire\u2019s Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, <i>Auspex</i>, <i>Nightmare</i>, <i>Protean</i><br /> <br /> <b>New Devotion: The Murmur<br /> (Auspex \u2022\u2022, Nightmare \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> A Hawk can mingle her mind with the fragmented consciousness of her bloodline brethren, granting access to various memories, patterns, and esoteric secrets. This augury takes the form of a horrifying, existential vision, or a riddle of fragmentary images tainted by cajoling whispers. The prophecy requires decoding once connection to the Murmur is severed, but it contains the ability to disrupt fate in a significant way, including preventing an event, a disastrous decision, or even a death.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs no Experiences if the vampire meets the prerequisites.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>Upon successfully using this Devotion, subtract the number of times the vampire has used the effect in the current story from six. She suffers a breaking point at that level if it equals or is lower than her current Humanity. If the resulting number is negative, she takes a Humanity 1 breaking point with the difference as a penalty to her player\u2019s roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits + Occult + Auspex<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Duration: </b>One night per Blood Potency<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results<br /> <br /> Success: </b>The Murmur reveals the future in fits and starts. For each success on the activation roll, the vampire gains [REDACTED] on a number of future dice pools for the duration relating to the prophecy she gained. [REDACTED]. She cannot use this Devotion again until the duration expires or she uses all of her [REDACTED], whichever comes first.<br /> <br /> The Wicker can also bestow a [REDACTED] on another character by using Dread Presence to inflict a glimpse of her awful prophecy on the subject. If she uses Face of the Beast, she can bestow <i>all </i>these [REDACTED] on another character (who can forgo the usual resistance if they consent).<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>[REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>[REDACTED]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 05-06-2022, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T01:05:50-07:00","id":1480270,"title":"","content":"I love this concept. Wickers remind me of Classic WoD Malkavians as a Gangrel Bloodline and it just works for me.<br /> <br /> I assume that the Humanity cost of The Murmur cannot be replaced by a Bane, as other transgressions can?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 05-06-2022, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T01:27:29-07:00","id":1480271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480270#post1480270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that the Humanity cost of The Murmur cannot be replaced by a Bane, as other transgressions can?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it can't be obviated. You've got to give a bit of yourself to the Murmur to get anything back...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T06:10:22-07:00","id":1480282,"title":"","content":"And only now did I have the epiphany that being split across multiple bodies is a precaution against Strix possession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T08:47:38-07:00","id":1480292,"title":"","content":"Is there a connection between Risen Beasts and the Belial's Brood from Spilled Blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T13:14:17-07:00","id":1480306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480282#post1480282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And only now did I have the epiphany that being split across multiple bodies is a precaution against Strix possession.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure seems that way, don't it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480292#post1480292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a connection between Risen Beasts and the Belial's Brood from Spilled Blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>There can be if you want there to be! The Risen Beast is more about finding a way to directly deal with your vampiric instincts so they don't cause you quite as much trouble (pause for laughter), whereas the Brood just toss Humanity right out the window. On a related note, it occurs to me that we didn't really talk about what happens to Gangrel with Passengers who fall to Humanity 0; I may see if I can squeeze that in, though it's also something I'm happy to let STs play out on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T14:27:11-07:00","id":1480310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480306#post1480306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure seems that way, don't it...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There can be if you want there to be! The Risen Beast is more about finding a way to directly deal with your vampiric instincts so they don't cause you quite as much trouble (pause for laughter), whereas the Brood just toss Humanity right out the window. On a related note, it occurs to me that we didn't really talk about what happens to Gangrel with Passengers who fall to Humanity 0; I may see if I can squeeze that in, though it's also something I'm happy to let STs play out on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to me that a Passenger with a vampire who dropped to Humanity 0 just gets to walk into being an inherent Belial Brood member, but that's me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T15:06:32-07:00","id":1480313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480310#post1480310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems to me that a Passenger with a vampire who dropped to Humanity 0 just gets to walk into being an inherent Belial Brood member, but that's me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly one possibility! Alternatively, I could see it just becoming a regular-degular draugr without the Man to balance it out. Like I said, it might be better to leave it open, but I'll see if I can fit a line or two in about it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T16:08:54-07:00","id":1480318,"title":"","content":"Alright, today let's look at the <b>Baetyl</b>.<br /> <br /> This will be a bit brief because I'm slightly low on time today, but I wanted to talk about the Baetyl because they represented a more specific example of a broader theme I wanted to do with the book: Protean as a more general form of shapeshifting. Similar to the Yarilo (who we'll talk about soon), the Termites take on shapes that aren't the traditional &quot;beastly&quot; forms of Protean. For the Baetyl, that's taking on inorganic forms (which is also part of their bane), and I think that makes for a fun expansion of the Gangrel's general inhumanity.<br /> <br /> Not too much to say about the development process here; this was a bloodline I immediately loved upon seeing the concept, though it did go through some mechanical overhaul as it went along. In contrast to the Wickers, this is a good example of a bloodline that also has a lot of more esoteric aspects yet doesn't go too far off the baseline in terms of its power-set.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, their &quot;Once upon a midnight darkly&quot; origin is actually based on a true story. See if you can find it.<br /> <br /> So, here are the Baetyl! I might take tomorrow off, but we'll see if I feel up for some more commentary.<br /> <br /> <b>Baetyl: The ones who tower over you</b><br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;The mountain knows secrets to cleave the sky in twain.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> A statue looms over you upon a stained metal dais. It doesn\u2019t move its lips, but its voice echoes in your mind, telling you of nightmares you\u2019ve feared longer than you remember, and dreams that could one day become your reality. It\u2019s not offering you a bargain, though. The voice in your head doesn\u2019t want you to achieve those dreams \u2014 it only desires truth. To know you. To know everything.<br /> <br /> When flesh blossoms from the heart of stone and the monster inside grinds your bones and drinks your blood, you realize it\u2019s still listening, tapping into the secrets in your sinew.</i><br /> <br /> The land has a history all its own. The fawn that takes its nourishment from the bounty of the earth. The wolf that hunts the fawn. The vulture that feeds from the wolf when it becomes carrion. Each animal gives to the land as much as it takes, and every hunt and memory is ready for the Baetyl to collect.<br /> <br /> The Baetyl are the sages of Clan Gangrel. Not content to dine on blood alone, they feast on inanimate detritus, learning truths the rest of the All Night Society would trample over. Wisdom only comes with the patience of stone and earth, and for their unique relationship to the land, their siblings call them Termites. But a Baetyl prides herself on this distinction: She speaks for the speechless, and for her efforts, they reward her curiosity.<br /> <br /> To achieve this gnosis, a Termite\u2019s first morsel is the Bloody Core, a stone bezoar bathed in blood. Only by swallowing the thing whole can her becoming commence. This object helps Baetyl digest their strange diets, and it changes their forms to better reflect that \u2014 in the end \u2014 you really are what they eat. Even the plastics and processed metals of the kine are just more fuel to a Termite, from which she can form steel teeth, granite claws, and unblinking electric eyes. Some can masquerade as statues, or the very ground beneath their quarry\u2019s feet. Kindred are right to fear a Haunt cloaked in shadows, or their minds breaking under the weight of a Lord\u2019s words, but how often does a Lick think of the pavement he walks upon? The stairs he climbs as he stalks his prey? What about the blood fountain at the center of Elysium?<br /> <br /> Some Termites share their gift \u2014 not with other Kindred, of course, but the dead familiars they raise in the bond of death. They feed their loyal hounds with gravel kibble and iron T-bone steaks; even bones have calcium around the soft and worthless marrow. By the time stone and iron grows where once was fur, the Baetyl is ready to help soothe the creature\u2019s pain. They add to the raw beauty of nature\u2019s hand with runes, spirals, and potent curses to make the stone hide flexible and durable. Some Termites raise more than one monster this way, both a statuary and a menagerie of things lesser minds might call homunculi \u2014 or just abominations.<br /> <br /> Then there are the Baetyl who focus on themselves. Instead of making monsters, they make themselves monstrous. Through the twisted manipulation of their bodies and the potency of Vitae, they endow themselves with animal features refined with the potency of mineral and earth. She\u2019s the jack-booted thug who walks into war chewing down a box of nails. He\u2019s the assassin whose wooden claws break a target\u2019s heart. The Baetyl are both wisemen and warriors, natural and unnatural. They are the eyes of unblinking statues and the creaks in floorboards, the paper with ceaseless stories written in inks of soil, metal, and blood. Do not fear the monster. Fear what it knows.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan:</b> Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Termites, Gargoyles (erroneously)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Chimeric Curse): </b>As a Baetyl ages and her connection to mortality wanes, more and more of the inorganic material ground up by the Bloody Core remains in her body, pushing up against the skin. This takes the form of strange nubs and bumps, like stone or metal teeth, or flesh turning stone gray. As such, her ability to interact with mortals is limited. In addition to the Feral Curse, Baetyl effectively have the same bane as the Nosferatu (<b>Vampire</b>, p. 103).<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, <i>Auspex</i>, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: The Bezoar Core</b><br /> <br /> Baetyl can consume inorganic and inanimate matter. As long as a Termite can fit an object in her mouth, she can swallow it. Once per scene, [REDACTED].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T21:20:26-07:00","id":1480335,"title":"","content":"The word 'baetyl' leads me to 'baetylus' and then 'Bethel', then the latter links to mantras like ONE MORE GOD REJECTED in my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T12:52:18-07:00","id":1480388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480335#post1480335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The word 'baetyl' leads me to 'baetylus' and then 'Bethel', then the latter links to mantras like ONE MORE GOD REJECTED in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>believe </i>the following definition is what the author was going for:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiktionary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(historical) A meteorite or similar-looking rough stone thought to be of divine origin and worshipped as sacred.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T14:14:38-07:00","id":1480409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480388#post1480388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I <i>believe </i>the following definition is what the author was going for:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that\u2019s what baetylus seems to mean. Common motif all over the world.<br /> <br /> It just happens to be that, for me stones of worship also mentally links to Shin Megami Tensei \u2014 and I consider that a plus <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T14:58:13-07:00","id":1480484,"title":"","content":"Welcome back!<br /> <br /> Did end up taking the day off yesterday, but I'm here again with the <b>Yarilo</b>.<br /> <br /> These are Gangrel who extend their power over Animals onto plants, and in turn extend their power over human minds to make mortals more plantlike. They take up more natural domains than a lot of modern Gangrel, though many of them have adapted quite well to city life; wherever you can find flora, the Vines will be creeping in like kudzu.<br /> <br /> This bloodline had a fair bit of ink spilled on it through development, at least in terms of mechanics. Initially, their mind-control powers weren't based on Dominate, but I felt that was too much of a case of reinventing the wheel; it's easier to come up with expansions for a power than to build a new system from the ground up. I also swapped out Resilience for Celerity, because that had more of a plant vibe (especially considering their bane).<br /> <br /> Like the Baetyl, the Yarilo are another bloodline where the body horror aspect of the clan takes on a different aesthetic. We actually had a whole sidebar about &quot;green Protean&quot; transformations, but ultimately I had to cut it for space, and I figured that aspect isn't buried too deep in the main text.<br /> <br /> So, here are the Yarilo. Tomorrow, I'll be going over some case files with the Daimonion, after which we have one more bloodline left!<br /> <br /> Oh, incidentally: it's come to my attention that there were some issues when I updated the clan books last month, so if you've updated since the 29th, or have purchased them for the first time, you may have still ended up with the old versions (and, for some reason, the Ventrue book had a bunch of its hyperlinks missing). Those are all fixed now. I'll be updating <b>Wild Hunt </b>with errata once I'm done posting excerpts, but I'll let everyone know when I do.<br /> <br /> <b>Yarilo: The ones who outgrow you</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cBreathe deep and cast off your cares. Be returned to the oldest power \u2014 the first power: Nature.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>\u2014 Pin your heart on the hawthorn tree</b><br /> <br /> Villagers in Ashbrook have given the old orchard a wide berth since the 1700s, after a plague swept the town causing all who lived there to walk in trances, tending to the trees but neglecting all other duties. Only when the church sent a new priest to the parish were the people slowly pulled out of their collective fugue.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2014 Paint its white bark red with blood</b><br /> <br /> He instituted an offering of lamb\u2019s blood on the roots of the trees, a practice that continues to this day on the vernal equinox. All was peaceful, at least until a fateful August afternoon in 1975, when a developer came to town with the intention of razing the gnarled old forest and putting up a shopping complex.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2014 Wait for the harvest moon to glow</b><br /> <br /> Despite the protests of some superstitious locals, the bulldozers rolled through, pushing down the first line of ancient peach trees. That night, on the full moon, the orchard fought back. Grinding earth and shrieking metal sounded through the still night air.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2014 The wood\u2019s savage might shall reap and sow.</b><br /> <br /> In the morning, the villagers saw that the old trees had moved. The machinery was all suspended in their branches, twisted beyond repair, and the construction workers and their big-city developer were gone. The only trace was a red color flushing the roots of all the trees. The spirits of the orchard had been appeased, it seemed. With luck, they\u2019ll sleep again for another two hundred years. </i><br /> <br /> The Yarilo are one with the pulse of the earth. This obscure bloodline of Savages is tied to the trees for their protection, community, and power. Far more interested in the flora over the fauna of their domains, the Vines creep through the greenspaces of the All Night Society, dedicated to preserving and mastering nature. Their long-sighted temperament makes them less brash than other Gangrel, but just as wild \u2014 and territorial. While others of their clan lash out with claw and fang, the Vines camouflage themselves in forest canopies, difficult to find and even harder to harm. And rather than trust their fates to blood-bound ghouls, the Vines\u2019 mental control spreads out in a miasma of spores, rendering their retainers pliable and docile. A true herd.<br /> <br /> Yet, despite their inextricable ties to nature, Yarilo can be found in even the most urban settings so long as there\u2019s a tree to hang from. Their philosophy is simple: Grow, flourish, and keep out. Their goals, however, are more complex, and their co-existence with the kine oscillates between shepherding their food and culling their foes. Either way, they embrace a role of stewardship. They are the taciturn graveyard gardener escorting generation after generation to their eternal rest. They are the game warden with the unseasonably high record of hunting accidents. They are the old-growth forest logging protester whose enemies suddenly have a glassy-eyed change of heart.<br /> <br /> Vines play their part in the Masquerade like long-suffering grandparents waiting for their wards to grow up. If they\u2019re beneficent, it\u2019s because the forest is an ecosystem full of bounty. If they are terrible, it\u2019s because nature is unforgiving. The woods hold grudges, and they are covetous of their land. So tread lightly, and be careful when you\u2019re pruning branches. Look twice at every lonely tree. You\u2019ll survive in the Yarilo\u2019s kingdom only if they allow it.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Vines, Arboreals<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Tinderbox Curse):</b> With their deep connection to forests, it should come as no surprise the Yarilo fear fire above all, but not in the way other Kindred might expect. As they draw closer to the Beast by embracing the wild, fire becomes a spiritual bane as well as a physical one. Whenever a Vine takes damage from fire [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, Celerity, <i>Dominate</i>, <i>Protean</i><br /> <br /> <b>New Devotions</b><br /> <br /> As an additional prerequisite, a Yarilo must learn Spore before they he acquires other Devotions from the following powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Spore<br /> (Dominate \u2022, Protean \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> The most basic of the Yarilo\u2019s mind-influencing abilities, this Devotion allows Vines to implant potential servants with mind-altering, fungus-like spores.<br /> This Devotion costs no Experiences if the vampire meets the prerequisites.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae<br /> <br /> <b>Requirement:</b> The vampire must have the blush of life active.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>None<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Duration: </b>Scene<br /> <br /> Once per scene, the Yarilo can spew out a continuous cloud of microscopic spores as she breathes and speaks. Any mortal who inhales theses spores over the course of the scene becomes trivially susceptible to the vampire\u2019s Dominate effects, applying half her Protean dots as a penalty on all rolls to resist. The vampire can affect a number of individuals in a scene equal to her Blood Potency plus one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T18:36:19-07:00","id":1480500,"title":"","content":"So that\u2019s where the vampire melons and pumpkins come from <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T08:32:12-07:00","id":1480546,"title":"","content":"The Yarilo are probably my favorite bloodline in the book. Anything that makes you look at it and go &quot;<i>that's</i> a vampire?&quot; wins points with me, and this book is full of those kinds of bloodlines, but the Yarilo's merits and devotions are just so cool and evocative. That they have similarities to my favorite 1E bloodline, the Asnam, is icing on the cake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T15:01:52-07:00","id":1480584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480546#post1480546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Yarilo are probably my favorite bloodline in the book. Anything that makes you look at it and go &quot;<i>that's</i> a vampire?&quot; wins points with me, and this book is full of those kinds of bloodlines, but the Yarilo's merits and devotions are just so cool and evocative. That they have similarities to my favorite 1E bloodline, the Asnam, is icing on the cake.</div> </div> </div> </div>That Asnam-like Devotion is one of my favourites in the book. Funny enough, another author had a similar concept as a general Devotion, but I ultimately felt the idea worked better as a bloodline effect.<br /> <br /> Anyway, let's talk about the Daimonion.<br /> <br /> The first thing you'll no doubt notice is the name, which was the author's (our very own <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar272_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"272\" data-vbnamecard=\"272\">saibot</a>) little joke about a certain misspelled Discipline of old...<br /> <br /> The Daimonion are what amount to Gangrel therapists. They're the ones you go to when the inchoate rage in your head is causing you serious issues. This was a pretty solid concept from start to finish; a few tweaks here and there, but I was very happy with the first draft. The only major tweak I made was replacing Resilience with Vigor: A) because we already had two other bloodlines with the exact same spread (Auspex was popular in this book), and B) because that felt a bit more &quot;active&quot; and assertive. The Daimonion don't just sit idly by while you rage out: they apply some hardcore cognitive behavioral therapy on your ass.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll let saibot chime in on any specific details!<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, I'll be back with the final bloodline: the Cerrid, who have been waiting patiently to steal the spotlight. After that, I might dip into the antagonist chapter, or I might discuss the Risen Beast...<br /> <br /> <b>Daimonion: The ones who've got you figured out</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I'm listening.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> What is the Beast? Ask a hundred different Kindred and you\u2019ll get a hundred different answers. Ask the Sanctified or Dragons and they\u2019ll tell you it\u2019s a curse inflicted by a vengeful God. Ask an Acolyte and she\u2019ll speak of the madness of Dionysus and the furor of the Erinyes. Ask the Night Doctor and he\u2019ll yammer on about supercharged Ids. Whatever the truth, if there even is a single one, all Kindred accept that the Beast is <i>personal</i>. Whether it\u2019s the worst part of yourself exaggerated by the Curse, unsullied animal instincts, or something else altogether, there\u2019s some sympathy between a vampire\u2019s Beast and the dead heart it nests within. If you understand the Beast, you understand the Man, though vampires in frenzy aren\u2019t known for being talkative.<br /> <br /> In truth, the Beast is always talking if you know the right frequency. And the Daimonion are <i>always </i>tuned in.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a common refrain that Gangrel \u201cget\u201d the Beast better than the rest of the Damned, but if any special insight truly exists, it\u2019s limited to their own, personal dark sides. Conversely, the Counselors are keenly aware of what other Beasts have to say about their \u201cowners,\u201d and this sense makes them invaluable to their Kindred, taking up respectable roles as psychoanalysts, therapists, or advisors to princes, bishops, and other powerbrokers. Their odd practice of \u201cTherian Psychoanalysis\u201d has earned them as good a reputation as any bloodline of Savages might earn, though detractors like to point out how easy it is to abuse their positions. Trust comes at a premium in the All Night Society, but the unique advantages (and frailties) of the Daimonion encourage some measure of cooperative thinking \u2014 mutually assured destruction among the wicked dead.<br /> <br /> In Ancient Greece, a <i>daim\u00f3nion </i>was a spirit guide or inner voice, one that would warn you of lapses in judgment and lead you to wise and moral action. Like their namesake, the Counselors are also guides of a sort \u2014 and isn\u2019t the Beast just another <i>daim\u00f3nion</i>? No surprise, they say, how often the council of Beast Whisperers leads to controlled atrocities. Critics are also quick to point out another etymology: From \u201cdaimon\u201d came \u201cdemon,\u201d and one might wonder if members of this line aren\u2019t just shoulder devils in tweed.<br /> <br /> Consider the wild-eyed shrink. She has the ears of the city\u2019s high officials and advises them on ways to manage the severe pressure of their Requiems. Pressure must be dealt with productively, she says. That\u2019s what the Beast is: pressure. But what might happen if her deep insights into the workings of the court were to fall into the wrong hands?<br /> <br /> Consider the diplomat. She doesn\u2019t break you with sledgehammer words or ensnare you with her aura of glory, but she does know what you want and how you tick. Your Beast told her. Don\u2019t worry; she just wants what\u2019s best for the domain, but alas, sometimes that means breaking some bones. Diplomacy among bloodthirsty monsters can be so heated.<br /> <br /> Consider the implacable sheriff. He can hold his own in a scrap, but his true strength is his unfailing insight. Whether it\u2019s hunting down draugr and other fallen Kindred or just plain and simple criminals, he\u2019s always a step ahead of his oh-so-predictable quarry. The Kindred sing his praises, but you don\u2019t clean up other\u2019s messes without learning a thing or two \u2014 or developing a few grudges.<br /> <br /> What do these Daimonion guide their Kindred toward, and why do they do it? If they know, they aren\u2019t telling. And what do they learn from their chats with the Beast? Pray they won\u2019t tell you, or else you might never be able to look in a mirror again.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Counselors, Beast Whisperers<br /> <br /> Bloodline Bane (The Curse of Attunement): A Daimonion\u2019s instinctual understanding of other Beasts goes deep \u2014 deeper than is comfortable. If a Counselor has the Tempted Condition at any level, when another vampire enters involuntary frenzy in her presence (that is, not riding the wave or using the Coil of the Wyrm), she must spend a Willpower or resist frenzy as well. The desire of the Beast in this case is to assist the vampire who triggered this sympathetic frenzy. A Counselor can only be in a sympathetic frenzy with one other vampire at a time. Once a Counselor has spent a Willpower to resist this lure, she is immune to this frenzy trigger for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Animalism, <i>Auspex</i>, <i>Protean</i>, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: An Ear for the Beast</b><br /> <br /> Daimonion are deeply perceptive of the needs and wants of other Kindred, as communicated by their Beasts. When asking the Storyteller questions with Auspex, a Daimonion gains an additional question as long as it pertains to a vampire\u2019s Beast. This includes questions related to frenzy, Kindred needs, and the mark\u2019s Dirge. If a Counselor acts on this knowledge in the same scene, she achieves an exceptional success on three successes on a relevant action. This benefit can be transferred to the subject if the Counselor communicates the insight.<br /> <br /> When a Counselor uses Auspex on [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit<br /> <br /> Therian Psychoanalysis (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Prerequisites:</b> Daimonion, Manipulation \u2022\u2022\u2022, Composure \u2022\u2022\u2022, Animalism \u2022 or Auspex \u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Your character knows how to rein in a rampaging Beast and draw forth the Man. She has an instinctual understanding of the way frenzying vampires think, move, and attack, keeping her safe as she takes control of the situation.<br /> <br /> <b>Soothe the Beast (\u2022): </b>Your character can use psychological tricks to diffuse the Beast\u2019s rage. As an extended action, she can attempt to talk another vampire out of frenzy as if she were one of his Touchstones (<b>Vampire</b>, p. 104).<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 05-09-2022, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T16:02:23-07:00","id":1480590,"title":"","content":"I would definitely like to hear about the Risen Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T13:31:02-07:00","id":1480687,"title":"","content":"Let's check in on our final bloodline: The Cerrid!<br /> <br /> Now, I don't know about you, but I've always wanted to play a vampire bard, and I think the author did a wonderful job of making that concept much scarier than it might first appear on the surface. The Cerrid are musicians, sure, but they're also urban legends: the guitar-wielding devil at the crossroads, the siren on the edge of the cliff, or (if you want to get a little German Expressionist) the serial killer who whistles &quot;In the Hall of the Mountain King&quot; as he stalks his prey.<br /> <br /> This bloodline had a fair bit of retooling from concept to final draft. Originally, they were more focused on infiltrating the music industry and being pop stars, but there were a few problems with that. For one, we'd kind of done it. One of our previous bloodlines, the Von Schrecks (cf. <b>Better Feared: Nosferatu</b>), is a gang of high rollers in the biz, and while they're more about movies than music, I felt we'd covered the vampires-in-the-entertainment-industry trope pretty well there. I also felt that the initial concept, as presented, was a bit more Daeva than Gangrel. But wandering minstrels who take blood as payment and have to feed their monstrous egos or else they <i>mutate</i>? That's very Savage.<br /> <br /> This bloodline is also a little bit of an homage to both the Gangrel and Ravnos of <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b>. Their bane is similar to the Outlanders', and their Devotions are a bit Chimerstry-esque, at least in one case (their Discipline spread is also, legitimately unintentionally, the same as <b>V5 </b>Ravnos, plus Protean).<br /> <br /> With all that said, here's the Cerrid, making their debut. Since this is the last bloodline, I think tomorrow I'll be back with some material on the Risen Beast, our big &quot;special&quot; system for this book.<br /> <br /> <b>Cerrid: The ones whose songs consume you</b><br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;Words bite as well as teeth.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> The key change comes with the slick sound of fangs running over her lip, halfway through a private performance in the wee hours of the morning. Her prey watches as if a goddess of music holds him in place, but really, it\u2019s just the result of her careful chord progressions. She likes to play with her food (in more ways than one), likes to see how far she can push their minds while holding their bodies in place with her song, taking in the way adrenaline and fear catapult through their systems.<br /> <br /> When she finally sinks her teeth through the soft flesh of his neck, it\u2019s a symphony of salty citrus. Each victim tastes different, and she revels in each new movement of the hunt.</i><br /> <br /> The Cerrid are traveling bards and poets without a home. Sappho and Homer didn\u2019t make their names singing hymns standing still, and they certainly didn\u2019t find their meals that way. Like many Gangrel, wanderlust consumes the Beguilers, but where other Savages slink, they hunt out in the open. They are sirens and harpies and sphinxes, coaxing prey with hypnotic lyrics before letting their Beasts devour. They recite improvised ballads at open-mic nights, staying only long enough to consume fawning fans or bring another into their sycophantic entourages. They are ghosts moving through the music industry, disappearing as quickly as they rise into the limelight.<br /> <br /> The Cerrid are slippery, sonorous yet monstrous. A Beguiler\u2019s immortal nature means her public persona will always become untenable when she doesn\u2019t age along with her career, and when this happens, she relinquishes her identity and grafts a fresh title to her dead heart. Some take this as an opportunity to learn a new instrument or enter a new genre, while others stick to what they know with more intensity than a coke high. Maybe she meets a spectacular demise as her popularity peaks, only to be spotted weeks later in the streets of Vegas, passed off as some incredible impersonator. Celebrity is overrated. For a Beguiler, the best part of being a musician is not the untouchable fame of uber-celebrity, it\u2019s the grungy bars where elbows rubbed become necks bitten.<br /> <br /> Beguilers can be solo acts or ensembles. An acoustic folk singer shares the coffeehouse stage with no one but their guitar, and a singer forms bonds with a sharp-toothed backup band, but regardless of her crew\u2019s size, a Cerrid always leaves behind worshippers \u2014 and legends. A banshee creeps into the bedrooms of unfaithful men to torture them with the terrible melancholy of her voice. A selkie at the riverbend plays the guitar so beautifully it adds years to your life, but only if you first provide a drop of your finest vintage. They are the unsettlingly cheerful whistle in the empty alley and the sinister rhyme that predicts the prey\u2019s demise. And once the music stops, so do you.<br /> <br /> It isn\u2019t all fame and fans and folklore, though. No, it\u2019s all about the art, and the Beast is the only audience that really matters. If a Beguiler fails to perform, to feed the hungry thing in her head with praise, the Beast claws through the human mask: scales dance up the side of her face and too pointed ears lilt upward. Even as they feed on warm bodies, the Beast is always hungry for an ego boost.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan:</b> Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Beguilers, Troubadours<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Cadenza Curse): </b>Music has charms to soothe the savage beast, and a Beguiler unleashes hers when she\u2019s disconnected from her art. At least once every (11 \u2013 Blood Potency) nights, a Cerrid must [REDACTED] via some form of performance. If not, the Beast rises to the surface: Fur sprouts on her hands, pupils contract into slits, or scales splash up her arms. This mutation reduces her effective Humanity by two dots for the purposes of the Feral Curse. To return to normal, she must regain [REDACTED] via performance. Otherwise, the mutation lasts until she next falls to torpor.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism, <i>Majesty</i>, Obfuscate, <i>Protean</i><br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: The Golden Throat</b><br /> <br /> The Blood grants all Cerrid a natural gift for story and song. Upon entry into the bloodline, Beguilers take a dot of Expression. If a Cerrid character already has the maximum dots in Expression, her player can raise a different Social Skill instead. Furthermore, when a Cerrid spends Willpower to bolster mundane Expression actions, she takes a +5 instead of a +3.<br /> <br /> <b>New Devotion: Fata Morgana<br /> (Majesty \u2022\u2022, Obfuscate \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Whether poetry or music, a Beguiler has the power to shape the world around her using only words.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 2 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>None<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Duration: </b>Scene<br /> <br /> For the rest of the scene, the vampire can use Obfuscate effects with her voice rather than via touch. Use the system for Touch of Shadow, applying any costs from other Obfuscate effects as normal. She can use her Discipline on any object or person she can see within (10 \u00d7 Blood Potency) meters; all she needs to do is paint a word picture of the desired effect, though the result is limited by her level of Obfuscate. For example, she can\u2019t make a door look like a castle gate unless she knows The Familiar Stranger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T23:20:08-07:00","id":1480730,"title":"","content":"Maybe one interesting little info with the Daimonion is that &quot;vampire psychotherapist/analysist&quot; was not the idea right from the start. I originally wanted to do a bloodline that has some special attunement and understanding for draugrs, but during the initial brainstorming it quickly became clear that it was too nich\u00e9 of a concept, so I broadened that to a more general &quot;Beast whisperer&quot; archetype, which then quickly turned into what we have now.<br /> <br /> The name of the bloodline was actually one of the last things I decided on. It actually came to me while trying to find inspiration in psychological and psychoanalyst terminology. Thus, the name originally came from its use in Jungian psychoanalysis. The connection to the etymology for &quot;demon&quot; was of course amazingly convenient and thematic, as was the opportunity for a small dig at the often bizarre Discipline names in Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Feel free to ask if there's anything else you are curious about!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T13:28:48-07:00","id":1480760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480730#post1480730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe one interesting little info with the Daimonion is that &quot;vampire psychotherapist/analysist&quot; was not the idea right from the start. I originally wanted to do a bloodline that has some special attunement and understanding for draugrs, but during the initial brainstorming it quickly became clear that it was too nich\u00e9 of a concept, so I broadened that to a more general &quot;Beast whisperer&quot; archetype, which then quickly turned into what we have now.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I was going over the book with my group, we definitely spent a moment wondering how the Daimonion's capabilities would interact with draugr [and Passengers, for that matter]. We eventually concluded that those sorts of interactions would be such enormous edge cases that we figured it was a &quot;what works best for the table/story&quot; situation, but it is very interesting to hear that they were originally envisioned as attuned to draugr...<br /> <br /> Also, the Risen Beast is definitely my group's favorite thing from the book, so I'm excited to hear more about its development!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T15:42:11-07:00","id":1480769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480760#post1480760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I was going over the book with my group, we definitely spent a moment wondering how the Daimonion's capabilities would interact with draugr [and Passengers, for that matter]. We eventually concluded that those sorts of interactions would be such enormous edge cases that we figured it was a &quot;what works best for the table/story&quot; situation, but it is very interesting to hear that they were originally envisioned as attuned to draugr...<br /> <br /> Also, the Risen Beast is definitely my group's favorite thing from the book, so I'm excited to hear more about its development!</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny enough, how the Risen Beast relates to the Daimonion and the Society of the Accord was an issue I tossed around a <i>lot </i>during development. Ultimately, I also came down on the &quot;edge case&quot; side of things; the Passenger is, ultimately, an optional system, and I didn't want to spend too much effort trying to jive everything together. That said, maybe I'll see if I can come up with some options in a forum post at some point.<br /> <br /> Now, speaking of the Risen Beast...<br /> <br /> This was our traditional &quot;the clan gets a unique subsystem&quot; chapter (a concept I've yet to find a succinct way to describe). It was actually the only one of these chapters <i>I</i> didn't come up with in the planning stage: it was, in fact, the brilliant idea of the chapter's sole author, which was another first for us. Typically, each chapter is collaborative to some degree (apart from the theme fiction that runs through the book). Usually, a couple of writers do the setting and one does the system, but this time, we felt it would be best to keep things to one voice, since this idea was brand new.<br /> <br /> Well, <i>technically </i>brand new. A sentient Beast concept <i>has </i>shown up in <b>Requiem </b>before. If anyone remembers the old <b>Chronicler's Guide </b>(which is somehow not a Storyteller's Guide), that book describes &quot;The Other&quot;, a sort of Shard system before Shards were a thing. We didn't really use that as a basis for our concept, but it was certainly in the back of my mind throughout development.<br /> <br /> So, what <i>is </i>the Risen Beast (AKA, the Passenger)? Well, I'll let our excerpt of the day do the talking for me. Tomorrow, I might start going into the ghoul families, though I'm also tempted to check in on the Brides of Dracula...<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>The Beast, Arisen</b>\u200b</div> <br /> Kindred like to pretend they\u2019re separate from their Beasts \u2014 that the atrocities they commit in the grips of frenzy aren\u2019t their fault, but that of another entity. It\u2019s a convenient collective lie that better allows vampires to cope with their Requiems. But, it is a lie. Kindred are monsters, and \u201cthe Beast\u201d is just their name for the collection of brutal instincts they possess but can\u2019t bear to accept. In a way, it\u2019s no different from superstitious mortals blaming evil spirits for their own misdeeds (\u201cThe devil made me do it!\u201d)<br /> <br /> Except\u2026 why does the Beast sometimes know things Kindred don\u2019t? If it\u2019s just a bundle of feral reactions, how does it know an assassin\u2019s lurking in a packed concert hall, or how to work the bizarre ligaments of the wings you just grew? Most vampires dismiss these questions as irrelevant. At best, the Beast is a tool to use against one\u2019s prey and one\u2019s enemies, and it should otherwise be kept locked in a box to better muffle its howling.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel, of course, have no choice but to listen to the Beast, as it lurks so much closer to the surface of their minds. Other clans banish their wilder sides to the cracks and crevices of their psyches, but the Savage Beast prowls just beneath the skin. Spend enough time listening to its growls and mutterings, and you might start to think it\u2019s something more than impulse and hunger. Some Gangrel, desperate for a sense of control, listen closer to those sounds, trying to make sense of the rage within. Some even talk to their \u201cother,\u201d like children might chat with a spooky imaginary friend; they know it\u2019s not real, but it\u2019s still calming to pretend someone\u2019s listening, even if that someone scares you.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s only when the Beast talks back that these Savages start to worry about what, exactly, they\u2019ve awakened.<br /> <br /> <b>To Grandmother's House We Go</b><br /> <br /> In the beginning, they were faint whispers in trees and distant howls through misty nights. Tonight, they exist as geocaches in federal parks and dead drops buried in forgotten subway tunnels: Rumors and stories of Gangrel who\u2019ve made their Beast into something more \u2014 more cunning, more rational\u2026 more dangerous. Savages who\u2019ve taken their worst impulses and forged them into something that thinks, something they can speak to or even bargain with. Clever. Patient. Risen.<br /> <br /> The name of the first to awaken their Beast is lost to the fog of history, but it\u2019s been happening for a long time, for at least as long as humans have had words to speak and understood the concepts of us and them \u2014 with all the violence contained within that distinction. Introspective Savages reckon it\u2019s their very independence that\u2019s responsible for the Risen phenomenon. If you never have to look outward for help, all that\u2019s left is to look within, and for Kindred, that means taking a long, hard look at the Beast.<br /> <br /> Some wonder if there\u2019s a more sentimental explanation, though. Gangrel, more than any others among the Damned, can survive all on their own, but that can lead to a rather secluded Requiem. If you can\u2019t trust other Licks, and humans are food, and animals are servants, who do you talk to? Who can you tell your secret fears or dreams? Who can you cry out to in the middle of the dark woods in order to prove you still exist? Perhaps, some speculate, the first Risen were born not of utility or soul-searching, but of loneliness.<br /> <br /> Gangrel aren\u2019t exactly known for historical records, so there\u2019s not a lot of hard documentation regarding the Risen. While it\u2019s not exactly a clan secret, it\u2019s difficult to confirm rumors of the Risen Beast amidst all the other stories surrounding the Savages. If the oldest Gangrel in the city claims to talk to her Beast, and that it answers, most Kindred aren\u2019t going to question her, but they probably don\u2019t actually believe her. At least not out loud. How do you prove the reality of a mental Passenger without sounding mad? In recent nights, Gangrel of a more scholarly bent, notably in the Circle of the Crone and Ordo Dracul, are attempting to put to paper their findings on the Risen, but for now, it remains a deeply personal journey.<br /> <br /> <b>Snips, Snails, and Puppy-Dog Tails</b><br /> <br /> There\u2019s no codified process to awaken the Beast, no certified ritual that guarantees success. The ways instinct and anger undergo metamorphosis into awareness and cunning are as individual as the Gangrel who attempt them. Some even stumble upon the process accidentally, desperation leading them to elevate the Beast for want of any other ally.<br /> <br /> The one constant is sacrifice. A Savage must give of themself in order to make the Beast more than it is. The form the sacrifice takes doesn\u2019t matter, just so long as it tears a piece of the vampire\u2019s Humanity away with it. The only caveat is that the vampire making this sacrifice cannot frenzy as she makes it. The sacrifice is a gift, given knowingly or otherwise from the vampire\u2019s conscious self to the Beast to aid in its rising.<ul><li>In the crumbling remains of a tenement building, clawed hands scrape symbols into peeling plaster. The bound man on the floor struggles against his bonds, pleading for his life, but his voice is not the one his captor wants to hear.</li> <li>The polished floors of the hunting lodge are scuffed where the corpses have fallen, but there\u2019s not a drop of blood to be found. She\u2019s promised every rivulet to the hunger inside her so it might listen the next time she begs it to stop.</li> <li>His fingers scrabble at the stalagmite impaling his belly, dead guts spilling out around it. He knows he doesn\u2019t need those pale organs anymore, that he should be able to pull himself up and off \u2014 but he can\u2019t. In the void of the cave, he calls out for someone, anyone, to help him, and from the darkness in his own mind, something responds.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>The Voice in My Head Doesn\u2019t Like You</b><br /> <br /> Those who make the sacrifice and survive the consequences feel the change immediately. They\u2019re not alone in their head anymore \u2014 something is listening to them, watching them, searching for weakness. The occasional, whispered word can be heard among the Beast\u2019s ever-present shrieks: Feed. Flee. Kill.<br /> <br /> When the first real words form, many Gangrel deny what they\u2019ve done. However, the Risen Beast will quickly make itself impossible to ignore. It no longer just demands action with urge and instinct. It speaks and, what\u2019s more, it questions:<br /> <br /> <i>Why not take it all? We\u2019re hungry.<br /> <br /> Are you sure you should let her live? She\u2019ll just hurt us again.<br /> <br /> The sun comes soon. Is this meeting really worth it?</i><br /> <br /> While it might sound disconcerting \u2014 and it is \u2014 to have a second voice questioning your choices, the advantage to having a Passenger is that the vampire can now explain herself, and show her Beast a world beyond the momentary present:<br /> <br /> <i>We leave some so we\u2019re not marked as a poacher.<br /> <br /> She owes us her life now, and that\u2019s more valuable than her ashes.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re winning the negotiations, and this will give us access to much richer feeding grounds.</i><br /> <br /> Naturally, it doesn\u2019t always work. Sometimes the Beast still boils over, but bargaining isn\u2019t an option other Kindred even know exists, let alone how to access it. Gangrel know the Beast must be sated eventually; it can only be put off with words for so long, and you can\u2019t hide from something in your own mind. In the meantime, however, remaining in control when other Kindred would fall to mindless fear or anger is invaluable. What\u2019s more, negotiation is only the first step in a relationship that could last for centuries\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Me and My Shadow</b><br /> After compromise comes cooperation. The Beast is now the Gangrel\u2019s Passenger; it has no choice in this, but it also has independent desires now, which may be very different from those of the vampire who rose it up. A Risen Beast soon acquires a personality, a twisted shadow of its Savage\u2019s, and while it\u2019s still a being of impulse and gluttony, its goals extend beyond simple animal instinct:<br /> <br /> <i>He always thinks he\u2019s so much smarter than us. We should show him! Hurt him so he never looks down on us again!<br /> <br /> The markers need to be clear. No one should be ignorant of our territory. I\u2019m thinking\u2026 dog skulls with rusted nails for teeth! It\u2019s good, right? You love it.<br /> <br /> Another meeting? But we just fucking got here! Skip it! Don\u2019t go! Look, that blond over there is winking at us. I bet he tastes like spun sugar\u2026</i><br /> <br /> One might be tempted to ignore these selfish agendas and get on with more important activities, but sometimes indulgence has a power all its own. Perhaps your Passenger thinks the blood of dancers tastes the most delectable. Drink deeply from the local recital hall and you\u2019ll find your senses sharper and your reflexes faster as your inner predator moves in concert. The Beast was born of you, after all, and the things it wants are, somewhere down in a shameful corner of your soul, the things you want too.<br /> <br /> This new dynamic dramatically alters the experience of frenzy. Usually, holding back the Beast is an act of concentrated will, a stamping down of mindless desire and instinct. However, with a Passenger riding shotgun in your brain, frenzy can be less \u201cgiving in\u201d and more \u201cletting go.\u201d The Beast is always stronger and sharper than you, so when some asshole you both hate needs his insides turned into outsides, why not let the Risen handle it?<br /> <br /> With you and your Beast in agreement, there\u2019s no struggle, simply action, and a deep satisfaction as your enemy falls to ribbons at the business end of your claws. Of course, working so closely with the Beast blurs the lines of identity, making any frenzy harder to resist. It can be tempting to just let the monster have what it wants, when it wants, but complacency may mean you can\u2019t stop when it really matters.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s another benefit, however. With a Risen Beast making a lair in his mind, the vampire becomes immune to possession by the Birds of Dis, or any other entity that cares to try (including Lords). Having gained enough sapience to have its own wants and needs, the Beast rejects any third party trying to slip into its already crowded headspace. Any successful attempt to subsume the vampire\u2019s mind instead results in frenzy as the Passenger violently displaces the intruder. If this effect were more widely known, perhaps more Gangrel would seek out the change.<br /> <br /> However, if a whole clan became resistant to the Parliament\u2019s predations\u2026 well. Ask the Julii what it\u2019s like defying the Strix.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T17:14:04-07:00","id":1480779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480769#post1480769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, speaking of the Risen Beast...<br /> <br /> This was our traditional &amp;quot;the clan gets a unique subsystem&amp;quot; chapter (a concept I've yet to find a succinct way to describe).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cSignature Subsystem\u201d ? Can\u2019t go wrong with alliterative names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T17:19:48-07:00","id":1480781,"title":"","content":"Yeah, The Other was what I thought of when I heard the word \u2018Passenger\u2019. Glad to see it turned out correct <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I find Passengers ironically amusing in how its the Savages who turn out to have a system (potentially) based on the more Humane desires \u2014 staving off loneliness, and seeking negotiation.<br /> <br /> To me, the Risen Beast in general also evokes certain forms of Divergence (Deviant), and a couple of Goetic Legacies (Mage). Interesting\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T17:36:48-07:00","id":1480784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480779#post1480779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u201cSignature Subsystem\u201d ? Can\u2019t go wrong with alliterative names.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might just steal that...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T17:42:12-07:00","id":1480785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480784#post1480784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might just steal that...</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not stealing if it\u2019s up for free! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T02:02:03-07:00","id":1480816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480760#post1480760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I was going over the book with my group, we definitely spent a moment wondering how the Daimonion's capabilities would interact with draugr [and Passengers, for that matter]. We eventually concluded that those sorts of interactions would be such enormous edge cases that we figured it was a &quot;what works best for the table/story&quot; situation, but it is very interesting to hear that they were originally envisioned as attuned to draugr...<br /> <br /> Also, the Risen Beast is definitely my group's favorite thing from the book, so I'm excited to hear more about its development!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For what my perspective is worth, here is my input.<br /> <br /> Draugrs: As you can see by the mention of the draugr-hunting sheriff in the intro and also another reference in the Rumor section, draugr are meant to be open books to the Daimonion. Mechanically, Beast Whisperers should always benefit from the additional Auspex question and [REDACTED] when targeting draugr. Whether Therian Psychoanalysis should apply is a lot murkier, especially because of the specific mechanics referenced. Technically, as per 1e's <b>Night Horrors: Wicked Dead</b>, draugr are <i>not</i> in a state of &quot;permanent frenzy&quot; or somesuch, so you would expect that they could still be calmed down to some degree. I would consider a spin-off Merit for variants directly related to handling draugrs. Could this include an effect that gives a chance to pull back a draugr to Humanity 1? <i>Maybe</i>.<br /> <br /> Passengers: You could spin it in two entirely different directions that could both make sense.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The one is that reading a Kindred with Passenger is actually <i>easier</i> as the Passenger communicates their desires much more easily understandable. This could even include Daimonion being able to directly converse with the Passenger (perhaps based on a Merit or Devotion) on some level for much more clear information. The Passenger, in turn, should have some means of proactively taking advantage of the bloodline's Bane to recruit accomplices. Such contact should leave the Counselor more likely to develop a Passenger of her own.</li> <li>The Passenger confuses matters. Imagine someone being forced into therapy or only going half-heartedly. Such patients may have a part in themselves that actively sabotages any chance of progress. In Kindred, <i>that's</i> the Passenger. The Passenger is jealous and would not give up its unique position of trust it has with its host to an outsider. The Counselor may still be able to tell that a Passenger is present quite quickly by the resistance they face. In that case their gift may simply not work at all or be turned against them with intentional misinformation (always a fun game, figuring out when the habitual liar is telling the truth). Those Daimonion that lean harder into the therapist angle may actually consider suppressing the Passenger a duty to aid the &quot;host&quot; in improving their Requiem.</li> </ol>Of course, both could be true based on the individual involved!<br /> <br /> <br /> And bonus: Society of the Accord<br /> As Yossarian has already implied, making special mechanics for members of a single bloodline in a minor covenant is generally a bridge too far, but the Daimonion and Society are an obvious fit. I would encourage Players and Storytellers to work in at least some specific (Merit-based?) advantages for Counselors in the Society. I would also like to point to the Curse of Attunement for having interesting implications for Dialogs and very unique negotiations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T03:14:21-07:00","id":1480820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480730#post1480730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe one interesting little info with the Daimonion is that &amp;quot;vampire psychotherapist/analysist&amp;quot; was not the idea right from the start. I originally wanted to do a bloodline that has some special attunement and understanding for draugrs, but during the initial brainstorming it quickly became clear that it was too nich\u00e9 of a concept, so I broadened that to a more general &amp;quot;Beast whisperer&amp;quot; archetype, which then quickly turned into what we have now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not even a fan of Requiem's focus on bloodlines - at all - but here you've taken the core idea of the Therion bloodline from 1st Edition's book on Belial's Brood (counselors who work dark magic to keep frenzy-prone vampires lucid and functional) and turned it into something better developed, free of the juvenile sacrilege baggage, and acceptable in &quot;polite&quot; vampiric society, and it's too damn clever for me to fail to commend you. That's a really impressive bloodline design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T10:01:06-07:00","id":1480842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1480820#post1480820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not even a fan of Requiem's focus on bloodlines - at all - but here you've taken the core idea of the Therion bloodline from 1st Edition's book on Belial's Brood (counselors who work dark magic to keep frenzy-prone vampires lucid and functional) and turned it into something better developed, free of the juvenile sacrilege baggage, and acceptable in &quot;polite&quot; vampiric society, and it's too damn clever for me to fail to commend you. That's a really impressive bloodline design.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to derail the thread, but I would like to give you a suggestion since you say you don't like bloodlines. Of course that makes a decent chunk of Requiem material useless to you, but you can still get a lot of mileage out of bloodlines by transforming them from whole families into individual weird elders. Enrich the strangeness of your setting and use all the mechanics that they offer, without making it seem to the players that being one of these weirdos is normal, common or expected. On the side of Merits and Devotions, often enough, just minor fiddling makes them appropriate to other Kindred. This would be doubly true in a setting without bloodlines where you don't have to keep them exclusive to one line for the <b>MY TREASURE</b> factor.<br /> <br /> And thank you very much for the compliment!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T17:16:01-07:00","id":1480895,"title":"","content":"Alrighty, let's get into some of the antagonists/allies: First up, the Brides of Dracula.<br /> <br /> I actually don't have much to comment on here, apart from the Brides are awesome and I'm really pleased how our 2E version turned out. They're not <i>too </i>different from their original incarnation, but now they have significantly more mechanical weight, and the doomsday prepper aspect gives them a little more focus (though it's a detail you can emphasize to any degree you see fit). We also couldn't resist the chance to update Count F***ing Dracula's stats. The Count also hasn't changed much, though he's learned a couple new tricks over the years.<br /> <br /> We <i>also </i>couldn't resist getting a quick update of the Bruja in there, since they feature quite a bit in the Brides' backstory. Plus one of the other authors thought up the perfect tagline for them, so we pretty much had to include them by law.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, let's continue with our other covenant: The Society of the Accord<br /> <br /> <b>The Brides of Dracula: The Vanguard</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Fuck you.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>You want to join the Brides of Dracula because</b><br /> <br /> You know might makes right. You were a biker or rally racer in life and want to keep burning rubber in death. You\u2019d rather learn things on your own terms than have someone tell you. You\u2019re not interested in hiding from your prey. You believe in individualism but you\u2019re still desperate for a family.<br /> <br /> <b>The big picture</b><br /> <br /> Vampires, superior to the mortal flock they\u2019re sired from, are predators at heart. There\u2019s no religious or spiritual significance to a sentiment like that: It\u2019s a statement of fact. Kindred are strong, so they hunt humans. They take what they want from the kine and move on. How insignificant is a mortal compared to a lone Lick, even aside from the powers granted by the Blood? Why bother hiding from the herd at all? Sure, it\u2019s good not to leave any witnesses, but that also means icing every motherfucker you even think saw you gnawing on some punk and then leaving them all rotting in a ditch. Some predators hunt in the shadows their whole existence, stepping into the light only when they\u2019re sure they\u2019ll never, ever be caught.<br /> <br /> The Brides of Dracula call these vampires \u201cbitches.\u201d<br /> <br /> Part gang, part cult, part Mongol horde, the Brides are the All Night Society\u2019s only officially chartered motorcycle club. More than that, they\u2019re an army, but they don\u2019t fight at anyone\u2019s behest. Their founder takes a hands-off approach to his band of wild monsters. Nor do the Brides fight for any ideals, or some vague political endpoint. Laws, decency, and even the Traditions are, at best, \u201cguidelines,\u201d or, at worst, contrary to the pursuit of whatever the hell a Fury wants. The strong rise above the weak, and the weak test themselves until they\u2019re strong or dead. Or both.<br /> <br /> Why the obsession with personal strength? Ask the Count. Count Dracula, son of the Impaler. Count Fucking Dracula, the meanest, toughest son of a bitch in the Danse Macabre. See, the Count has done his work. He\u2019s read the tea leaves and applied his book learning, looked into the future and found it wanting. One night soon, Kindred won\u2019t be able to deny what they are to the world, and that\u2019s a world that\u2019ll hunt down every last bloodsucker under the gleaming eye of the sun. For the vast volume of secrets and lies that keep the All Night Society safe, they\u2019re still fragile things, and in an age of social media, smartphones, and increasingly deadly weapons, a time will come when there\u2019s no more hiding. Humans already know vampires are real, but once they figure out how to pick them out of a crowd, it\u2019ll be apocalyptic, and the Brides are the Count\u2019s Vanguard against the coming storm.<br /> <br /> The Furies thrive in a culture of war against everyone and everything. Sooner or later, something\u2019s going to cast a painful light upon the Kindred, and they aren\u2019t going to be caught unawares. Some chapters are doomsday preppers, building secret fortresses where they\u2019ll party as the walls tumble down. Others are quasi-religious, always moving judgment day down the calendar whenever a prophecy doesn\u2019t deliver. Armageddon is always looming, but no one wearing a cut really gives a fuck what form it takes. The Brides will survive the end and march into the uncertainty of eternity. Till then, and even after, they\u2019re going to ride like there\u2019s no tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> Every Bride worth her colors knows it all starts with one man: Count Fucking Dracula. First among Brides, the Count ain\u2019t some possessive asshole, but his reputation does precede him. On a midsummer night in 1995, that reputation led Ken Salk \u2014 the boss of a mickey mouse crew called the Desert Raiders \u2014 to track down the Count after a half-dozen drug sales were disrupted by a crazy, hulking nightmare in a leather trench coat. But Salk was only human, and that night was the last that\u2019d be true. Apparently, the Count saw something in the scrawny little fucker, so the Big D Embraced him. Thus, the first Bride was deflowered. Soon, other Kindred followed in Ken\u2019s wake, a tide of Licks brave enough to stand in the Count\u2019s seven-foot-seven shadow. They organized, the strong ripped away from the weak and the sharks pulled from the waves, and the Count began to build his army.<br /> <br /> Or that\u2019s the word we hear from the Mother Chapter. Sure, everyone claims they\u2019ve met the Count, but he\u2019s like a cryptid: You always just miss him no matter how hard you look. Everyone has an opinion on where he\u2019s currently hiding and what he really wants. If he needs to send down orders, they\u2019re always through the Mother Chapter, but orders are so rare that no one bats an eye about never hearing from the Count directly.<br /> <br /> Once Salk remade his gang, they began roaming the continental US looking for recruits. They\u2019d \u201cpatch\u201d the baddest motherfuckers in each town they rode through, leaving them behind to spread the word. These badasses, in turn, made more badasses, and soon, there were chapters all across North America, reaching from Mexico to the long highways of Canada. Expansion into the former set off our first and (thus far) only turf war. The Bruja bloodline and their biker thralls had deep roots all over the Southwest, so the Mother Chapter ordered a hostile takeover. That provided us the bloodline\u2019s smuggling routes, drug chemists, hogs, and most of its membership, as well as a more intimate understanding of Kindred society. Now we had everything we\u2019d needed to prepare for the tribulation ahead.<br /> <br /> Tonight, we wait for the war to come, remaking ourselves into an army that can survive without supervision, an army that can be ready for anything and everything humanity might throw at us. The All Night Society is changing, and not for the better. The beasts of the dark have grown too obsessed with politics, hunting merely to survive. The Count wouldn\u2019t abide that \u2014 and neither should you.<br /> <br /> <b>Our practices</b><br /> <br /> We\u2019re organized into chapters overseen by Salk and his childer in the Mother Chapter. We ain\u2019t no democracy, and that means you follow the rules \u2014 all of them. There are a lot, but most treat on how to deal with civvies and how to properly contaminate any potential crime scenes you happen to make whilst minding your own goddamn business. You might also be called to war, driving a state or two over to fuck up a domain, protect your sister chapters, or just fire bomb some rich prick\u2019s haven.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, you wear your cut, and until you meet the Final Death, you don\u2019t take it off. You patch it with your colors: the skull to show you\u2019re a Bride, logos for your local chapter, and then all the flair you earn for being a badass. Crash Elysium? That\u2019s a patch. Wipe out a police station on your lonesome? That\u2019s a patch. Think up something so awful we ain\u2019t got a patch for it? That\u2019s a fucking patch. Collect them all, you creepy bastard. \u2019Course, the baddest of them all are those who wear the Red Tooth. You only get that for eating a soul, and you\u2019ve not seen a riot till you witness a chapter celebrating some newbie popping her cherry.<br /> <br /> Our most important practice is the rally. A rally is food, folks, and fun, a place we can shoot the shit or plan the next big kill. Sometimes, we put on our own events, drawing Licks from miles around to take in the bloodshed, but mostly, these are private affairs, or ways for chapters to settle scores on an even playing field. Otherwise, we take to the mortal circuit, preying on drunk Hell\u2019s Angels as they cheer us on. Oh yeah, they know all about us. Nothing draws a crowd like the Brides of Dracula. Most don\u2019t take us for actual vampires, but we play up the spooky shit for the crowd. Bonus points if the Masquerade police show up and you run over some Invictus dirtbag with your ride (you better believe that\u2019s a patch).<br /> <br /> But for all the rules, all the rallies, all the fighting, the most important thing is freedom. If you aren\u2019t being called on to do something by your chapter president, or someone higher up on the food chain, you can do whatever the fuck you like. Usually that means getting involved with drugs, or maybe an extortion racket or two \u2014 this is a gang, after all. Any money you earn is yours to keep, save for a small wealth tax when the Mother Chapter needs to do some fundraising. But hey, if you\u2019re running low, there are other ways to contribute. The expectation, of course, is that you\u2019re gonna share with your crew the same way you\u2019d share with a brother or a sister \u2014 or a sibling, if you like (the Count don\u2019t care what\u2019s in your pants). You know how to fix up bikes? Be a good Bride and help out changing oil and fixing gearshifts. You know how to cook? Great \u2014 whip up the best damn meth in the state and make the whole chapter filthy rich.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019ve got a cut, you\u2019re your own Bride, just like the Count. A real one-percenter type. You put in the work when you\u2019re asked, and you work hard. CEO mindset. Once that\u2019s done, no one\u2019s gonna bat an eye if you play so hard you leave a few bodies in your wake. You didn\u2019t just earn it: You\u2019re entitled to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T16:39:02-07:00","id":1481023,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's have a look at the Society of the Accord!<br /> <br /> As I've said elsewhere, this clan book series has also been a stealth update of various bits and bobs from <b>The Danse Macabre</b>, which, for my money, is one of the best supplements White Wolf ever put out for a vampire-related TTRPG. Apart from things like banes (and gargoyles, who we'll get to soon), my major focus has been to give the covenants from that book a 2E polish. I'd like to go through all of those factions eventually (including the third-tier versions of the big five), but that's a discussion for another day!<br /> <br /> The Society of the Accord is a cult/self-help group that believes it's better to come to an understanding with their Beasts rather than outright repressing them. That concept hasn't changed too much from the original presentation, but we did significantly alter their mechanical benefit: The Treaties. Originally, Treaties were Coils of the Dragon-like Disciplines, and while that was by no means a bad way of representing their abilities, we had a few reasons for wanting to scrap that system. For one, we've kinda done &quot;not-Coil&quot; powers a <i>lot </i>in this series, and while that doesn't necessarily preclude doing more (and indeed, you'll see some in <b>Bloodlines: The Ageless</b>), I wanted to see if there were better ways to accomplish the thematic goals of the concept using different mechanics. We also felt that, by their nature, &quot;treaties&quot; aren't really permanent things you just get to have. A Coil is a permanent alteration of your Curse, but a Treaty is a contract with terms and responsibilities.<br /> <br /> To that end, the author took a page from the Carthians and the Invictus, using a sort of &quot;Oaths meets Laws&quot; structure. Treaties are an agreement between a vampire and her Beast, but they're also only accomplished through collective action; i.e., Dialogs, the bloody, dangerous rites Hellions conduct to satisfy their side of the bargain with the Beast.<br /> <br /> The Accord fit very well with a Gangrel book, not only because of the obvious thematic connection, but also because they're a chance to explore a different side of the clan. Not all Hellions are Savages, of course, but those who do join the covenant represent a more intellectual side of their lineage while still being ridiculously bloody.<br /> <br /> Without further ado, here's the Society of the Accord. I think I'll probably take Saturday off again, but I should be back on Sunday with a ghoul family!<br /> <br /> <b>The Society of the Accord: The Hellions</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You're just in time for your session! Start running.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>You want to join the Society of the Accord because</b><br /> <br /> You\u2019re tired of fighting the Beast. You want to apply modern psychology to the Kindred condition. You chafe against the Traditions. You\u2019re not ashamed of being a monster.<br /> <br /> <b>The big picture</b><br /> <br /> Every vampire suffers from the Beast\u2019s urgings. Indeed, traditional wisdom within the All Night Society states that it must be resisted and denied at every turn. Pity the poor predator burdened by her instincts: Woe is the restless dead, cursed with immortality and chained to a monster. It\u2019s enough to make you lie recumbent in your haven with the curtains open.<br /> <br /> Isn\u2019t that just so insufferably <i>Victorian</i>? The world has moved beyond such moral self-flagellation. There\u2019s so much more now that we understand about the human condition, and we know wallowing in misery just drives you deeper into it. And, being once human, these new ideas of psychology almost certainly apply to the Kindred. These are foundational principles for the Society of the Accord, to open a dialog between the Man and the Other. Beast is such a sinister name for a constant companion \u2014 and do you really want to alienate such a valuable ally?<br /> <br /> It sounds noble enough on paper, but there\u2019s a certain old adage about what you pave the road to Hell with. The Hellions do have means to keep the Beast under control, to some extent, but they do so through brutal games of bloodshed and dominance. They drape themselves in layers of symbolism and ritual to hide their cruelty, but there are only so many ways you can dress up chasing around members of your covenant until they fear for their Requiems, ending with an orgy of frenzy on both sides of the equation.<br /> <br /> Between the violence they bring in their wake and their philosophy sharing more than a few similarities with, oh, say, Belial\u2019s Brood, the Psychonauts prefer to keep their practices secret. This, so far, has kept the Society of the Accord from ever growing beyond an underground counterculture. Lost neonates and disaffected ancillae, unhappy with the stifling hierarchies and expectations of the larger covenants, are the most likely to join, often scouted out by senior members when their dissatisfaction becomes clear. Elders are rare, as Hellions tend to have a short shelf life. Accidents happen, after all. A careless cleanup draws negative attention from the Prince, or maybe the Society is finally considered more trouble than they\u2019re worth. That, and massive murder rate spikes invariably result in a few mortals with a grudge.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, if you ask a Hellion, it\u2019s better to have a happy-but-short death than a long, uncomfortable immortality. The Society has a reputation for relentless hedonism, and that\u2019s not unearned, but they\u2019re not without sense, and those who buy into the rumors of being one step away from draugr would be surprised by the academic bent their teachings take. Then again, so much of the Kindred condition is monstrosity draped in pretty language and posturing at humanity. They\u2019re just taking a different route.<br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> A desire to escape the negative effects of the Beast has existed for as long as the Kindred. Rumors have circulated for centuries of vampires who manage to do this, though substantive proof has been thin on the ground, usually explained away as the saintly vampire being a hermit. This state of enlightenment has been referred to as \u201cGolconda\u201d in modern times, though it\u2019s rejected by most covenants as idealistic at best and dangerous at worst.<br /> <br /> The Society of the Accord is perhaps the longest-lasting Golconda cult \u2014 not that we use the word <i>cult</i>. That\u2019s a loaded term. Still, by Kindred standards, our Society is young. We started as small, isolated secret societies with wildly varying practices. Few left any records, but there were always just enough left in the ashes to spark further interest in Golconda. The Apostles of the Destroying Angels were the first group to commit their ideas to writing, but their theory that the Beast was an angel of death tethered to a vampire\u2019s corpse proved\u2026 unpopular with the Sanctified; the idea that sufficient prayer and carefully applied violence could appease the angel even less so. Yet, while the Church might\u2019ve been able to put the Apostles\u2019 havens to the torch, their treatises survived. Now their practice of letting the Beast speak through frenzy is our own, though trying to say it\u2019s some divinely sent power, or that whatever it kills deserves it, is a superstition best left in the past. Or at least, don\u2019t give it too much credit.<br /> <br /> Later, the Brotherhood of Enlightened Predation, inspired by their mortal contemporaries in London hellfire clubs, started as a way for Kindred gentry to have just a few moments of wild indulgence after the first few decades of death got dull. One infamous and particularly wild night left the Brotherhood with several newly risen revenants in their care, and while the experiments conducted on these pseudo-vampires did prove useful in furthering an understanding of the role of hunger in controlling the Beast, the secondary result of keeping around abused, ravenous monsters without proper safety precautions was entirely predictable. However, there were enough survivors who kept an interest in the academic study of the vampiric psyche to form the earliest version of what we now call the Society of the Accord.<br /> <br /> These nights, the Hellions have learned from their predecessors and remain sparse. The most optimistic of us believed the Internet might give us a shot in the arm and provide an easier way to spread our teachings, but this hasn\u2019t panned out over the past thirty years, and it seems unlikely to bear fruit in the future. The All Night Society is loath to change, and a group that flies against the Traditions as much as we do isn\u2019t exactly predisposed to gaining any real footholds.<br /> <br /> Tonight, we\u2019ve begun to adopt the trappings of psychoanalysis and self-help as a framing device for our practices. It\u2019s a happy coincidence that cognitive behavioral therapy strongly resembles the reasoning behind our Dialogs, though a human therapy session would typically have less murder involved \u2014 how dull!<br /> <br /> <b>Our practices</b><br /> <br /> All vampires have an inner impulse that drives them from Humanity. You can frame it as a metaphor, and we certainly do try to personify it (for better or worse), but its existence is a practical reality whether you like it or not. That \u201csomething\u201d takes over in times of heightened emotions, tearing away the fa\u00e7ade of the Man to leave the monster underneath. What sets the Society of the Accord apart from other Kindred is that we believe we can reason with that monster.<br /> <br /> Hellions keep a fragile peace with the Beast through a regimen of reward and punishment. Some nights, we gather together for a feeding frenzy, or force ourselves to face what the Other fears most, whether that be fire or emotional agony. Sometimes we just hunt each other to bring our instincts to the forefront. Regardless of the means, it\u2019s always a night to remember, if only for the destruction it leaves behind. These occasions are called \u201cDialogs,\u201d and outsiders are rarely invited, if only because such events tend to provide excellent blackmail material.<br /> <br /> Gatherings of Hellions are called Voleries, and for many, the Volery replaces the coterie as a primary social unit. Within the Volery, there are several positions that fully initiated members can work within, though these are not static. The Navigator is in charge of a night\u2019s Dialog, the Advocate gives voice to the participants\u2019 Beasts, and the Cleaner works to keep the Masquerade in place in the typically violent aftermath.<br /> <br /> One reason we prefer to stick together is that the idea of ceding ground to the Beast goes against what most covenants teach. The problem is, doing so produces results. Ask a Hellion and they\u2019ll say the traditional treatment of the Beast gets the \u201cstick\u201d part of the equation right by denying what it wants \u2014 but if you beat an animal enough, it only obeys out of fear. And once that fear is gone, you\u2019ll live just long enough to regret it.<br /> <br /> Dialogs, however, provide the carrot. The Beast wants blood, a chance to show its dominance, or to be let off its leash for a few moments. More often than not, this involves casualties, and those casualties aren\u2019t always human. Usually, we let prospective members who\u2019ve earned our trust have just a small taste of what\u2019s to come by accompanying us on a hunt. The first taste is free, no questions asked, and most end up coming back again. Otherwise, we put newcomers through a gauntlet where senior members are whipped into frenzy, with the potential initiate being hunted until they, too, fall to the Other. We even provide medical aid for all involved parties afterward. We might be monsters, but we\u2019re civilized ones.<br /> <br /> Once you\u2019ve survived that, the sky\u2019s the limit. Everyone\u2019s path to forming a relationship with their Beast is a bit different, but we have a few favorites. Starvation brings the Beast to the forefront, but just to make sure you don\u2019t try to break your fast too early, we provide a saferoom. The key is ours, though, not yours, and the locks are for your own safety. Hey, you\u2019ll get out eventually. Some nights, we wait for the dawn outside a haven to see whoever can stand the sunlight the longest before fleeing to safety. The winner gets the first taste of blood on the next hunt; the loser gets to be the one who tries to break in through barred doors.<br /> <br /> But the hunts are really the main draw. You, a few other members of the Volery, a gathering of humans, no witnesses, and no survivors. It\u2019s always worth the wait. Ultimately, the Man must learn that the Beast is his companion, one that cannot be controlled or ignored. The desire to stand over a pile of flesh that used to be a person while licking the blood from your fangs isn\u2019t something to be ashamed of. There\u2019s nothing wrong with wanting to take some harpy\u2019s head off his shoulders after the way he insulted you last year \u2014 everyone knows he\u2019s a prick and would deserve it. Those impulses to kill and dominate are just part of being a vampire, and the harder you try to fight them, the worse the Other will be when it finally gets free. With us, you get to choose the time and place to do these things. Better yet, you get to do it with backup. Until then, we\u2019ll hold some space for you to listen to all of those nasty little impulses you\u2019ve been trying to hold back.<br /> <br /> The end result of a Dialog is a Treaty \u2014 the Accord \u2014 where the Man and the Other reach an understanding. It\u2019s not a friendship by any means; it\u2019s more akin to a relationship between a falconer and her bird. The bird has no real love for this person, but it understands that following orders means its needs will be fulfilled, so it doesn\u2019t lash out and harm its master. Conversely, the falconer must understand the fragility of this relationship and not test its limits. In the end, there\u2019s peace.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s happy enough, and that\u2019s what matters. Can you really hope for anything more?<br /> <br /> <b>Treaties</b><br /> <br /> The pinnacles of a Hellion\u2019s meditative work are <i>Treaties</i>, abilities that alter her relationship with the Other and its needs: It becomes more patient, less likely to frenzy, and more flexible in the face of threats. While frenzy is the most readily obvious of the Beast\u2019s manifestations, Treaties rarely empower its use. Rather, the Society of the Accord allows for a greater finesse over what the Beast can do.<br /> <br /> Only a vampire with Status in the Society of the Accord can purchase these Merits, and he must prove his commitment if he wants to gain the most potent of them. To learn any given Treaty, a vampire must have a Status equal to at least one less than a Treaty\u2019s rating, to a minimum of one dot. For example, a character with three dots of Hellion Status can purchase 1\u20134-dot Treaties, but he cannot purchase any 5-dot ones. He must also participate in an appropriate Dialog (below).<br /> <br /> <b>Dialogs</b><br /> <br /> Keeping up with your Treaties takes work, and to remain in good standing with the Other, a Hellion must participate in Dialogs.<br /> <br /> There are three classes of Dialog recognized by the Hellions, each representing a different aspect of the Beast: Anger, Fear, and Need. Each Treaty is keyed to a different Dialog type. The Accord describes Dialogs in dualistic terms, with each pole representing an \u201cargument\u201d for humanity or bestiality. A Hellion is said to be Humane, for example, if she refrains from draining a victim to death, whereas she\u2019s Bestial if she does the opposite. These Dialogs are an ongoing rapport between the Man and the Other.<br /> <br /> Participation in the appropriate Dialog preserves any corresponding Treaties for one lunar month, and these rituals are never performed alone. As such, at least three Hellions must be involved with a Dialog for it to be considered successful; typically, this involves a Navigator, an Advocate, and a Cleaner, but smaller Voleries can muddle through without these specialized roles.<br /> <br /> A Dialog must employ at least one of the following elements of the appropriate type. Characters must contribute as many elements as Treaty types they have, or else those they neglect are not considered to be renewed. As such, Psychonauts tend to focus on one Treaty type over the others, though jacks-of-all-trades aren\u2019t unheard of.<br /> <br /> <b>Dialogs of Anger</b><br /> <br /> Participating in a collective hunt. Allowing a Volery member to taunt or humiliate you to the point of frenzy. Engaging in combat with another member until inflicting at least three points of lethal damage to each other.<br /> <br /> <b>Dialogs of Fear</b><br /> <br /> Facing exposure to a bane. Allowing multiple Volery members to lash out at you. Playing the part of prey during a mock hunt.<br /> <br /> <b>Dialogs of Need</b><br /> <br /> Cornering a group of humans and feeding to excess. Locking yourself in a room and avoiding feeding until starving. Facing frenzy due to hunger. Spending a night communing with a burrow of revenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T14:14:47-07:00","id":1481199,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's dig into some ghoul families.<br /> <br /> One minor goal I've had with ghoul families has been to update all the First Edition clan ones, but, to my knowledge, there aren't any Gangrel ghoul families in <b>Requiem 1E</b>, even in the original <b>Ghouls </b>sourcebook. The only one that comes close is the Alleymen, who, in addition to being Ventrue despite REALLY feeling like Gangrel, were updated as a <i>kind </i>of ghoul in <b>Half-Damned</b>. In some alternate reality, had they not been covered already, I might have nicked them off the Lords, but that's neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> Which is a long way of saying that the three ghoul families who appear in <b>Wild Hunt </b>are wholly original creations. Let's begin with the <b>Midnight Wolves</b>.<br /> <br /> So, one thing I particularly like about ghoul families in Second Edition (both in the core and <b>Half-Damned</b>) is that they have a lot more agency. In First Edition, they were too often hapless victims with little say in their lot in life, and I think 2E makes them <i>far </i>more viable as protagonist characters, along with ghouls in general. In that context, a family like the Midnight Wolves was a natural next step.<br /> <br /> The Mad Dogs act as bounty hunters cum protection racketeers for the All Night Society, riding roughshod as modern-night cowboys. That's a pretty strong concept, and, as such, this family probably had the least amount of ink spilled on it through development. They originally were a bit too much like the Brides of Dracula, though, so we gave that mercenary aspect more emphasis, which provided them a more distinct niche. I also added their special Merit late in development, because I forgot how cool Taste of the Wild is; those ghoul Merits in the core are all great in general. That was inspired by the third sample character in the write-up, who's the first non-human member of a ghoul family we've done. I absolutely loved that idea, and the author injected a lot of pathos into it. It's also just a great plot hook in general.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, I'll be back with the Champions of the <b>Neo-American Wrestling Alliance</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Midnight Wolves: The ones with something to prove<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You\u2019re a funny guy. Tell me another after I feed you your fangs.&quot;</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>Your motorcycle growls like a wild animal as the highway disappears beneath you toward a blood-red horizon. A road sign flashes through your periphery; the bar\u2019s coming up. You kick the gearshift and cruise on in to rest your ride along with a dozen others parked outside. You\u2019re hungry, but business comes first.<br /> <br /> The door creaks open and a dozen sets of eyes turn to regard you. The bartender doesn\u2019t look up. She knows better than to get involved. This isn\u2019t the first time she\u2019s seen you, and besides, she knows you\u2019re good to cover the damage.<br /> <br /> Your black, steel-toed boots drum a sluggish beat against the dirty tile floor. You approach the biggest, meanest-looking motherfucker in the bar, the one with a price on his head in three domains.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere are two ways this can go down: quick or fun,\u201d you say.<br /> <br /> The biggest, meanest-looking motherfucker laughs, fangs flashing in the dull neon of old beer signs. The whole table stands, and they surround you. Someone glasses you from behind and you stagger, shards biting into your scalp. You reach a hand up and it comes away slick with red. Adrenaline surges through you like a guitar riff, and you smile.<br /> Looks like you get to eat after all.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> Typically, the more established a ghoul family is, the longer it\u2019s been around. Many Kindred respect ghouls as members of the All Night Society \u2014 not necessarily as members of equal rank, but even the most prestigious families have to build connections and infrastructure to become valuable assets to their regnants. The Midnight Wolves stand in sharp contrast.<br /> <br /> In the early-1800s, way out in what\u2019s now Colorado, a Savage called Mary Quick fancied herself an outlaw. This wasn\u2019t especially common among the dead, as daylight tended to complicate matters, but Mary wasn\u2019t easily deterred. She found herself a posse of smalltime cattle rustlers led by a dude named Jack Beaumont. Jack was smart enough to recognize a good offer when it sauntered into camp and punched him in the gut, and that\u2019s how Mary found her first Midnight Wolves.<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t take long for them to become public enemies on the frontier, less for their actual robberies and more for what they did to anyone who tried to bring them to justice. But after a few years of building their reputation, Jack and his boys started to feel restless. The power Mary gave them was like nothing they could\u2019ve imagined, but it was only a taste. The frontier was growing smaller every day, and Kindred influence crept ever westward along with it. It wasn\u2019t hard to find vampires who were interested in some established muscle who could take care of business at high noon, and that\u2019s how the Mad Dogs pushed into Nevada and California.<br /> <br /> As for Mary? Jack always claimed she got tired of the outlaw life, but no one\u2019s heard from her since around the Gold Rush. Still, her legacy lives on in a gang of Bloodhounds, ones who\u2019ll still do just about anything to prove themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> The Midnight Wolves are the last surviving vestige of the American frontier, cowboys and killers who won\u2019t accept the quiet lives of city folk. Sure, they traded in their horses and six-shooters for Harleys and sawed-offs, but the thirst for violence remains. Still, violence in and of itself is usually only a means to an end, and the Bloodhounds have repurposed yet another aspect of their frontier past: bounty hunting. This provides them just enough cover for all the hellraising that actually interests them. Midnight Wolves use their ability to operate over daylight hours to track and corner Kindred outlaws, whether those who pissed off the authorities or just those Licks who have high-roller enemies. If you\u2019ve got enough cash and Vitae, you can buy a Bloodhound.<br /> <br /> Wolf gangs are common all across the Pacific Coast and American Southwest, most of which are based out of dive bars, mob casinos, and other nexuses of human misery. There aren\u2019t many Midnight Wolves who care to waste their time actually running a business, but fortunately for them, plenty of humans are willing to pay for protection, or Kindred who'll tolerate their rowdiness if it means having reliable goons to handle their enemies.<br /> <br /> Other than whichever dead man\u2019s paying for them tonight, their command structure is non-existent; worrying about seniority is for First Estate pencil necks, and money doesn\u2019t count for much if you aren\u2019t strong enough to keep it.<br /> <br /> Contrary to popular belief, however, Mad Dogs aren\u2019t stupid, and they don\u2019t have a death wish. Few among their number go around antagonizing the entire All Night Society, and the ones who do invariably meet violent and lonely ends. Brass knuckles can only do so much against blood sorcery or Protean claws. That\u2019s why they hunt in packs, and that\u2019s also why they keep their noses clean, at least when it comes to the Danse Macabre.<br /> <br /> But Midnight Wolves who\u2019ve been around for a while all too often lose their headstrong bravado. While their family is defined by the drive to prove itself, those jaded few are the ones who\u2019ve realized exactly where they fit in the world. There\u2019s a reason that the rest of the cowboys died out.<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Bloodhounds, Mad Dogs (derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Touchstone: </b>A gang\u2019s leader is treated as its Touchstone.<br /> <br /> <b>Benefit:</b> Midnight Wolves never back down, not even in a hopeless fight. After taking lethal damage in a scene, a Bloodhound\u2019s unarmed attacks deal +0 lethal damage instead of bashing for the remainder of the scene, including to vampires. In addition, Bloodhounds gain the Taste of the Wild Merit (<b>Vampire</b>, p. 298) for free at character creation.<br /> Drawback: Midnight Wolves never back down, not even in a pointless fight. After taking lethal damage in a scene, a Bloodhound must spend a Vitae to exit the scene non-violently or to retreat from a fight before it ends. Otherwise, she gains the Broken Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>[REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes:</b><ul><li><b>Daeva: </b>Look, but don\u2019t touch. Especially if you don\u2019t have the cash.</li> <li><b>Gangrel: </b>We\u2019ll try to kill each other sometimes, but hey, that\u2019s family.</li> <li><b>Mekhet: </b>Rodents.</li> <li><b>Nosferatu: </b>Outsiders, like us.</li> <li><b>Ventrue: </b>Never trust anybody who talks that much.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T15:27:30-07:00","id":1481265,"title":"","content":"A good Monday to you all. Time for another ghoul family: The <b>Neo-American Wrestling Alliance</b> (henceforth, <b>NAWA</b>)!<br /> <br /> I don't have much to say here, other than to note that this was an exceptionally fun concept. There was a bit of retooling from the initial drafts, mostly in regard to how they interact with the All Night Society, but I'm really happy with how it all shook out. I particularly like that this is a ghoul family that applies its gifts of the Blood to more (kind of) practical ends, using their high durability as ghouls to perform sick stunts that would more or less kill mortal wrestlers. And if the local Kindred get a nice, rowdy crowd to sup upon? So much the better.<br /> <br /> I also want to call out the illustration of this family as being one of my favourites in the book (linked on the STV product paged). Luchadores and vampires go together like a metaphor for things that go well together.<br /> <br /> So, here are the NAWA, and tomorrow I'll be back with the <b>Redwater Bay Police</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>NAWA: The ones you cheer for<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Ever cut loose for a crowd of thousands? No feeling like it.&quot;</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>Neon lights and LED screens fill the stadium with contrasting electric songs, and the rumble of the crowd that\u2019s swelling in the bleachers is choral accompaniment \u2014 music to your ears.<br /> <br /> You never feel more alive than on fight night. All those people chanting your name as you ricochet someone\u2019s face off the turnstile? There\u2019s no other high that can compare. Not from before your first taste, or after.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you still think back to the life you left behind, the one with the bank job you hated and the fianc\u00e9 who was screwing his way through the apartment building. Then your intro music comes on and the stadium roars. You wonder if gladiators ever felt this good, and you make a note to ask the boss about it later. After all, the boss used to be one.<br /> <br /> But right now, your public awaits.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> Maxine Donahue founded the Neo-American Wrestling Alliance for one purpose: to make modern gladiators for a modern world. If you catch her in a good mood, she\u2019ll regale you with stories of her time back in the arena; just don\u2019t make the mistake of asking her about anything else from back then, or her good mood will cease and your lifespan will quickly follow.<br /> <br /> These nights, there aren\u2019t many Kindred around who actually lived through the fall of Rome, and ghouls from back then are basically unheard of. \u201cMaxine Donahue\u201d isn\u2019t exactly a Latin name, and there are some vampires who think she\u2019s full of shit, but most of them are also smart enough not to say that to her face.<br /> <br /> But Maxine is the real deal. She was a Gallic slave in her old life, and some asshole thought it would be amusing to put a dull sword in her hands and watch a scrawny girl fight a real gladiator. No one was laughing when that scrawny girl ripped his throat out with her teeth. Even back then, she knew how to get the audience\u2019s attention.<br /> <br /> Among that audience was the Gangrel who would become her regnant, a vampire named Borso. Borso purchased her, taught her how to be a real champion of the ring, and then eventually sponsored her so she could really test her mettle. She didn\u2019t disappoint, and as the girl\u2019s star rose, Borso started to see her as more than just a simple asset. The story goes that he offered to Embrace her, but she turned him down for reasons she doesn\u2019t care to explain. She still accepted the gift of his Blood, and the moment she tasted it, she was truly born as the first Champion.<br /> <br /> At least, that\u2019s how she tells it. Embellishment is part of the job.<br /> <br /> The two of them fled the fall of Rome and traveled the world together. Every century or so she\u2019d adopt a new identity to fit the times and whichever culture they found themselves in. If she flourished in the ring, it was nothing compared to when she stepped out of it. With each passing decade she came more into her own, and everywhere they went, she\u2019d find a crowd that was happy to watch two people beat the shit out of each other. That\u2019s how their stable of Champions grew; she would look for the fighters who could hold their own while still putting on a show, then make them an offer. Eventually, their new family settled in America, a place that really knew how to appreciate violence. That\u2019s where she first learned of modern professional wrestling, the \u201cevolution\u201d of the gladiatorial fights of her old life, something that elevated arena combat to an art form. And with Vitae powering her Champions, it meant they could put on a show unlike any a human wrestling organization could ever hope to do. She would make superstars.<br /> <br /> Yet as Maxine grew brighter, Borso only seemed to fade deeper into the shadows. He\u2019s still around, at least as far as anyone knows, but it\u2019s been a hundred years since anyone\u2019s actually seen him. The way Maxine tells it, he just doesn\u2019t care to see anyone but her most nights, and no one is in a position to argue the point. It\u2019s a common joke among some Kindred that Maxine was the real vampire all along, and Borso was <i>her </i>ghoul. Other Kindred don\u2019t think it\u2019s much of a joke.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> The Neo-American Wrestling Alliance is one of the top promotions in the business. Many Kindred weren\u2019t too crazy about Maxine\u2019s scheme to broadcast her employees\u2019 death-defying abilities to a general audience, but hey, most professional wrestling outfits were already doing shit in the ring that should kill normal people. Besides, <i>everybody </i>knows wrestling is fake.<br /> <br /> That aside, even her most vocal critics have to admit they put on one hell of a show. It\u2019s no surprise that NAWA became an overnight sensation, especially with a little support from the shadows. Even vampires with no interest in wrestling can still benefit from a room full of rowdy, drunk humans. It\u2019s better still if all those humans have a built-in excuse not to question anything weird that they might notice (\u201cIs that guy drinking that chick\u2019s blood?! Great production values!\u201d). If a NAWA show is coming to town, chances are the local Kindred paid big for a buffet.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t misunderstand, though. Plenty of Licks love the show even more than the kine do, Gangrel especially. Even if the matches are staged to have a certain ending, that flying elbow off the top of the cage and the sound of a collarbone shattering is pretty fucking real. And a little Vitae will make sure you can see it all again the next night. The Blood\u2019s way better for your health than steroids, and you really don\u2019t have to worry about a stunt coordinator if you can just unbreak your neck.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s part of the problem. Some night soon, a point may come when the audience will start really seeing past the kayfabe. If that point does exist, Maxine seems fixated on finding it. If she succeeds, she\u2019ll finally find a fight she can\u2019t win for the first time in her very long life.<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Champions, Champs, Borso\u2019s Beasts (among themselves)<br /> <br /> <b>Touchstone:</b> Maxine Donahue, founder, CEO, and public face of the company. Sometimes she even gets in the ring, and for that, her Champs love her all the more.<br /> <br /> <b>Benefit:</b> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Drawing a crowd isn\u2019t always what it\u2019s cut up to be, especially if they start showing up at your apartment. Rolls to find or identify Champions enjoy a +2 modifier, which compounds with any dots of Fame she might have. Furthermore, at the beginning of a chapter, the Storyteller rolls a single die. If the result is a success, she can introduce an unexpected and dramatic complication for the Champion at any point during that chapter. For example, if the wrestler is attempting to move through a building without being noticed, he might run into one of his biggest fans who recognizes him on the spot. If he wants to get information at a bar, then maybe one of the other patrons decides to see how tough he really is. This complication should not constitute an immediate failure, but it should force the Champion to think on her feet.<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes:</b><ul><li><b>Daeva:</b> In this business, you\u2019ve gotta respect a good face.</li> <li><b>Gangrel:</b> The only ones who really know what it means to let go.</li> <li><b>Mekhet: </b>They help us draw a crowd; in return, they get a crowd to skulk in.</li> <li><b>Nosferatu: </b>Horror storylines are big right now.</li> <li><b>Ventrue:</b> Tough as hell, and damn do they know how to work an audience.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T15:41:25-07:00","id":1481268,"title":"","content":"Wrestling always seems to be that field where supernaturals blunge into mortal society, and I love the idea for that. <br /> <br /> Aaand now I know what to base my ideas of Wuxia martial arts clan ghoul families on if I ever exert myself to start typing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T21:04:25-07:00","id":1481275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481268#post1481268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrestling always seems to be that field where supernaturals blunge into mortal society, and I love the idea for that.<br /> <br /> Aaand now I know what to base my ideas of Wuxia martial arts clan ghoul families on if I ever exert myself to start typing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Surrealists get proven wrong at wrestlign matches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T21:25:57-07:00","id":1481276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481275#post1481275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surrealists get proven wrong at wrestlign matches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing wraps up a debate like a good ol\u2019 fisticuff.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, the God-Machin\u2014 I mean, YouTube\u2019s algorithms just started recommending to me the \u201cNanomachines, son!\u201d meme videos. Hmm\u2026 biomechanical Gangrel with nanotech Protean\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-17T11:29:11-07:00","id":1481308,"title":"","content":"Alright, final ghoul family today: the <b>Redwater Bay Police</b>.<br /> <br /> This is probably the most overtly antagonistic ghoul family we've done, and also the most specific to a particular setting. Among the NMD writers, I'm a bit notorious for kiboshing &quot;vampires secretly being behind real events&quot; story hooks (hate 'em!), but I <i>do </i>like story hooks where vampires are pushing their luck on the Masquerade in such a way that things will almost certainly go horribly wrong. The RBPD is a great example of that hook in action (as is the NAWA, come to think of it). We don't explicitly state the kind of trouble they'll be bringing down sooner or later, but I think we included a few good hooks on how to make it happen.<br /> <br /> Not too much to say about development. I had remembered there being bigger changes in development, but this was actually closer to the first draft than I recalled. The only big change was adding their Merit, which I actually think would make a good general benefit for certain kinds of Invictus ghouls.<br /> <br /> Now that we're through the ghouls, next I think I'm going to break tradition slightly and pull some stuff out of the Merits/Devotions/etc. chapter. We've got a lot of fun systems this time around. This will also give me an excuse to talk about what we did with the Red Surrender...<br /> <br /> <b>Redwater Bay Police: The ones who maintain order<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Alright, sir, start from the top. Tell me exactly what you think you saw.&quot;</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>It\u2019s a Tuesday night in the middle of July, and Redwater Bay is as peaceful as ever.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the kind of place where parents don\u2019t have to worry about what their kids are getting up to; the police keep the neighborhood safe, and they have the statistics to prove it.<br /> Redwater\u2019s got the lowest violent crime numbers in the state, and even vandalism is virtually unheard of. Of course, every so often, a family does up and move out of town without so much as a goodbye. But these things happen, and most folks have come to agree that it\u2019s perfectly normal.<br /> <br /> Yes, the police in that precinct really are a credit to their uniform. So why is it that anytime you see an officer, all the little hairs on the back of your neck stand on end? If they make eye contact, you feel an animal compulsion to run and hide, like a rabbit staring down a wolf. They\u2019ll smile, and you\u2019ll smile back, but all you can think of is a predator showing his fangs. It\u2019s probably nothing. Authority figures are always a little intimidating\u2026<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a Tuesday night in the middle of July, and Redwater Bay is as peaceful as ever. Just make sure the cops don\u2019t have a reason to knock on your door. </i><br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> While it\u2019s common practice for Kindred to enthrall powerful humans, typically, vampires won\u2019t go to the effort of juicing up just any public servant who\u2019s under their influence. It\u2019s just not a good investment. So, in the late 1990s, when an Invictus Savage named Rochelle Abara made exactly that investment with her city\u2019s entire police precinct, it drew a lot of skepticism from her peers in the First Estate. But Rochelle knew potential when she saw it, and if you don\u2019t take some risks sometimes, you\u2019ll never get your reward.<br /> <br /> That reward took the form of Noelle Rathborne, an up-and-coming sergeant who was ambitious to the point of hunger; she was the kind of person who desperately craved power over others \u2014 just the sort of person you want as a cop \u2014 and she saw her position as an ideal avenue to pursue that goal. However, with whispers of brutal tactics and \u201cmissing\u201d evidence threatening to end her career, Rochelle saw a chance for leverage.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t the first time a suit tried to offer Noelle a deal, but it was the first time she was genuinely interested in the possibilities. Her new regnant promised her a whole precinct of unquestionably loyal officers: They would keep the peace however they saw fit, and in return, they would clean up after any messes other Kindred left in their territory. Sometimes that meant dissolving body parts in rubber bins behind a hardware store; sometimes it meant scrubbing blood spatter out of shag carpet; and sometimes, it meant \u201cbringing someone in for questioning\u201d on special request.<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t take long for the crime statistics in Redwater Bay to become something other precincts only aspire to. It does help quite a bit when your officers are erasing the evidence of vampire-related murders or disappearances, but then, every precinct will pad its numbers in one way or another.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> Since Captain Rathborne took over, Redwater Bay has seen very little staff turnover, and anyone who might inquire about that gets pretty much the same answer: Noelle runs a tight ship, and she demands both loyalty and dedication from her officers. People who keep asking questions are prone to suffering messy accidents, or taking all-expenses-paid vacations to sulfuric acid baths.<br /> <br /> The residents of the neighborhood all seem thrilled with this turn of events. Honestly, a little too excited, as if they\u2019re putting on a performance for someone in the cheap seats. If anyone points this out, they\u2019re quick to laugh it off and change the subject. They all know, on some level, that the police don\u2019t tolerate dissenters.<br /> <br /> As for Rochelle Abara, she\u2019s happily reaped the fruits of her efforts for years, but she hasn\u2019t repeated it yet. A few decades isn\u2019t that long in a Requiem, and there\u2019s still one important thing she needs to know: What happens when people start realizing none of Redwater Bay\u2019s police officers are aging? Yes, there are ways of making sure no one looks too hard, but even a Savage knows to respect that old adage about not shitting where you eat. The First Tradition must be respected, and if it isn\u2019t, it might be time for Captain Rathborne to take a well-deserved retirement.<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Rooks (among the Invictus), Pigs (among everyone else), RBPD<br /> <br /> <b>Touchstone: </b>Captain Noelle Rathborne serves as her precinct\u2019s Touchstone, as she takes a personal interest in every bloody detail her officers handle.<br /> <br /> <b>Benefit: </b>[REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Redwater Bay police officers take after their scheming regnant and, as such, they feel more connected to Kindred and other ghouls than they do to humans. Rooks lose the 10-again quality for all Empathy, Persuasion, and Socialize rolls made against humans who don\u2019t relate to their current assignments.<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes:</b><ul><li><b>Daeva: </b>You think Gangrel make a mess? Try cleaning up after a Serpent\u2019s house party.</li> <li><b>Gangrel: </b>Then again, if you do get a call from a Savage, bring a shovel and a bottle of bleach. Trust me.</li> <li><b>Mekhet: </b>If I say, \u201cFollow up on a lead,\u201d I mean, \u201cTalk to a Shadow.\u201d</li> <li><b>Nosferatu:</b> For a few favors, a beat cop\u2019s best friend. Probably won\u2019t care for the favors, though.</li> <li><b>Ventrue: </b>Don\u2019t expect a soft touch, but it never hurts to know the DA\u2019s domme.</li> </ul><br /> <b>New Merit: Qualified Immunity (\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Prerequisite: </b>Redwater Bay Police<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Not only does your character benefit from the usual code of silence among cops, she\u2019s one of Rochelle\u2019s favorites, and her regnant\u2019s Invictus connections provide her a means to take far more extreme action in the name of \u201cjustice.\u201d Whenever she performs an illegal act to preserve the Masquerade, the Conspiracy of Silence will make any complications go away, provided she doesn\u2019t leave too much of a mess.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Rochelle\u2019s influence only goes so far. Your character should make sure to repay any big favors in kind, or else she\u2019ll be assigned to something much worse than desk duty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-17T12:57:30-07:00","id":1481312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481265#post1481265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also want to call out the illustration of this family as being one of my favourites in the book (linked on the STV product paged). Luchadores and vampires go together like a metaphor for things that go well together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it, too. It is really different from most of what I've contributed so far! And while on the subject of art I contributed to this book, I was very happy you were on board with giving the Redwater Bay ghoul the iconic &quot;BITCH&quot; shirt from <b>Bloodlines</b>. I love that stupid shirt, and it brought me immense joy sneaking it into the book!<br /> <br /> And I'm interested to hear about the design process for the Red Surrender. I was really impressed by how simple and straightforward the updated rules are. Kinda like how the Pareidolia Condition strips down Malkavia to its most interesting essentials in <b>False Gods</b> [at least imo].<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-17T14:12:28-07:00","id":1481313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481312#post1481312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it, too. It is really different from most of what I've contributed so far! And while on the subject of art I contributed to this book, I was very happy you were on board with giving the Redwater Bay ghoul the iconic &quot;BITCH&quot; shirt from <b>Bloodlines</b>. I love that stupid shirt, and it brought me immense joy sneaking it into the book!</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved the reference, and as I'm sure everyone must know by know, I love a good <i>VTMB </i>Easter Egg; I think we're 4 for 5, because I can't remember managing to fit one into <b>Better Feared</b> (though I guess the Von Schrecks could be read as an extremely orthogonal reference to Gary Golden). The <b>Strange Shades </b>one is very subtle, but the <b>Sin Again </b>and <b>False Gods </b>ones are pretty overt<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481312#post1481312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm interested to hear about the design process for the Red Surrender. I was really impressed by how simple and straightforward the updated rules are. Kinda like how the Pareidolia Condition strips down Malkavia to its most interesting essentials in <b>False Gods</b> [at least imo].</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny enough, for how efficient that Merit ended up, Red Surrender went through a <i>lot </i>of conceptual retooling over the course of writing. I'll talk about it in detail tomorrow, but it was initially a much more robust system, and early on, it was going to sort of be a stepping stone to gaining a Risen Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 05-17-2022, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T16:21:12-07:00","id":1481412,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's dig into some Chapter Three stuff.<br /> <br /> I don't think I've talked about this before, but the &quot;chapter 3 toolkit&quot; concept has probably changed the least from my very early conception of this project (i.e., the whole series). I even just dipped into my very jury-rigged outline for <b>Strange Shades </b>to see if that was true,* and sure enough, the basic idea is more or less intact. While the basic structure has expanded slightly, it's always involved Devotions, Merits, banes, and a little discussion of the Clan Curse. <b>Wild Hunt </b>breaks this format a bit by including a long section on Protean.<br /> <br /> Protean was always a power I was a bit indifferent to in <b>Masquerade </b>and <b>Requiem 1E</b>, mostly because it was very limited for a shapeshifting power. I was always a more a fan of Vicissitude and its more (perhaps <i>too</i>) freeform system (the influence of which you'll see below). So, it shouldn't be surprising that Protean in 2E went from being the Discipline I was least interested in to being right up there with my favourites\u2014for the record, Auspex, Dominate, and Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I thought it was important to talk about Protean from a player and Storyteller perspective. Not that we couldn't have talked about the other clan powers, but Protean is so wonderfully weird. It's the only physical Discipline with discrete powers, and it's the only one that you can actually <i>see</i>. It also makes the Gangrel the odd ones out among the five clans, in that their unique power isn't socially or mentally influential (Auspex is kind of an edge case, but you see what I mean). More than anything, I wanted to get into the Gangrel as shapeshifters: how that affects their psychology compared to the rest of the Damned, and how it makes them absolutely vicious hunters. All Disciplines are tools of the hunt, of course, but Protean is the most overtly so.<br /> <br /> Another thing I wanted to cover in this chapter was the Red Surrender, from <b>Savage and Macabre</b>, which went through a LOT of reworking over the course of writing the book. Originally, we conceived it as a stepping stone to gaining a Risen Beast, but we quickly realized that didn't really make sense. The Red Surrender is about integrating with your Beast's instincts, whereas a Passenger is about providing the Beast with a bit more of the Man. Eventually, we decided they needed to be separate, though it then took us a while to figure out how to even present the Red Surrender <i>as </i>a separate thing. Our first idea was to leave it as a thing Gangrel can do, but I didn't love the idea of having two &quot;signature systems&quot; in one book, and, upon having another readthrough of the original, I felt it was ultimately a pretty simple concept, one that didn't need much coverage. The author's first draft included a lot more bells and whistles, but I edited a lot of that down, to the point that I realized it felt like I was creating something more like a Merit...so I turned it into one! However, I did make sure that, if you prefer to have it still be an inherent quality of the Savages, you can really easily do that. Not everyone's going to want to use the Risen Beast, and if you prefer something a little more brutal, the Red Surrender's got your back. I'm a fan of simple, blunt systems that do a lot with a little, and I think this one has those qualities in spades.<br /> <br /> Which is all a rambling way of introducing a bunch of excerpts from the systems chapter. Tomorrow, I think it's time we get into the Horrors, starting with the <b>Blood Mold</b>...<br /> <br /> * &quot;Ideally, I\u2019d like this book to come in at around 50 pages, but I\u2019m okay if it ends up over or under. In other words, don\u2019t pad, but if you have an idea, throw it in and we\u2019ll see if it sticks.&quot; Oh, sweet, naive Past-Me...<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Three: Tools of the Hunt<br /> <br /> Devotions<br /> <br /> Awaken the Horrid Form<br /> (Animalism \u2022, Protean \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Some Gangrel learn to command the flesh of others like they do animals, pulling horrors from their victims\u2019 skins.<br /> <br /> A vampire must be touching her subject to use this Devotion.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 2 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Vitae per adaptation (1 Willpower, optional)<br /> <br /> <b>Requirement: </b>The victim must consume or be anointed by 1 Vitae (included in the cost).<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Dexterity + Crafts + Protean vs. Stamina + Blood Potency (if unwilling)<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Duration: </b>Night<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results<br /> <br /> Success: </b>The Gangrel applies adaptations from Predatory Aspect to a human, ghoul, or another vampire, up to a limit of her Protean dots divided by two (rounding up). This does not have to be one of her own forms, but inflicting a form she doesn\u2019t know requires her to spend an additional Vitae. This effect stacks with any forms the subject can already access through Protean, but the vampire can\u2019t double up the same effects.<br /> <br /> If the subject is a ghoul, the vampire can spend a Willpower to make his transformation permanent, but she cannot use this Devotion on him again unless to remove or swap out adaptations.<br /> <br /> If the vampire knows Uncanny Aspect, she can apply a single form from that Discipline for two Vitae.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Gangrel grants a part of her essence to the subject, who counts as being twice-removed in terms of blood sympathy with her for the duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure: </b>O, that this too too solid flesh would melt!<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> If he\u2019s a vampire, the subject\u2019s Beast recoils at this alteration, and he enters frenzy with the Gangrel as his target. If a human or ghoul, he suffers cardiac arrest or another catastrophic medical event.<br /> <br /> <b>Consume<br /> (Auspex \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Protean \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> This horrific Devotion allows a vampire to absorb her prey, slowly feeding on him until he withers away to nothing. The vampire\u2019s body merges with her victim\u2019s, mystically containing his mass without any outward signs.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 5 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Vitae<br /> <br /> <b>Requirement: </b>The vampire must drain a mortal victim of blood to the point of death.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>None<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Duration: </b>One week<br /> <br /> The vampire draws the victim into her body, completely absorbing him, and knowledge flows between the two. She gains all stored Willpower the victim had and, for the duration, can use any of his Mental and Social Skills if they are higher than her own. If the vampire wishes to consume a new victim before the duration expires, she must spend a Vitae to messily regurgitate the previous victim\u2019s bones and partially digested viscera beforehand.<br /> <br /> <b>Forced March<br /> (Celerity \u2022\u2022, Resilience \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> A product of Clan Gangrel\u2019s frequent need to cross large expanses of the wild before the sun catches up, this Devotion allows Kindred to move at top speed over long periods. Forced March is most often employed by Carthian Savages, especially couriers, preventing the Revolution\u2019s enemies from zeroing in on important communiqu\u00e9s.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 2 Experiences to learn, or 1 if the vampire is a member of the Carthian Movement.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>3 Vitae<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Duration: </b>Hours equal to Resilience<br /> <br /> The vampire can move at the maximum Speed allowed by Celerity for the duration. Except for reflexive actions such as Perception, she can do nothing but move in this time.<br /> If the vampire stops for any reason, she must reactivate this Devotion and repay all costs. However, any potential assailants must match her Speed or else they have little chance of catching up to her.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits<br /> <br /> Aspect of the Predator (\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Prerequisite: </b>Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Sometimes, the trick to getting rid of the competition is just looking like you\u2019re the bigger monster. When lashing out, your character\u2019s Blood Potency is always treated as one dot higher than another vampire\u2019s. This means she never has to spend a Willpower to respond to another Beast, and other characters must always spend one to respond to her.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Failing to back up your bark with sufficient bite can be disastrous. If your character loses a Predatory Aura contest with a vampire of higher Blood Potency, she must take the Bestial Triad Condition even if she would normally be immune to it, and its duration is doubled.<br /> <br /> <b>Atrocious, Advanced (\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Prerequisite: </b>Atrocious<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Your character\u2019s Beast is a thing of legend, a feral demon that resides within her veins. Once per chapter, gain a Beat whenever she invokes the Monstrous Beast in someone who has attacked her within the same scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>When lashing out with the Competitive or Wanton Beast, any failure becomes a dramatic failure.<br /> <br /> <b>Flesh Focus (\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Effect: </b>Your character is more in tune with the shape-changing aspects of Protean than other Savages. At one dot, she can memorize and assume a fourth adaptation with Predatory Aspect. At three dots, she can assume a specific second trait with Unnatural Aspect by spending an extra Vitae.<br /> <br /> <b>The Red Surrender (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Prerequisites:</b> Gangrel, Beast is not Risen<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Gangrel are closer to the Beast than other Kindred \u2014 too close, some say, but well out of hearing of any nearby Savages. Still, some believe it\u2019s not close enough.<br /> With the Red Surrender, your character can blur the lines between the Beast and her own personality. Unlike the Risen Beast (p. 79), this is a communion rather than a division, and as such, those who\u2019ve chosen the path of the Passenger can never use this technique.<br /> <br /> While operating under the Red Surrender, your character enjoys a variety of benefits from the Beast\u2019s power. Once per chapter, she can spend a Willpower to take the Tempted Condition. As long as this Condition lasts, she gains the following benefits:<ul><li>+1 on Athletics, Intimidation, Stealth, and Survival rolls; this applies to Disciplines and Devotions;</li> <li>+1 to Initiative;</li> <li>+1 to Perception;</li> <li>If she spends Willpower on dice pools involving Animal Ken, she gains a +5 instead of a +3.</li> </ul><br /> Each time the Tempted Condition compounds, the trait bonuses above increase by one, to a limit of +5. Once per scene, your character can spend another Willpower to compound Tempted a step, or she can provoke the Beast and hope she wins.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Letting the Beast so close to the surface means the Man falls into the depths. Any breaking points suffered during this period suffer the Tempted Condition\u2019s penalty as a modifier.<br /> <br /> <b>In the Flesh: A Players Guide to Protean</b><br /> <br /> <i>Our only security is our ability to change.</i><br /> <br /> \u2014John Lilly<br /> <br /> Razor sharp claws. Limbs warped to run faster, climb higher, and dig deeper. Grasping tails, spreading wings, gaping maws and things less easily described. Any or all of these images might come to mind when discussing Clan Gangrel. With the Beast made manifest in their very flesh, is it any wonder the Savages have such an intimate connection to it?<br /> Possessing the Discipline of Protean alters a vampire\u2019s Requiem in fundamental ways that no other power of the Blood does. This section examines how it affects not only the physicality of the Damned, but the very core of their identities.<br /> <br /> <b>Skin Like Quicksilver</b><br /> <br /> Even among the unique powers granted to each clan, Protean is special. Every other clan Discipline has some parallel that can be connected to human abilities, or even thought of as normal skills magnified.<br /> <br /> Auspex? Who doesn\u2019t make leaps of intuition now and again?<br /> <br /> Dominate? There are entire workshops and books dedicated to making people do what you say.<br /> <br /> Majesty? Charm is cheap! So many people are effortlessly enticing, with smiles that open doors and legs alike.<br /> <br /> Nightmare? There are those who can silence dissent with a raised eyebrow, who project menace in every move they make or thought they think.<br /> <br /> All these powers, unnatural though they may be, can be thought of as simply \u201chuman\u2026 but more.\u201d And, indeed, they often are by Kindred clinging to the past, but there\u2019s nothing human about exploding into a cloud of mist, or melding into a block of granite, or shedding your body like an old coat in favor of one with wings, claws, and scales. Protean, more than any other Discipline, announces its user\u2019s inhumanity to both herself and the world. To possess it is to hold constant, undeniable proof that one is no longer mortal, and the impact of that fact can\u2019t be overstated. Daeva and Ventrue submerse themselves in the herd of humanity, pretending to still be one of them. Mekhet and Nosferatu lurk unseen among the masses, desperate to still be a part of them. The Gangrel who soars above the crowd on wings she didn\u2019t possess yesterday knows, unequivocally, that she\u2019s something fundamentally different, and that there\u2019s no going back.<br /> <br /> <b>Bit by Bloody Bit</b><br /> <br /> The powers granted by Protean are so diverse that it\u2019s worth going through the Discipline\u2019s various abilities to better examine how it alters the experience of its users. Below you\u2019ll find a dot-by-dot discussion of each level.<br /> <br /> <b>Unmarked Grave</b><br /> <br /> Protean doesn\u2019t ease anyone into its use. Right off the bat, young Gangrel find their whole bodies merging with the earth while their minds remain active and aware, a feeling indescribable to anyone who hasn\u2019t experienced it themself. This is often enough to cause dysphoria and other mental trauma as the neonate is forced to grapple with their radical alteration of space.<br /> <br /> However, Protean\u2019s earliest gift is also one of its most potent. To possess even the barest understanding of the Discipline is to be untethered from domain or haven in a way that Kindred without it simply can\u2019t match. Savages new to their Requiems might not appreciate how powerful this gift is at first, but all come to be deeply thankful for it in time. The knowledge that safety from the sun (or, indeed, most threats) is just a patch of dirt away helps instill the confidence the clan is known for.<br /> <br /> <b>Predatory Aspect</b><br /> <br /> Perhaps the most iconic Gangrel ability is being able to take on a variety of animal-inspired features at a moment\u2019s notice, and it\u2019s available relatively early in their Requiems. It\u2019s hard to overstate the sheer versatility of Predatory Aspect; it turns a Gangrel\u2019s body into a Swiss army knife, from extra limbs to multiple senses. Still, it acutely throws a Savage\u2019s monstrous nature to the fore. Sure, that Haunt over there might be sort of creepy, but her Gangrel friend just grew ten thousand insect legs and is crawling around on the ceiling \u2014 which one is less human again?<br /> <br /> The obvious nature of these alterations also means that a vampire must be conscious of their surroundings and any potential witnesses when calling upon their gifts. Many Kindred abilities can be dismissed as tricks of the light or passing mania, but watching someone radically alter their physical form right in front of you is hard to dismiss. This Masquerade-induced need to hold back helps explain the isolationist nature of many Gangrel, and why they often prefer more secluded environments where they don\u2019t need to worry about prying eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast\u2019s Skin</b><br /> <br /> A less strange but much more versatile transformation than Unmarked Grave, a vampire with Beast\u2019s Skin is only limited by what animals she can sink her fangs into. While there are many options for both stealth (rats, house cats, snakes) and combat (wolves, bears, lions) granted by this ability, perhaps none are more Requiem-altering than taking on a form that can fly. Personal flight is a dream long held by humanity, and many Gangrel report feeling something akin to true joy the first time they launch themselves into the night on their new wings. Be it in the form of a bat, owl, eagle, crow, or something stranger, the ability to enjoy a whole new dimension of movement is a mind-expanding experience. If nothing else, Savages who can fly note how infrequently Kindred or people actually look up.<br /> <br /> Not only does this facilitate travel across vast swaths of terrain unseen, but the potential for hunting is significant. If Unmarked Grave is the first taste of freedom, then Beast\u2019s Skin is the full course meal. What does domain mean to Kindred who can travel between cities through the air? What meaning do a prince\u2019s laws have when you can leave when things get too complicated?<br /> <br /> The idea of a totally untethered Requiem is seductive, and this is yet another reason so many nomads are Gangrel. However, a vampire without ties is also one without Touchstones, or other tools to keep the Beast at bay, a problem Savages already struggle with. A wise Gangrel keeps a few roosts to land in, lest they become little more than a gory urban legend on a lonely stretch of highway.<br /> <br /> <b>Unnatural Aspect</b><br /> <br /> If the tools granted by Predatory Aspect are the most iconic, then the weapons given by the penultimate Protean ability are the most notorious. Easily the greatest contributing factor to the wariness other clans regard the Gangrel with is their propensity for sprouting awful claws that can rend even the resilient flesh of the Kindred asunder. Often, just the sight of these horrid talons is enough to stop fights before they begin, and it\u2019s at this point that those with Protean understand how much power they really possess.<br /> <br /> While some become swaggering brutes, many Gangrel who reach this level actually become more reserved and willing to resolve conflicts without violence (especially those who bear the Unholy\u2019s infamous claws). They know how much destruction they\u2019re capable of \u2014 particularly if they fall to frenzy \u2014 and they feel a sense of responsibility to not use their power recklessly. It helps that, at this point, most Savages feel they have very little left to prove.<br /> <br /> <b>Primeval Miasma</b><br /> <br /> Protean\u2019s final gift is a potent one. As a miasma, a Gangrel has the safety of Unmarked Grave coupled with the ability to move almost anywhere, as little can bar her entry. What\u2019s more, one doesn\u2019t even have to resume a solid form to feed, and some Savages are known to spend nights on end in this shape, simply luxuriating in the unfettered feeling.<br /> The only weakness of this shape is its lack of speed; any healthy prey can easily outpace the miasma, and moving anywhere in the form takes significant time. Still, this Discipline can impart a true sense of invincibility upon those who achieve it, and that feeling is hard to argue against, especially when you happen to get caught up inside it.<br /> <br /> This is the ultimate expression of the survivalist nature of Clan Gangrel, and it leads many of them to become foolhardy. After all, what\u2019s to fear when you can dissolve into a nigh-invulnerable cloud at a moment\u2019s notice? It\u2019s at this point that older Savages, the ones who\u2019ve existed for centuries and have seen all the terrible, dark corners the of world, will offer a smile without humor and mutter, \u201cYou\u2019ll see.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T16:41:15-07:00","id":1481414,"title":"","content":"Excellent tools. Even more excellent roleplaying tips. We simply can\u2019t have enough when in comes to the \u201cthese innate abilities to your template change your experience in these ways\u201d stuff. I wonder if I can do something similar for Mage\u2026 a future uncertain, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T08:31:40-07:00","id":1481459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481412#post1481412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing I wanted to cover in this chapter was the Red Surrender, from <b>Savage and Macabre</b>, which went through a LOT of reworking over the course of writing the book. Originally, we conceived it as a stepping stone to gaining a Risen Beast, but we quickly realized that didn't really make sense. The Red Surrender is about integrating with your Beast's instincts, whereas a Passenger is about providing the Beast with a bit more of the Man. Eventually, we decided they needed to be separate, though it then took us a while to figure out how to even present the Red Surrender <i>as </i>a separate thing. Our first idea was to leave it as a thing Gangrel can do, but I didn't love the idea of having two &quot;signature systems&quot; in one book, and, upon having another readthrough of the original, I felt it was ultimately a pretty simple concept, one that didn't need much coverage. The author's first draft included a lot more bells and whistles, but I edited a lot of that down, to the point that I realized it felt like I was creating something more like a Merit...so I turned it into one! However, I did make sure that, if you prefer to have it still be an inherent quality of the Savages, you can really easily do that. Not everyone's going to want to use the Risen Beast, and if you prefer something a little more brutal, the Red Surrender's got your back. I'm a fan of simple, blunt systems that do a lot with a little, and I think this one has those qualities in spades.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I cracked open <b>Wild Hunt</b> for the first time and started reading about the Risen Beast, I was like, &quot;huh, so I guess they opted not to update the Red Surrender for this? I am a little sad to see that go, but this seems very cool, so I can't mind too much.&quot; And then leafing through Chapter 3, I saw the Red Surrender, and realized that, yeah, in retrospect this doesn't actually mechanically do much more than a Merit [and oh! what a <i>nasty</i> drawback!]. Regrettably, a case where the cool thing for the 1e clanbook was all style and little substance. I also recall seeing a couple 2e conversions of the Red Surrender floating around the forums that were a daisy chain of Conditions or something, and those all seem so unnecessarily overwrought, now.<br /> <br /> I think I can echo all the other praise that the team has received for <b>Wild Hunt</b>'s Chapter 3. It is easily my favorite of the Chapter 3s across the clanbook updates, and the only one that I've actually, um, read all the way through, oops! And sure, that is mostly my gangrel brainrot giving me the strength to read through a bunch of specialized Devotions and Merits, but still. Basically every other Merit I was like, &quot;This will be perfect for my next gangrel character!&quot; And as usual, I loved the stuff at the end of the Chapter, especially the Protean essay, which was a pleasant surprise. I am sure you could write similar essays for the other signature Disciplines, even if they maybe do not need it as much [on the other hand, maybe an essay for Auspex is warranted given how many people treat it as some kind of win button...].<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481412#post1481412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Protean was always a power I was a bit indifferent to in <b>Masquerade </b>and <b>Requiem 1E</b>, mostly because it was very limited for a shapeshifting power. I was always a more a fan of Vicissitude and its more (perhaps <i>too</i>) freeform system (the influence of which you'll see below). So, it shouldn't be surprising that Protean in 2E went from being the Discipline I was least interested in to being right up there with my favourites\u2014for the record, Auspex, Dominate, and Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, I am someone who only really got into <b>Vampire</b> with 2e [I played some CofD 1e, but mostly Changeling and Promethean], and I am consistently surprised by how unnecessarily limited equivalent powers are in both <b>Requiem 1e</b> and <b>Masquerade</b>. And not just Protean, but the rest, too. It was a different time, I guess.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T12:56:40-07:00","id":1481474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481459#post1481459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I cracked open <b>Wild Hunt</b> for the first time and started reading about the Risen Beast, I was like, &quot;huh, so I guess they opted not to update the Red Surrender for this? I am a little sad to see that go, but this seems very cool, so I can't mind too much.&quot; And then leafing through Chapter 3, I saw the Red Surrender, and realized that, yeah, in retrospect this doesn't actually mechanically do much more than a Merit [and oh! what a <i>nasty</i> drawback!]. Regrettably, a case where the cool thing for the 1e clanbook was all style and little substance. I also recall seeing a couple 2e conversions of the Red Surrender floating around the forums that were a daisy chain of Conditions or something, and those all seem so unnecessarily overwrought, now.<br /> <br /> I think I can echo all the other praise that the team has received for <b>Wild Hunt</b>'s Chapter 3. It is easily my favorite of the Chapter 3s across the clanbook updates, and the only one that I've actually, um, read all the way through, oops! And sure, that is mostly my gangrel brainrot giving me the strength to read through a bunch of specialized Devotions and Merits, but still. Basically every other Merit I was like, &quot;This will be perfect for my next gangrel character!&quot; And as usual, I loved the stuff at the end of the Chapter, especially the Protean essay, which was a pleasant surprise. I am sure you could write similar essays for the other signature Disciplines, even if they maybe do not need it as much [on the other hand, maybe an essay for Auspex is warranted given how many people treat it as some kind of win button...].<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, I am someone who only really got into <b>Vampire</b> with 2e [I played some CofD 1e, but mostly Changeling and Promethean], and I am consistently surprised by how unnecessarily limited equivalent powers are in both <b>Requiem 1e</b> and <b>Masquerade</b>. And not just Protean, but the rest, too. It was a different time, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>The freedom CofD 2E provides you as both a player and a designer is truly unparalleled. It's partly why I haven't really given <b>V5 </b>much of a try beyond using it as reading/setting material (I complain about metaplot, but I'm also kind of in it <i>for </i>the metaplot). After you use <b>Requiem 2E</b>'s Discipline and Devotion system, you never want to go back.<br /> <br /> But yeah, having plumbed the depths of 1E, it's a very different design space. Bloodline Disciplines in particular are very conservative (with some exceptions) with what they'll let you do, which tended to make them either handy but extremely niche or broadly applicable but mechanically useless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T15:20:53-07:00","id":1481487,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's look at some Horrors!<br /> <br /> The horror section of Chapter 4 probably had the most changes from conception to final execution, and the Blood Mold in particular went through a lot of reworking. Initially, this concept was a disease that affected vampires, turning them into cannibalistic, body-horror mutants driven to feed on their Kindred. Not a bad idea, but if you've read our books before, you're probably thinking of the Noctuku Strain right now. Cannibalistic, body-horror mutant Kindred are a fine concept, but we'd rather emphatically done it before. One thing I strive <i>not </i>to do is repeat ourselves, and this was a case where there just wasn't enough difference.<br /> <br /> So, the big shift here was changing the mold's vector from vampires to humans: Humans who rise from the dead &quot;spontaneously&quot; and develop a hunger for blood that grants them greater and greater power until they explode into spores to begin the cycle all over again. That worked a lot better as both a difference from the Noctuku, and as a more unexpected element to throw into stories. Maybe the coterie thinks they've got a poacher on their territory, only to discover it's some <i>mortal </i>is feeding on their herd...only to then discover he's not mortal in any way that counts.<br /> <br /> Another change was in the basic ways these antagonists work mechanically. Initially, there was a whole suite of dread powers for them; again, not a bad idea, but another thing I strive to do is to not reinvent the wheel. Protean already has plenty of adaptations that cover a similar design space, and it also felt more thematic to imply that the mold was sort of... <i>infected </i>with Protean. We leave the backstory somewhat open-ended on that front, but there are a few hooks you could play around with if you wanted a closer connection to the Gangrel in particular.<br /> <br /> So, here's the Blood Mold! Tomorrow, I'll return with <b>gargoyles</b>...<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Mold: The Creeping Terror</b><br /> <br /> &quot;<i>It's not as bad as it looks!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>AKA: <i>Ophiocordyceps lucifuga</i></b><br /> <br /> Fungus is something of a paradox: simple but complex, neither plant nor animal, a harbinger of entropy yet a branch of life all its own. Fungi are adept at returning dead, inert matter into the food chain, and what\u2019s a vampire but a walking, talking, thirsting pile of compost?<br /> <br /> It was only a matter of time before a fungal network got a taste of undeath and evolved. In the end, nature devours us all. The Kindred exist comfortably at the top of the food chain, but beneath their feet lies a hungry and ever-expanding predator that craves the brittle flesh and sanguine ichor of the dead. It is a patient and subtle killer, and if you\u2019ve noticed it, no antifungal will save you.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> Back in the 70s, a Savage Carthian called Marguerite Samson founded the Second Earth Revival Fellowship, a commune and cult of personality she used to protect her territory in the local state park. Then, in the late 90s, corporate logging interests associated with the Invictus rolled into her turf. Marguerite couldn\u2019t have that, and her particular style of dispute resolution left six human loggers and a First Estate ghoul dead. She planted the bodies in an unmarked grave deep in the forest, hoping that nature would take care of the rest.<br /> <br /> In a way, it did. The topsoil around the bodies was laced with fungus from the parasitic Ophiocordyceps family. Steeped in the rich, profane nutrition of Vitae-infused human flesh, the fungus drank deeply. Slowly, it evolved to feed a new hunger, and to do that, it borrowed the bodies it had been provided. Imagine Marguerite\u2019s surprise when the Invictus flunky and his goons wandered back into her commune three days after she killed them all. Visualize her shock as they began to grow in size and appendages whilst they drained her coterie. Picture her horror as they ate her alive. From there, the creatures headed to the city, slaughtering four more Kindred before the collective might of the domain\u2019s elders destroyed them.<br /> <br /> Yet fungus is pernicious. It doesn\u2019t constitute a discrete being, but rather an assemblage of many. One of the creatures managed to enter the end stage of its bizarre life cycle, bursting into a miasma or spores as its host was destroyed. Hitching a ride on nothing more than the wind, it\u2019s been spreading ever since.<br /> <br /> <b>Waking Up Dead</b><br /> <br /> Occult medical experts call this new species <i>lucifuga </i>(\u201cday-fearing\u201d). It can grow on just about any surface, taking on the appearance of a fuzzy carpet the color of deep red wine. This appearance is the source of its other, more common name: Blood Mold. It enjoys the dark, and those without the knowledge to differentiate would say that it resembles a bad case of black mold. Its brittle mycelia allow it to particulate airborne spores, which, ideally, migrate into any nearby lungs.<br /> <br /> In living tissue, the fungus is no more dangerous than any other spore or mold. Mortal blood lacks the essential nutrition of Vitae, so <i>O. lucifuga</i> instead uses human bodies as a transmission vector for its rotting infection. Living victims develop a wet, wracking cough and flu-like symptoms, as well as a sensitivity to light, but while those with weakened immune systems or asthma may develop pneumonia, most recover with the aid of drugs. Infected Kindred, on the other hand, find their blood supplies grow thin, though this never poses much danger beyond inconvenience, and the infection will burn itself out by consuming too much of its host\u2019s precious Vitae.<br /> <br /> The real fun begins when the fungus finds a corpse. Without an immune system or Blood Potency to fight off the invasion, within a few hours, the fungus will replace any damaged tissue with its own, resparking the corpse\u2019s nervous system and raising the body from the dead.<br /> <br /> In a few nights or weeks, the Blood Mold pushes its host to feed. Each time he does, the parasite colonizes the corpse\u2019s body more and more, mutating it into a monstrous entity best suited to prey on as many victims as possible. At first, patches of mold spread across his flesh, starting at the mouth and lower orifices, followed soon thereafter by sprouts of woody, fibrous growths with a shriveled texture like morel mushrooms. When the victim speaks, his breath carries the stale sweetness of rot. By the time these growths spill from his mouth, nose, eyes, and skin, the colonization is complete. From there, he becomes a grotesque and massive beast with only two drives: feeding and breeding.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems</b><br /> <br /> O. lucifuga seeks out animal and human corpses to propagate its existence. Like any fungus, it lives in dark, dank places, but without a host, it cannot reach its full potential.<br /> <br /> Blood Mold will infect any cadaver that\u2019s been dead no longer than a day or two, but once a corpse hits the \u201cactive\u201d stage of decay, it\u2019s no longer viable. Living humans infected with O. lucifuga experience mild cold symptoms, while vampires gain an unsightly, sweet-smelling skinrash and suffer a reduction in Vitae capacity, losing an additional point per night. Kindred clear the infection whenever their Vitae pools next fall to zero, utterly starving the fungus in a matter of moments.<br /> <br /> If a carrier vampire feeds on a mortal victim to the point of death, the victim will always rise as a host.<br /> <br /> <b>Host Traits</b><br /> <br /> <i>O. lucifuga </i>hosts share the following qualities:<br /> <br /> <b>Alien Urgings:</b> When faced with reasonable opportunities to feed, the host must resist the urge with Resolve + Composure. Unless he gives in of his own violation, failure means he enters a frenzy-like state, which the fungus might still attempt to induce if he doesn\u2019t drink his victim dry. The host\u2019s mutation stage (below) acts as a penalty to this roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Sense: </b>Hosts gain the Bloodhound Merit, ignoring the Wits prerequisite. Furthermore, while they don\u2019t have Predatory Auras, hosts can recognize Kindred from the sweet scent of their Vitae.<br /> <br /> <b>Sanguine Hunger:</b> Hosts can feed as Kindred do. However, instead of a Kiss/Assault effect, the fungus inflicts victims with a paralytic poison, rendering them immobile for each turn of feeding (treat this as the Stunned Tilt if necessary: Chronicles of Darkness, p. 286). Humans have no resistance to this chemical, but vampires can resist the effect per turn with Stamina + Blood Potency, taking the host\u2019s mutation stage as a penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire Traits: </b>A host has Blood Potency 0, which cannot be increased. Being ambulant corpses, hosts also downgrade damage like Kindred, though wounds still heal over time. However, natural healing always adds more fungal matter, making the infection\u2019s presence more obvious as time goes by. They also do not pass out from full bashing or lethal damage in their Health tracks.<br /> <br /> <b>Unkillable: </b>If a host \u201cdies,\u201d the fungus will resurrect him within a day, healing all wounds. The only way to kill a host is to burn his corpse to ash or to expose it to sunlight at later stages of mutation. Resurrection involves replacing more of the creature\u2019s body with fungus, and this automatically advances the host\u2019s mutation stage.<br /> <br /> <b>Mutation Stages</b><br /> <br /> Blood Mold hosts go through five stages of mutation. At each stage, the fungus replaces more and more of the victim\u2019s body with itself. These stages progress based on how often the host feeds: Whenever the host consumes blood, roll his unmodified Resolve + Stamina. On a failure, he mutates into the next stage. If the blood came from a vampire, apply the total Vitae taken as a penalty on this roll.<br /> <br /> The effect of each stage is cumulative.<br /> <br /> <b>Stage 1</b><br /> <br /> The sudden influx of repaired tissue leaves the subject feeling energized despite his recent demise. He looks like he\u2019s put on some muscle and lost some fat, partly due to his desiccated flesh and partly due to the masses starting to build up under his skin. Upon rising, the host gains a dot of Strength, which can take this Attribute past the human limit.<br /> <br /> <b>Stage 2</b><br /> <br /> Fungal tissue swells in the victim\u2019s muscles, granting him another dot in Strength but riddling his skin with rashes and distending his form as fruiting bodies begin to press against his flesh. This stage also grants limited shapeshifting abilities: Choose two adaptations from Predatory Aspect. The host can spend a Vitae to manifest these forms for a scene at any time with an instant action. Furthermore, sunlight deals him a bashing damage per minute of exposure, which cannot heal until he seeks shelter or he spends Vitae to repair the damage manually.<br /> <br /> <b>Stage 3-5</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 05-19-2022, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T15:06:19-07:00","id":1481560,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve just reread Risen Beast on account of getting the impression that it made you immune to mind control first time I read it, glad to see you didn\u2019t give people a way to be immune to 3 disciplines but also glad I checked before posting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T15:29:45-07:00","id":1481563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481560#post1481560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve just reread Risen Beast on account of getting the impression that it made you immune to mind control first time I read it, glad to see you didn\u2019t give people a way to be immune to 3 disciplines but also glad I checked before posting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're not immune to mind control, just possession. The Passenger <i>might </i>know when your memories are altered, if you buy the Twin Minds Merit, but unless you get the five-dot version, it won't be able to say <i>what </i>changed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hello again! Let's talk about gargoyles (have <i>you </i>talked to your doctor about gargoyles?)<br /> <br /> Gargoyles are an odd feature of both iterations of <b>Vampire</b>. They're not something that comes to mind in more generic vampire fiction(?), and I <i>feel </i>like the trope of living gargoyles has much more to do with the cartoon, though I also have a vague sense that White Wolf's gargoyles predate it, so who knows.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, gargoyles in Requiem have a spotty history. They're mentioned in the original core rulebook (along with hell hounds and homunculi), but they're more or less an afterthought: they don't have special powers, and it doesn't explain how you create them. They don't appear again in any significant fashion until <b>The Danse Macabre</b>, where they're given a complete overhaul.<br /> <br /> Obviously, our take on gargoyles is based on <b>TDM</b>'s presentation, though we expanded their concept and simplified their systems. Now, they effectively work more like non-human vampires, at least at base. Our big change was making them viable as player characters, dividing them into two distinct types: Automata and Rampant. Automata are effectively barely sentient robots, whereas Rampant manage to (in one way or another) attain a semblance of Humanity.<br /> <br /> Why the change? As with anything I do, for the drama. <b>Requiem</b>'s 1E gargoyles are <i>neat</i>, but one thing I think the <b>Masquerade </b>version has on them is consequences, the danger that they might turn on you. That said, I wasn't hugely comfortable with the baked-in slave/master dynamic that's core to the <b>VTM </b>version, so how you treat your awakened gargoyles is dependent solely on what kind of vampire you are. There are still definitely ethical questions you can delve into about creating mindless automatons to do your bidding, but that's down to you and the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here are gargoyles. Before I go, I'd just like to once again note that we love reviews, and I'd be eternally grateful if you could find time to head over to the Vault and leave one, or just a star rating. Getting feedback on these things is VERY useful, if only because it can help people get past the minor stigma that sometimes attaches itself to community content. I'd say go do that right now, but DTRPG seems to be having some sort of conniption at the moment. So, uh, keep us in mind when they're back up and running. (Also feel free to comment here, too; I sometimes worry I'm just talking to myself.)<br /> <br /> <b>Gargoyles: Children of the Stones<br /> <br /> AKA: The Graven</b><br /> <br /> Vampires are creatures of flesh, but the Blood doesn\u2019t always limit itself to the organic. Vitae spares little from its corruption, blighting even stone and steel, and with just little effort and hubris, the Curse can take hold in more solid things than corpses.<br /> <br /> Since time immemorial, vampires have birthed beings both dead and never alive, hardier than ghouls and far more loyal than childer. Gargoyles make ideal servants for Kindred with no need for a personal touch: The Children of the Stones are devoid of drive or desire, and they\u2019ll follow their creators\u2019 orders unto Final Death.<br /> <br /> Or maybe not. Some of the so-called Graven can gain a touch of the Humanity their unholy births denied them, stealing into the night to make their own way in the All Night Society, whether for freedom, revenge, or a better offer.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> The gargoyle looming over church eaves is an indelible image. These sneering grotesques carried a power all their own, and before they became mere waterspouts, they were wards against the Devil, a practical application of holy terror to protect the house of God. While the righteous slept, the gargoyles stood vigilant, and for their trouble, they were treated with a superstitious respect. The Children of the Stones have similar origins, and undoubtedly this is why they share a name with these figures. Ancient Kindred were just as prone to ritual and magical thinking as the mortals they once were, offering blood sacrifices to idols, lucky charms, and other fetishes shaped in the rough form of a man. What they thought when these objects first started coming to life is unknown, but it didn\u2019t take long for them to learn how to use them.<br /> <br /> Graven in the Roman Camarilla were carved of polished marble in the form of griffins, gorgons, and other mythological beasts to patrol the halls of the Necropolis. In Viking Scandinavia, they were crafted with wood as wicker imps who would sabotage their masters\u2019 enemies in the daytime. And in China, Kindred nobles would imitate the emperor, commissioning terracotta armies to protect themselves for their journeys through death.<br /> <br /> Tonight, gargoyles have shed much of their mythological and spiritual baggage. More akin to multitools of the Damned, most Graven live up to stereotypes as guardians glaring down from castle keeps, or as menials designed to keep havens in efficient order. Some designs \u2014 especially among elders with more blood than sense \u2014 range into the esoteric. A vampire might create a flock of single-use Graven, each a key to successive doors through an arcane vault. Or maybe the gargoyle has no practical application at all, instead serving as a semi-sentient art installation, nothing more than an unliving symbol of its master\u2019s power.<br /> <br /> <b>Automata and Rampant</b><br /> <br /> A gargoyle is a blunt, bespoke instrument; nothing more. Most can communicate with their masters, though spending time with a talkative one isn\u2019t unlike typing at an above average chatbot. For this reason, Kindred are even given to calling them Automata, a term that gained currency as the Industrial Revolution helped humanity develop its own advanced technology.<br /> <br /> However, it has no agency beyond its master\u2019s wishes, and for some Kindred, that in itself is worth the heavy blood investment. Yes, a ghoul or a childe can understand the spirit of a command, but most gargoyles will <i>never </i>deviate from the letter.<br /> <br /> The key word here, however, is \u201cmost.\u201d In rare cases, a gargoyle can earn a scrap of the Humanity it never had, achieving an intellect beyond impulse and devotion. Kindred call these creatures Rampant, Graven who escape the confines of their design perimeters to become something almost like a real vampire. Some Rampant abandon their creators to make their own Requiems, while others come to new terms with their progenitors, offering services on more equal ground. Still others watch and wait, keeping up a fa\u00e7ade of docility for the chance to take revenge on years of mindless toil. How this transformation takes place is unknown (or at least inconsistent), but the possibility is often enough to put vampires off using Graven servants altogether.<br /> <br /> <b>In the Covenants</b><br /> <br /> As with everything else, the five great covenants have differing viewpoints on the creation and use of gargoyles.<br /> <br /> <b>The Carthian Movement: </b>Many Firebrands ban the creation of gargoyles. Whether Automata are sapient or not is beside the point \u2014 building creatures with no purpose beyond service is no better than any other feudalistic practice in the All Night Society. However, Rampant gargoyles do sometimes find their way to the Movement, though their inability to maintain a Masquerade makes remaining difficult. Even among the most liberal Firebrands, a gargoyle can\u2019t contribute to the cause in the way a normal vampire can, so many are limited to grunt and wet work.<br /> <br /> <b>The Circle of the Crone:</b> The Acolytes view gargoyle creation as holy. Spawning life (even a facsimile) from inanimate things is surely sacred to the Dark Mother, and so the Crone rewards her faithful servants with faithful servants of their own. Gargoyles are regarded with a certain reverence among the Mother\u2019s Army, though that\u2019s no guarantee they\u2019ll last long: Sacrificing a gargoyle for a Cr\u00faac ritual is rumored to infuse the magic with incredible potency\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>The Invictus: </b>There\u2019s nothing this covenant likes more than new toys, especially ones that can protect their assets. The Invictus uses gargoyles as technology: weapons, security systems, amenities, and any other functional roles its elites can think of. Most First Estate Automata are outsourced, crafted by Dragon or Acolyte builders for considerable sums or favors, but some lower-ranking Invictus members will create their own Graven, even though many elders look down on <i>nouveau riche </i>who would use gargoyles as a quick fix to make up lacking for a proper powerbase.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lancea et Sanctum: </b>Many a Sanctified church has a gargoyle installed in the eaves, watching and waiting for anyone foolish enough to violate holy ground. The Church\u2019s theology views gargoyles as less than animals, inherently sinful things they can use as they please to effect the Dark Father\u2019s will. This belief extends to the Rampant, though the Sanctified don\u2019t really recognize a distinction. Coincidentally, Sanctified gargoyles are the most likely to turn on their masters if they achieve sapience, seeking revenge for years of thankless tasks.<br /> <br /> <b>The Ordo Dracul: </b>No other covenant produces as many gargoyles as the Ordo Dracul; even the Mother\u2019s Army seem like dabblers in comparison to the Order\u2019s assembly lines, and in some cities, it\u2019s unheard of for Defiant not to maintain at least one Graven servant around their chantries. Gargoyles and their never-living state provide all sorts of opportunities for research and development, an endless source of fruitful experimentation. Defiant are also the most accommodating to Rampant, as long as they\u2019ll submit to some testing now and then.<br /> <br /> <b>The Birthing Ritual</b><br /> <br /> To create a gargoyle, a vampire must conduct a special ritual similar to blood sorcery. This rite has different trappings depending on the vampire\u2019s clan and covenant, but whatever the surface details, the core mechanism is the same across the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> Before conducting the ritual, the vampire must fashion an appropriate chassis for her creation. This need not have moving parts; it just needs to take the shape of the intended gargoyle, as well as the primary material that will take up its form. Once the ritual is complete, the Blood will provide all the necessary logistics of mobility. If other vampires contribute to the gargoyle\u2019s creation, the creature will follow their commands as well, but its creator\u2019s orders override all others.<br /> <br /> Successfully creating a gargoyle is a Humanity 3 breaking point.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>Vitae equal to five plus the gargoyle\u2019s intended Blood Potency. A new gargoyle\u2019s Blood Potency cannot exceed more than half its creator\u2019s, rounding up.<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve + Occult + Blood Potency<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended (target is ten plus the gargoyle\u2019s desired Blood Potency, and each roll represents an hour of time)<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results<br /> <br /> Success:</b> The ritual accumulates successes. If the target number is met, a new gargoyle is birthed.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The vampire makes great strides in completing the birthing ritual. Her player can choose one of the usual effects of an exceptional success on an extended action, or she can take either the Ecstatic Condition or the Raptured Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The vampire accumulates no successes. Her player can choose to abandon the birthing or take the Stumbled Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The birthing ritual fails, and the vampire takes the Tempted Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Creation</b><br /> <br /> Create gargoyle characters following the steps outlined below.<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T17:42:12-07:00","id":1481570,"title":"","content":"Having playable Gargoyles in VTR is an excellent idea! The rules for the Birthing Ritual is also neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T02:20:40-07:00","id":1481741,"title":"","content":"As soon as I'll have some money, I'll be buying that book ! I'm sure it is stellar work !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T11:31:47-07:00","id":1481767,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this is the place for errata, but it looks like Version 1.1 still has the Heartwood merit have both Wooden Bounty and Rustling Leaves as two dot effects and Vast Ecosystem as a three dot effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T11:44:14-07:00","id":1481768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481741#post1481741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As soon as I'll have some money, I'll be buying that book ! I'm sure it is stellar work !</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what we like to hear! And consider leaving us a review, if you have a chance. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, Hunting Grounds.<br /> <br /> These are places tainted either by vampire blood or horrible tragedies that awaken and become bloodthirsty landscapes. The concept was pitched to me veeeeeery early in this book's process, possibly even before I wrote the outline, and I liked it a lot from the start. Vampiric &quot;places&quot; is a cool, simple concept, and (while we don't relate Hunting Grounds directly to them) I'm always down for more Mysterious Places.<br /> <br /> That said, I think this might be the system I altered most in development. Initially, Hunting Grounds had Attributes and Numina and so on, and I more or less excised all of them, leaving only Blood Potency and Influence, which we modified from ephemeral beings. Ultimately, I felt that creatures like this are very elemental, and giving them a lot of stats made them a bit too &quot;knowable&quot;. I also just generally like to make Storyteller-facing systems as uncomplicated as possible. Plus, the &quot;Hounds&quot; of these places are basically just ghouls, and those are going to be the true point of contact for most player characters.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, I've done pretty much all my corrections for the Gangrel book, so I'll be uploading the errata'd version later today. I also had most of a long weekend to go hunting for missed typos in the other books (I broke down and resorted to Grammarly, because I'm utterly typo-blind to these books at this point), so those will be updated as well. If there <i>are </i>any typos left after that, they're craftier than me, and I leave them to their sinful business. I might try doing an errata form next time I put out a big release; 90K+ words is just...a lot of words, and the next books ain't gonna be shorter...<br /> <br /> And now I'm just musing out loud, so here are Hunting Grounds! Tomorrow, the final Horror: The <b>Narya</b>!<br /> <br /> <b>Hunting Grounds: The Hungry Earth</b><br /> <br /> <i>&lt;a low rumble followed by muffled screams and the sound of branches breaking&gt;</i><br /> <br /> <b>AKA: Badlands</b><br /> <br /> The Savages share many legends around the fire. While some are just ghost stories to see who can spook their Kindred the most, these yarns often illustrate useful lessons, especially to fledglings. If a vampire sheds her essence too often, some say, her haven will take on her curse. The candlelight dims in her presence, the spiders weave words in the webs, and the floors creak almost like a moaning voice. Or so the tales go. Mostly, this is superstition, coupled with an animal inclination not to shit where you eat.<br /> <br /> Still, Vitae is nothing if not adaptable. Sometimes, the taint of death pools in low places, and the pain refuses to fade away. Sometimes, the land goes bad. Stains like this exist throughout the world, and left to fester through neglect or ignorance, this seeded corruption can sprout. Hunting Grounds are the end result of this awful bloom, and while not all are the product of Kindred carelessness, these places all share the Beast\u2019s mindset without any of the Man\u2019s self-control.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> Hunting Grounds are vampires. They feed on blood and manipulate the living to get their fill of it, hiding in plain sight as the masses walk on by. They don\u2019t cling to covenants or Traditions or Humanity or discrete bodies, but maybe that just makes them a purer strain of death than the Kindred. Strix sometimes roost in Badlands for this reason, providing the creatures with fresh victims in exchange for shelter during the daylight hours.<br /> <br /> Hunting Grounds form when too much blood spills in one place. Usually, this is due to a vampire lairing in the same area for many years, letting her prey\u2019s viscera dribble into the earth. Draugr often create Badlands because of their habit of leaving kills to rot in their nests, but any vampire who doesn\u2019t bother to clean up after a meal can spawn one of these creatures. At other times, this spark of hunger emerges from human influence, like a killer storing hundreds of victims in a single grave, or a battle flooding the soil with gore.<br /> <br /> However it takes shape, bloodlust leaks from a Hunting Ground like radiation. It works its way through the air, the earth, the groundwater, and into all the creatures that live within its reach. The influence spreads first through wild beasts like birds and rodents, then through domesticated animals, then, finally, into humans. And as this influence grows, so too does the Hunting Ground\u2019s thirst.<br /> <br /> Most Kindred have never heard of Hunting Grounds, but Gangrel have encountered them many times over many centuries. Whether this is due to the sort of places the clan chooses for havens or because they give rise to Badlands more often than other vampires is a topic for debate, but it was undeniably the Savages who named the phenomenon, and it\u2019s the Savages who are most often left to deal with it.<br /> <br /> <b>One of Us</b><br /> <br /> The primeval cunning of a Badland isn\u2019t intelligence, per se, but it knows a predator needs a pack, especially one without mobility. While Hunting Grounds have an inherent mastery over the low beasts who burrow and nest within it, most recognize humans are apex predators in their own right, and they can tap into that strength for their own greedy ends. Like Kindred, a Hunting Ground can grab mortals by the lizard brain through the addictive power of Vitae, and once a person belongs to it, she becomes its \u201cwilling\u201d agent in the world. She becomes its Hound.<br /> <br /> Despite the name, Hounds need not be feral brutes on leashes. Humans have always been hunters, and a good hunter adapts to its environment and prey. A Hound can just as easily kill with a knife in her victim\u2019s back as she can with an \u201caccidental\u201d misfire during deer season, or a box of poisoned muffins at a PTA meeting. In some Badlands, Hounds are hulking, hairless monstrosities born from humans merging with forest animals; others are filled with beautiful people whose lovely eyes belie their soulless, mindless interiors; and yet others are populated with \u201cnormal\u201d people who carry the sickly sweet scent of tumorous interiors like walking, talking rotten fruit.<br /> <br /> <b>Where the Heart Is</b><br /> <br /> At the center of each Hunting Ground is its Heart, the spiritual seat of its hungry urges. Like the Hunting Ground itself, the Heart can be anything: a forest pit lined with thousands of bones, a bloody altar in an old church, or even the fountain inside a shopping mall. The Heart is the only place where the Hunting Ground\u2019s thirst can be quenched, but, like any vampire, it\u2019s also the part that\u2019s most vulnerable, and even while stalking prey, the Hounds mustn\u2019t stray too far away from it. It\u2019s the seat of their community and the ritual focus of their lives. Should an interloper manage to damage the Heart, either by destruction or exorcism, the Hunting Ground dies, and any gifts bestowed upon its servants end with it.<br /> <br /> <b>Three Badlands</b><br /> <br /> Local legend says an epidemic closed the sanitarium, but in truth, it was the thing growing beneath the floors, supping on the blood and trauma of its residents. However, when the place was shut down, the creature lost its food supply, and so it fell to dormancy. Eventually, an enterprising Lick acquired it as a bolt hole, a place she could bury her prey without fear of scrutiny. Unfortunately for her, the Invictus was watching, and when they came to put her down, the bloody fight awakened the structure. Now the vampire and the sanitarium work together, using Kindred victims to grow their mutual territory, exponentially.<br /> <br /> The Tri-County Shopping Mall is dying. Years ago, it was a magnificent monument to 80s consumerism, a home away from home for weekend shoppers, teenagers, and elderly walkers, but today, it\u2019s succumbing to wounds dealt by online shopping and other modern conveniences. When a bankrupt shop owner hurled himself to his death from a third-floor railing, the land beneath the mall awakened. Though small in number, its Hounds are composed of a healthy mix of youthful bodies and families who\u2019ve begun to lure others into their burgeoning cult. In a way, the mall hungers for community. It longs to be full of life again, and if it can\u2019t have that, the blood will do just as well.<br /> <br /> Everyone in town knows the wishing well in the middle of the park. Once upon a time, it was the town\u2019s original water supply, but over the years, a lack of maintenance left it as little more than a relic and an eyesore. That is, until a little boy drowned trying to skim coins from it in the middle of the night. The body was never recovered, and the well woke up. Now, rumors are spreading that the old wishing well can really make your dreams come true if you make the right offering. The well hungers for sacrifice, and the larger the trade, the greater the reward. As long as the sacrifice holds value to the person offering it, the Hunting Ground will accept it, and as the sacrifices build up, so too does its ability to grant wishes to its faithful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T11:47:03-07:00","id":1481769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481767#post1481767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if this is the place for errata, but it looks like Version 1.1 still has the Heartwood merit have both Wooden Bounty and Rustling Leaves as two dot effects and Vast Ecosystem as a three dot effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't really a place for errata, so here is as good as any. Good catch! As per my post above, I'm updating the file today, and I'd missed that one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T14:42:15-07:00","id":1481780,"title":"","content":"Hunting Grounds look terrible! Uh, for its victims I mean, not us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Their methods of creation seem to imply they\u2019d almost always coincide with death-Resonant Loci and Avernian Gates. Now imagine the hellhole <i>that</i> would spawn\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T15:16:29-07:00","id":1481868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481780#post1481780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunting Grounds look terrible! Uh, for its victims I mean, not us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Their methods of creation seem to imply they\u2019d almost always coincide with death-Resonant Loci and Avernian Gates. Now imagine the hellhole <i>that</i> would spawn\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they coincide with a lot of other nastiness. We didn't want to get too deep into that territory, because it's better if these things stand on their own feet, but we definitely had some crossover in mind.<br /> <br /> Now, let's talk about the Narya!<br /> <br /> The Narya (aka, the Colossi) are non-Kindred vampires, kind of <b>Wicked Dead</b>-style. They have a lot of similar traits to the more typical vampires, especially (suspiciously) the Gangrel, but their archetype is more about hubris than predation. No longer able to make more of their kind, they walk the night making trouble for the Kindred by imposing all sorts of pointless, baroque schemes on them to pass the time better, and, maybe, in the hopes of one day finding a way to breed again. They're also far more vulnerable to the sun than Kindred, instantaneously petrifying into statues with even a glint of sunlight.<br /> <br /> Obviously, they're something of an homage to another vampire-adjacent property, which shall remain nameless. Ironically, the thing they're a reference to is like the one thing I know about that property; I was once forced to watch half a season of it for reasons that are too arcane to go into here.*<br /> <br /> In terms of development, the big changes came in the form of making them less referential. The first draft was a <i>tad </i>too nodding and winking, so I upped the Tzimisce-ness of them, giving them an ambiguously Eastern Euroasian origin and making their major weakness into a kind of hyperfocus on their vices: more Greek tragedy, less anime. I also made their connection to the &quot;void&quot; a bit more prominent, and implied a few <b>Werewolf </b>connections you might be able to suss out...<br /> <br /> So, have a look at the Narya. Tomorrow, I think I'll do a quick excerpt of the Clan Bane section, and after that, I think our journey might be at an end. Maybe I'll see if I can dig up any cut material. There was some fun stuff about &quot;Project Shaterglass&quot; for the Mystikoi that I had to chop for space, for instance.<br /> <br /> <b>Narya: The Colossi</b><br /> <br /> <i>The most potent warriors are patience, time, and me.</i><br /> <br /> <b>AKA: Antediluvians</b><br /> <br /> Kindred were not the first vampires to rule the night. Those who count themselves among the All Night Society are merely the most successful. Long before the Kindred drank their first draft, other horrors stalked the dark in search of prey.<br /> <br /> The Narya are one such horror. These deathless monsters \u2014 vampires in all but name \u2014 say they once ruled a golden empire, yet now their numbers have dwindled to barely a handful. Scant evidence of their past exists in eerie and intricate statues, murals, and reliefs, but little does the waking world suspect that these immaculate works house the monsters they depict. And when these ancients rise, it is with a deep and desperate hunger.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> The Colossi claim their human ancestors ruled over a long-lost kingdom in a remote part of the earth, long before the time of the biblical flood. However, this kingdom was nearly shattered when a sudden catastrophe befell it. The ground shook, the moon swallowed the sun, and the sky was sundered. In desperation, the royal family of this land offered up a sacrifice to the \u201cvoid\u201d spreading from the wound in the sky. When the calamity passed, the nobles were changed into gods, not only masters of their people, but masters of the physical form, whether their own or anything they touched. What they called themselves is lost to time \u2014 even they do not recall \u2014 but Kindred records use the term Narya, a Sanskrit word for heroism and potency. The Narya themselves prefer Colossi, for they stride across the world as giants among lesser beings.<br /> <br /> Now more than mere mortals, the corrupted royal family raised temples to their own egos, devouring sacrifices in the thousands and waging proxy wars against each other for their own amusement, all hidden in the shadows. For although they were eternal, their pact with the void had cursed them to turn to stone under the wrathful gaze of the sun.<br /> All of humanity might be under their wretched yolk tonight had the unthinkable not happened: Almost overnight, the Narya became sterile. Some speak of a plague that passed silently among them, the symptoms only apparent long after it was too late, while others believe they made some slight against the void, punished for their hubris.<br /> <br /> The Colossi had always limited their bloodline, but without a means to breed, the rigors of time, ennui, and the threat of a hateful sun devastated their numbers. Now those who remain have embraced the long sleep of torpor in hopes of emerging in more interesting eras, or perhaps to find the key to their survival in human innovation.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood and Stone and Flesh</b><br /> <br /> Each Colossus can reshape her body at will, similar to the Savages but with far more versatility. Unfortunately, this does not include creating more of their kind. To the Colossi, the Kindred are an inferior strain of vampirism, but not in how they reproduce. For all their power and functional immortality, the Narya breed as humans do, but none have successfully mated since their golden age. Some have tried to conceive with ghouls, dhampir, or even Kindred, but the results are always the same: failure.<br /> <br /> Maybe that\u2019s for the best. While the Colossi can savor food and drink, they cannot survive without the blood, and they often have a thirst that can match any methuselah\u2019s. However, even that would be more manageable than the sudden and capricious moods that possess them. These emotional jags come on like hurricanes, driving the Narya to acts of selfishness that would make a draugr raise an eyebrow. While in these states, a Colossus might consume an entire city in one night, slaughter his own armies, or uncontrollably weep until the sun rises and seals his fate.<br /> <br /> No known mortal weapon can slay a Colossus, but they do fear two things. The first is the sun their ancestors betrayed to the dark; the second is the loneliness of eternity. With no prospect of a future for their dying race, many have lost themselves to despair and embraced the daystar\u2019s judgment.<br /> <br /> Now that only a handful remain, this loneliness has consumed them. The Colossi long for the companionship of their own kind, whether as friends, lovers, or rivals, and they scour the world in search of one another, especially on the off-chance that a coupling might produce heirs. When these efforts fail, many take their frustrations out on the ever-changing world and its inhabitants. Some orchestrate power fantasies and mystery plays, drawing unwitting actors into their webs to play heroes and villains, often with themselves at the center of the narrative. And when this too grows wearisome, the Narya returns to torpor. Within a tomb of living stone, the vampire sleeps away the centuries and dreams of nights past until she wakes to repeat the blood-drenched cycle all over again.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar: Lies, Damned Lies, and History</b><br /> <br /> Kindred who\u2019ve heard of the Narya and their empire wonder at the latter\u2019s veracity, which isn\u2019t to say the Colossi are lying, but also they\u2019re predisposed to self-aggrandizement, and, if nothing else, vampires know having a long memory doesn\u2019t mean you have an accurate one. Some Kindred have heard stories of this fallen kingdom and sought its remains, though if any Narya still recall its location, they\u2019re keeping mum, at\u2026 least until they get a good offer.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems</b><br /> <br /> The Narya function like Kindred except as follows:<br /> <br /> Anchors: Colossi see no need to hide their natures, and they have even less use for the All Night Society. As such, Narya have Virtues and Vices rather than Masks and Dirges.<br /> Banes: Narya are no more vulnerable to fire than humans, but even minor exposure to sunlight turns their bodies to stone. Once petrified, they can never be restored, but they remain mentally aware until something or someone destroys their remains.<br /> <br /> <b>The Beast: </b>Narya lack Beasts. Instead of frenzy, they suffer Hamartia (below). Furthermore, a Colossus who loses her last Humanity dot does not become a draugr. Instead, she gains a persistent form of the Cathectic Condition (p. 165).<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Sympathy: </b>Narya are considered once-removed from their parents and children and twice-removed from all other Colossi. They treat Kindred who know Protean as thrice-removed, though this relation only goes one way.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>While they can learn blood sorcery, Narya have no Disciplines of their own (with the exception of Protean; see below). Instead, they can manifest Discipline powers by spending Vitae equal to the total dots they wish to access. This lasts a scene and is limited to the ten powers common to most Kindred. Narya cannot improvise Devotions or Merits that tie into Disciplines, but they can learn them, ignoring prerequisites. They must manifest these prerequisites to use these powers, however.<br /> <br /> <b>The Embrace: </b>Narya cannot Embrace and do not spawn revenants through careless feeding. In theory, they can reproduce naturally, but none have been able to do so for eons.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghouls and Blood Bonds: </b>Narya can form Vincula, but they cannot create or foster ghouls. Colossi are immune to Vitae addiction and add their Resolve dots to any rolls to resist blood bonds.<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Intensity: </b>In addition to the usual effects of Physical Intensity, a Narya can spend Vitae to increase a Mental or Physical Attribute by a dot, up to her trait limit. The vampire can do this as many times in a scene as she has Blood Potency dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Physiology:</b> Narya bodies have human autonomic functions, including natural healing. Instead of a blush of life, a Colossus can spend a Vitae to seem corpselike. Furthermore, they sleep like mortals and do not need to spend Vitae to rise for the night, though they also do not experience a Cleansing effect. By spending a Vitae and a Willpower, a Narya can heal all bashing damage in her Health boxes. She also does not need to rest to heal aggravated damage, though she can only mend a point per scene. Furthermore, only full aggravated damage can send her into torpor, at which point she can don her Stone Chrysalis (below).<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts of the Void</b><br /> <br /> The Narya differ from the Kindred in their mutable forms and command over matter. However, the darkness also exacts a heavy price upon their souls, inflating their egos to tumorous proportions as they fall further away from Humanity.<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*I don't get the hype. It had some moments, but it mostly just bored me. &quot;Roundabout&quot; <i>is </i>a banger, though. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T15:39:51-07:00","id":1481871,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile I do get the hype and have no idea where it\u2019d be boring \u2014 though the Narya do seem enough removed from it to be independently valuable. In fact, with the Antediluvian nickname, they look more Masquerade/KotE-ish. Which is a good thing for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T17:40:49-07:00","id":1481881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481871#post1481871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile I do get the hype and have no idea where it\u2019d be boring \u2014 though the Narya do seem enough removed from it to be independently valuable. In fact, with the Antediluvian nickname, they look more Masquerade/KotE-ish. Which is a good thing for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>do </i>have a bit of KOTE-body horror going on, don't they? I didn't even think of that. Like I said, the &quot;main&quot; reference is fairly obvious, but you don't need to know it to use them, and these things share DNA with a lot of White Wolf content of yore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T19:24:42-07:00","id":1481890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481881#post1481881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026\u2026 Like I said, the &amp;quot;main&amp;quot; reference is fairly obvious, but you don't need to know it to use them, and these things share DNA with a lot of White Wolf content of yore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best way to make references and share dna, IMO <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T19:40:58-07:00","id":1481893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481868#post1481868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, they're something of an homage to another vampire-adjacent property, which shall remain nameless. Ironically, the thing they're a reference to is like the one thing I know about that property; I was once forced to watch half a season of it for reasons that are too arcane to go into here.*</div> </div> </div> </div>For a second, my brain had mis-processed the information about the Narya in this context to a point where I briefly went &quot;No-he <i>can't</i> be talking about Trinity Blood, no one has cared about Trinity Blood since it's second episode*&quot; before realizing which franchise you were talking about and going &quot;Oh, okay. That makes sense.&quot;<br /> <br /> *This is not me saying you should care about Trinity Blood. Check out the other thing instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T19:58:40-07:00","id":1481894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1479721-wild-hunt-gangrel-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1481893#post1481893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a second, my brain had mis-processed the information about the Narya in this context to a point where I briefly went &quot;No-he <i>can't</i> be talking about Trinity Blood, no one has cared about Trinity Blood since it's second episode*&quot; before realizing which franchise you were talking about and going &quot;Oh, okay. That makes sense.&quot;<br /> <br /> *This is not me saying you should care about Trinity Blood. Check out the other thing instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's one or two episodes more than i ever cared, to be honest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T17:28:57-07:00","id":1482038,"title":"","content":"Hello! Let's look at the clan bane essay! I said I'd do this yesterday, but then I had a whole mess of work to do for my dayjob, and I just wasn't feeling it. But, here we are now!<br /> <br /> So, in the last three books, we've made a point to include sections on the clan banes as sorta player/ST guides, though this evolved over time. We did have material about the Nosferatu bane, though more in updating their &quot;Deviations of Flesh and Feel&quot; system from <b>BTHTB</b>, and we didn't really go into the Mekhet curse apart from offering some new personal banes and an optional shorthand system for the Hollow curse. This section as a kind of essay started with the Ventrue book; the Lords' bane is really interesting thematically and mechanically, but I think a lot of readers don't grok it upon first viewing, and I wanted to go into why it's such a fun, creepy curse. Subsequently, we did the Daeva bane, which is a lot more self-explanatory compared to the Ventrue's, but it's also one that requires a bit of player buy-in.<br /> <br /> This brings us to the Gangrel, who probably have the most straightforward bane of the bunch. Now, I quite like the simple brutality of the Feral Curse; it's much more thematic and fun than their original mental fuzziness (a clan weakness I don't think I ever heard a positive opinion about in all my years playing 1E). But, I think that simplicity hides some of its depth. Here's how I put it in my outline:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019d like a brief section on how to work with the Gangrel clan bane: An ST/player\u2019s guide to the Feral Curse. The Gangrel probably have the easiest bane to understand out of the five clans[...]they frenzy more easily. Bam. Done. But what does it <i>mean</i>?<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve got a limited word count here, but I think you can pack in a lot, especially if you give us some in-character testimonials and scenarios. Like, how does it feel to have that constant rage in the back of your head? What\u2019s it like being the Kindred with the Beast closest to the surface? I want to go a little into the psychology of this bane. In some ways, it\u2019s the most obviously destructive, but I\u2019d like to hear about the more subtle downsides too. All good banes affect playstyle and character behavior, so in what ways does the Feral curse influence a Gangrel? </div> </div> </div>This essay did end up a bit shorter than the ones in the book's sister volumes, partially because we felt we needed a bit more space to talk about Protean, but I'm really happy with the direction the author took it.<br /> <br /> So, here's our take on the Feral Curse, and with that, I've officially run out of things to excerpt! Like I said before, I'll see if I can dig up any cut content, and maybe I'll talk about some development aspects of the cutting process.<br /> <br /> <b>Wild at Heart: The Feral Curse</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;But one mustn\u2019t underestimate the primal appeal \u2014 to lose one\u2019s self, lose it utterly. And in losing it be born to the principle of continuous life, outside the prison of mortality and time.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> \u2014 Donna Tartt, The Secret History<br /> <br /> Cowards call it a bane. Savages call it a birthright.<br /> <br /> Rage, hunger, instinct \u2014 Gangrel don\u2019t view their curse in clinical terms. Nor, really, do they view it as a \u201ccurse\u201d at all. This primal force is just the nature of being Savage. Every clan knows what it feels like when the Beast takes the reins, so if the Gangrel know it more intimately than other Kindred, that\u2019s to their benefit\u2026 isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> This section discusses the Feral Curse, the bestial urge that burns a hole through Savage souls until only an animal remains.<br /> <br /> <b>Just Below the Surface</b><br /> <br /> <i>Some nights, my mind feels like a thin crust of ice. The Beast is just below the surface, pushing and pushing, shattering everything I am. There\u2019ll be no more sure footing after I break. Even if I claw my way back \u2014 fight against that tireless fury \u2014 I\u2019ll have destroyed all I love, ruined my last chance, burned every last bridge.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut,\u201d the Beast whispers, \u201cwon\u2019t that feel good?\u201d<br /> <br /> And it does. God help me, it does. It\u2019s more than an addiction: It\u2019s life.</i><br /> <br /> Every vampire knows the Beast. Some deny it, others muzzle it. But for the Gangrel, the Beast is riding shotgun, reading the map, and \u2014 when you least expect it \u2014 taking the wheel. The Beast enables Savages to bring what they do best to new extremes, to be stronger, tougher, and deadlier than all the other Licks. Yet, while that pounding force coursing through every limb can make a vampire into a potent monster, it erodes a little more of the Man each time the tide comes in. One flash flood, and that sense of self might be swept away entirely.<br /> <br /> Even the youngest Savages don\u2019t need to dig deep to access the Beast. It\u2019s always lurking just behind their eyes, and it doesn\u2019t need an invitation to burst forth. It\u2019s instinctual violence, insatiable hunger, and a defiant sense of survival. It will only ever go down fighting \u2014 even if it started the fight in the first place. There\u2019s no logic, or at least there\u2019s nothing more complex than the most primal urges. It cannot be bargained or reasoned with. It cannot be assuaged.<br /> <br /> After all, it\u2019s inherent to the Blood, and if a vampire doesn\u2019t fight it, she suffers less struggle and strain. Why run from the Beast when you could ride it into battle? This force is an integral part of the Requiem, always present and eager to rise, so the Savages rise with it, borne aloft on a sea of blood. That primal euphoria cuts everything into clear categories: black\u2013white, live\u2013kill, eat-or-be-eaten. Gangrel like clear-cut lines. To be straightforward. Simple. The ever-present rage keeps things very simple indeed, but whether that predilection flows from their slipping Humanity or their swelling Beast is anyone\u2019s guess.<br /> <br /> <b>Intrusive Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> <i>Survival of the fittest, my sire said. I\u2019m young. I need to compete for food and territory or I\u2019m not going to last long in this world. I need to stay sharp. But the Beast snarls at every threat, rages out whenever I\u2019m challenged. It\u2019s off the leash before I can even scramble for the harness.<br /> <br /> The blood dries. I come back to myself. Or as much as ever comes back these days.<br /> <br /> The enemy didn\u2019t know a fledgling like me had that much fight inside. I didn\u2019t know either, honestly.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut do they think I\u2019m a threat?\u201d<br /> <br /> I try to shut out that thought, but I can\u2019t. The predator in me is always loudest at times like this. Always looking for bloody angles.<br /> <br /> They\u2019ll be back. I know they\u2019ll be back, and if I let them get away, they\u2019ll keep pushing. \u201cDon\u2019t give them that chance,\u201d the voice in my head growls.<br /> <br /> Just kill them. Kill them all.</i><br /> <br /> The Beast slathers like a devil on each Savage\u2019s shoulder, a wicked conscience and an endless font of intrusive urges. <i>Bite him. Take her. Jump! </i>It\u2019s not just a matter of impulse control; it\u2019s a matter of salvation. As reckless as the Beast is \u2014 and as sloppy as it makes its vampire \u2014 it fights to win. Other clans may see the Savages as quick to anger, but it\u2019s easy to fear what\u2019s not well understood. Gangrel understand intimately.<br /> <br /> Among packmates, a bit of a tussle, some spilled blood, a little in-fighting? That\u2019s nothing to sweat over. They all feel their tempers flaring. There\u2019s no high ground to stand on when everyone gets the urge to react with abandon. So, while their mistakes and offenses might get them into hot water with the other clans, among their own, a brawl is over when the dust settles. No point hashing it out, trying to dig into the why of it. No point trying to soothe bruised egos when the Beast is all id.<br /> <br /> Yet, understanding these truths doesn\u2019t negate the danger. The Beast knows no social niceties. It cares nothing for bad timing, and it\u2019s a stranger to restraint. That can get a vampire into trouble he might not survive. Shooting his mouth off at the wrong time. Eviscerating the wrong retainer. Diablerizing the wrong Lick. The Beast can be a damn liability, and while the Gangrel know it, they\u2019re still going to let it loose. They can\u2019t help it! It\u2019s in their nature.<br /> <br /> <b>Weapon of Last Resort: Playing the Bane</b><br /> <br /> <i>This old Savage has weathered wars and feuds and regicides. I\u2019ve been through it all thanks to my Beast. It always gave me warning before things turned bad. It lets me fight back, strike first, get out of Dodge while the getting\u2019s good.<br /> <br /> But I couldn\u2019t always take others with me. Kin who didn\u2019t have a Beast quite so loud, quite so sharp.<br /> <br /> I ran, fought, and survived while they were torn to shreds behind me. Lost one after another \u2014 but I kept on keeping on.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m old and lonely. But I\u2019m never alone.</i><br /> <br /> At the end of the night, the Beast is a Savage\u2019s nuclear option. It\u2019s a weapon they can always use when all else is lost. It might eat through one\u2019s Humanity. It might destroy one\u2019s Kindred. It might even slaughter one\u2019s Touchstones, but the Gangrel will crawl out, still kicking. As the tethers that keep a vampire anchored fray and fall away, the Savage becomes ever wilder. The memories of whatever life looked like before \u2014 a life without that incessant pull \u2014 become hazy. They cease to hold the Gangrel\u2019s focus. Then, they cease to be important motivators. Then, they simply cease to be.<br /> <br /> As your character\u2019s clan bane intensifies, think about how this affects her persona. Does she become skittish like an animal at loud noises? Does she growl when displeased? Or does she just forget to not stare at her prey? Many Savages take on these ticks and habits without realizing it, though some rare few adopt them to keep other vampires at bay.<br /> <br /> Still, the Beast can only tear through its host for so long before it wears through. At that point, the Savage becomes little more than a gibbering husk that haunts both Kindred and kine. Perhaps this is what the other clans fear: That if the Gangrel are allowed to run amok unchecked, there won\u2019t be any stopping their rampages.<br /> <br /> The secret is, many Savages fear this too. To fully give in to the Beast means that whispering shadow becomes the only one left standing at their side, inseverable as their own Vitae. As such, consider how your own character clings to her human side. All Kindred must attend to this aspect of the Requiem, but Savages are so close to the Beast that ceding ground to it has far more obvious \u2014 and violent \u2014 consequences. Even the Nosferatu evoke fear because they\u2019re not quite human; the Gangrel are animals. Some Savages use meditation techniques or practice martial arts to keep their predatory sides in check, while others put themselves in spaces where the rage has less of a chance to rear its head; more than a few Gangrel have taken grunt work for their domains because it means they don\u2019t have to deal with people. The Savage who cleans up corpses and crime scenes to preserve the Masquerade doesn\u2019t have a lot of time to hunt, but he still eats well.<br /> <br /> Of course, isolation is just another way to feed the Beast. Many Gangrel try to separate themselves from their prey because they think they can do less harm that way, but violence is only one aspect of the Feral Curse. A Lick who spends all her time alone neglects the human niceties that gird the Masquerade. She forgets that humans don\u2019t go around with stale blood on their breath, and that clothes aren\u2019t optional in most places. This is the eternal paradox of Gangrel blood, to keep humans at an arms\u2019 length for their own safety, yet needing them as close as possible to remind the Beast to stay in the shadows.<br /> <br /> Keep this problem in mind as you build your Savage character, and think of ways she might try to deal with it. Even if she\u2019s as humane as a Gangrel gets, this tension should always be at a simmer, threatening to boil over every time she loses control. Some of the best drama comes from embracing contradictions, and the Feral Curse is a great way to make your character\u2019s Requiem thrillingly \u2014 and bloodily \u2014 incongruous.<br /> <br /> <b>Common Banes</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T12:04:15-07:00","id":1482276,"title":"","content":"Hello again! I said I'd be back to post some cut content, and here I am, like some sort of promise-keeping guy.<br /> <br /> The first is Project Shatterglass, the brief plot seed we included with the Mystikoi. This was great, but it made the bloodline seven pages long, and I try to keep them down to six at max. I managed to preserve a chunk of the introductory text, but the bullet points had to go:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Story Seed: Project Shatterglass</b><br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul has taken care to maintain good relations with the Mystikoi, sheltering the bloodline from its Sanctified enemies on many occasions throughout history. However, the Defiant rarely do anything without an angle, and they have plans for the Illuminated. Referred to unofficially as Project Shatterglass, some elders of the covenant have been studying the techniques and adaptations of the Mystikoi for centuries, and they\u2019re close to a breakthrough concerning mass application. What does this mean for the domain where the first tests are about to get underway? Here are a few possibilities:<ul><li>The Mystikoi begin to spread their need for Essence like a disease, but not their adaptations to hunt for it. Soon, the domain is full of addicts desperate for a fix they cannot get on their own. What happens when one of the player characters becomes infected? Or is the coterie a group of Illuminated who\u2019ve unknowingly exacerbated the problem?</li> <li>Something goes catastrophically wrong, and a massive rift is torn between the worlds of flesh and spirit. Now, dangerous ephemeral entities are emerging on the streets of the domain, and the local werewolves are apocalyptically pissed off. Will the player characters try to get to the bottom of this disaster and put it right, or will they take advantage of the chaos to settle old scores?</li> <li>Mystikoi have been arriving in the domain for weeks at the behest of the Ordo Dracul. Now, the climax of Project Shatterglass has seen the entire bloodline transformed into ephemeral hunters that can strike from Twilight without warning. No longer concerned with politics or the Masquerade, the Illuminated are running amok, attacking Kindred and kine alike. The player characters encounter Jeremy Wong, the only Mystikos to apparently escape the transformation, and he claims he can reverse the process \u2014 but he needs their help to do it.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> I also found a Devotion I cut from Chapter Three. It was a cool power, but it was very, very similar to a Yarilo bloodline power, and I felt it fit better as a special function of that group rather than a general power (we also had a fair few &quot;the vampire refuses to die&quot; powers in this one anyway). That said, feel free to use this in your own chronicles if it fits!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Subsume Being</b><br /> <br /> <b>(Dominate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Protean \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> True immortality is beyond the reach of the Kindred, but this Devotion is the next best thing. The rare vampire who possesses this Devotion can outlive her own Final Death, being reborn into the bodies of others.<br /> <br /> Rumor has it that this Devotion is based on one stolen from the Asn\u00e2m bloodline (Bloodlines: The Devoted, p. 11), but if so, the mechanisms are quite different.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 4 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Humanity dot<br /> <br /> <b>Requirement: </b>The mortal victim must have a third-stage Vinculum to the vampire.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>None<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> In a shower of blood and pain, the victim\u2019s mind and body transform into a likeness of the vampire, whose own body crumbles to dust. The victim is Embraced as part of the transformation, and the vampire retains all her Attributes, Skills, and Disciplines, but not her Blood Potency. </div> </div> </div>And with that, I don't think I have anything else to excerpt (I could talk about the fiction? Is anyone interested in that?) That said, feel free to continue asking questions or making comments, as I'm very happy to keep the conversation going, even if it's about one of the other books. I'll keep an eye on the thread (as well as the one on the RPG.net forums).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}